\par }{\fs20\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof {\shp{\*\shpinst\shpleft1440\shptop2070\shpright10800\shpbottom2070\shpfhdr1\shpbxpage\shpbxignore\shpbypage\shpbyignore\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt0\shpz2\shplockanchor\shplid2049{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn shapePath}{\sv 4}}{\sp{\sn fFillOK}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFilled}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fArrowheadsOK}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelh}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelv}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}{\shprslt{\*\do\dobxpage\dobypage\dodhgt8194\dpline\dpptx0\dppty0\dpptx9920\dppty0\dpx1190\dpy2070\dpxsize9920\dpysize0\dplinew15\dplinecor0\dplinecog0\dplinecob0}}}}{\f0\fs16  \par }}{\footerf \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }{\footer \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}} of {\field{\*\fldinst NUMPAGES}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 {\par\fs20\b \uc2 STOCKS PLUNGE AS UNEMPLOYMENT RISES DOW DROPS + POINTS ON WEAK JOBS REPORT\b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 August 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, NOMINEE, DELEGATES, BIDEN, 538, RUNNING, MATE, KELLY, WALZ, SHAPIRO\par \par \uc2 FUTURECAST, TRACKING, TROPICAL, STORMS, HEAT, RAINFALL\par \par \uc2 FREED, RUSSIA, PRISON, BIDEN, WHELAN, GERSHKOVICH, FOGEL, KURMASHEVA, KARA-MURZA\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY, STOCK, MARKET, DOW, JOBS, REPORT, FED, RECESSION, INTEREST, RATES\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) An emotional 24 hours for those families. Mireya, thank you. News tonight about the US economy and a sharp drop in the stock market, fueled by lower-than-expected jobs numbers. And now growing concerns the Fed may have waited too long to lower interest rates. The Dow plunging 610 points today. At one point, it was down more than 900. Let's get right to ABC's chief business correspondent Rebecca Jarvis. Rebecca, walk us through what happened today.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STOCKS PLUNGE AS UNEMPLOYMENT RISES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOW DROPS 600+ POINTS ON WEAK JOBS REPORT\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whit, that disappointing jobs report put talk of recession back on the table on Wall Street. Employers added just 114,000 jobs in July, well below the 185,000 forecast. The unemployment rate increased to four point three percent, which is still low, but it shows joblessness has jumped more than half a percent since January, something that just doesn't happen in a healthy economy, and historically a sign a recession is imminent. On Wall Street, the selling was broad-based but the tech names, some of those high-flyers earlier this year were some of the hardest-hit today. And you put it all together, and it is a signal the Fed is likely to cut, perhaps even aggressively, come September. Whit?\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240807ek8200005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ALL EYES ON CRITICAL JOBS REPORT EXPECTED TO SHOW JOB GROWTH COOLING BUT STILL STRONG\b0\par\par\uc2 339 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 July 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HURRICANE BERYL ROARS ASHORE\par \par \uc2 BERYL, LANDFALL, DAMAGE, MEXICO, GULF COAST\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, DEBATE, PRESSURE, DEMS, NEWSOM\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, DEMOCRATS, CANDIDACY, CONCERNS, DONORS\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, STARMER, BRITAIN, LABOUR PARTY, HISTORIC\par \par \uc2 TRUNK, DRUNK, DEAD, CROWD, INJURED, ARREST\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY, JOBS REPORT, UNEMPLOYMENT, FEDERAL RESERVE\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Just too tragic, and thinking about all of those families. All right, Aaron, thank you. We turn now to the economy. All eyes are on the latest jobs report out this morning. And Elizabeth Schulze joins us with the breakdown on all of it. Good morning, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON CRITICAL JOBS REPORT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPECTED TO SHOW JOB GROWTH COOLING BUT STILL STRONG\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, Rebecca. And this jobs report will reveal if employers are shifting into a lower gear, slowing down their brisk pace of hiring. Analysts expect that 200,000 jobs were added to the workforce in June. That would be fewer than the 272,000 new jobs in May. Not it's really important to watch the unemployment rate, which is now at a two-year high of 4%. Still an historically strong number, but it has been ticking up.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And last month the unemployment rate for younger Americans between the ages of 20-24, spiked to 7.9%. That was its highest level in nearly three years. So this is a sign that employers are getting more cautious and selective. We are seeing companies prioritize prior work experience when they're looking at resumes, which is a challenge for new applicants in the workforce.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) If this jobs report shows the market is cooling, that could encourage the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  to finally cut interest rates this fall. That would be a long-awaited relief for borrowers who are trying to pay off their credit card debt or take out a new car or home loan. Whit.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240718ek750002z\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 UNEMPLOYMENT RATE JUMPS FOR NEW GRADS WHAT'S BEHIND THE TREND & WHERE TO FIND WORK\b0\par\par\uc2 1,071 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 June 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTREME HEAT SURGING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TROPICAL THREAT BEARS DOWN\par \par \uc2 HEATWAVE, ALERTS, TEMPS, WILDFIRES, ADVISORIES\par \par \uc2 BOEING, CONGRESS, HAWLEY, CALHOUN, SAFETY\par \par \uc2 PUTIN, JONG \uc2 UN\uc2 , FESTIVITIES, WEAPONS, UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 NETANYAHU, ACCUSATIONS, WEAPONS, GAZA, HEZBOLLAH\par \par \uc2 GAETZ, INVESTIGATION, HOUSE, ETHICS, VENMO\par \par \uc2 EXPLOSION, COLLAPSE, HOUSE, HOSPITALIZED, MONDS, WALSH\par \par \uc2 MAYS, MLB, NEGRO LEAGUES, LEGACY, CAREER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TROPICAL DEVELOPMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TIMBERLAKE, DWI, ARRESTED, POLICE, COURT, ASWAD\par \par \uc2 MURDAUGH, LAWSUIT, MURDER, MEDIA, DOCUMENTARIES, SMITH\par \par \uc2 APPLE, PAY LATER, CANCELED, AFFIRM, INTEREST RATES\par \par \uc2 MONEY, UNCLAIMED, WAGNER, OHIO, AMUSEMENT PARK\par \par \uc2 HISLOP, GRADUATE, STANFORD, 105-YEAR-OLD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARMER SUMMER NIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, HEAT WAVE, WILDFIRES, HEAT DOME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD HEAT TAKES HOLD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: L.A. SCHOOLS BAN CELL PHONES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STANLEY CUP FINAL\par \par \uc2 CELL PHONES, LAUSD, BAN, DISTRACTION, SOCIAL MEDIA\par \par \uc2 STANLEY CUP, FINALS, OILERS, PANTHERS, GAME 6\par \par \uc2 COLLEGE, GRADUATES, JOBS, UNEMPLOYMENT, TIPS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we're back now with our "GMA" Cover Story and the latest on the job market.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNEMPLOYMENT RATE: AGES 20-24\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAY 2023 6.3% TO MAY 2024 7.9%\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LARGEST ANNUAL INCREASE IN 14 YEARS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The unemployment rate for 20 to 24-year-olds in May jumped by its biggest annual increase in 14 years despite a strong overall job market.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Elizabeth Schulze is back to help us break it all down and Elizabeth, what is this data telling us?\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you know, Michael, this is frustrating for a generation of graduates. They started college in the middle of the pandemic and now they are facing a more challenging jobs market.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNEMPLOYMENT RATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 4.7% RECENT COLLEGE GRADS AGES 22-27\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 3.7% ALL U.S. WORKERS\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, if you look at data from the \uc2 New York Fed\uc2 , what it's gonna tell you is that the unemployment rate for recent college grads, 4.7%. That is about a percentage point higher than for all workers right now. So, part of what's going on here is that we're just seeing the overall pace of hiring slowdown in the economy. These are still low rates, but employers are pulling back.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW JOB PITFALLS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EMPLOYERS SLOWING DOWN HIRING PACE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JOB OPENINGS DOWN IN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TECH, CONSULTING, FINANCE, MEDIA\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And this is especially the case when you think about industries in professional services. So, think of jobs in tech, finance, media. Those companies, they hired super-fast during the pandemic and now they've been pulling back.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, but say you need a job now.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What fields are hiring?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW JOB OPPORTUNITIES: SERVICES SECTOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEALTH CARE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LEISURE & HOSPITALITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EMPLOYERS PRIORITIZING CANDIDATES WITH WORK EXPERIENCE\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, so, there's, there is a lot of good news here. There are a couple sectors that have been adding tens of thousands of jobs every single month, especially in the services sector. So, look, think about healthcare. Nursing facilities, hospitals, a lot of open positions right now, and their wages are going up in those sectors. Leisure and hospitality also big. Hotels, restaurants, gyms, seeing a lot of hiring in those industries. And then, one thing we're seeing right now is that employers are really prioritizing hiring workers who have previous experience. So, one thing you want to think about, if you're trying to get a job, or switch to another one, is how you can play up the skills that you've gotten in an old job and how they will translate to a new one.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, the, so I am applying for a job. How do I make myself stand out, though?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO MARKET YOURSELF FOR NEW JOBS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REACH OUT TO ESTABLISHED NETWORK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BE OPEN TO NEW INDUSTRIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RESEARCH COMPANY AND JOB POSTING BEFORE INTERVIEW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEND THANK YOU EMAIL AFTER INTERVIEW\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right. So, one of the things you always want to do is 101, cast a wide net in your network. If you're a college grad, you might think, "Well, I don't have a network yet." But that can include professors.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STRUGGLING TO FIND WORK: TIPS TO NAVIGATE THE JOB MARKET\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That can include professors, it can include friends, anyone you know from school. Just don't hesitate to use those connections. Be open-minded about industries that you could work in. So, one thing that we see right now in the economy is jobs in healthcare might actually look a little bit more like tech jobs. So, think about if you could look into an industry that might not be the first thought. Always want to research the company and the job posting. If you are doing an interview, if you're writing a cover letter, you need to tell them exactly why you want that specific posting. Know the details and know that before you go in ahead of time. Finally, and this one is pretty easy, do not forget to send a thank you email after you do an interview.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Be courteous.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Just, 101, being nice, it goes a long way.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It does go a long way. Elizabeth, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thanks, Michael.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I think you helped somebody get a job today.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I hope so, That's the goal here.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Alright. Gonna go to you, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And be careful about using Chat GPT for that thank you email.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Just in case. Okay, guys, thank you. We turn now to our series "GMA" Out Loud, highlighting inspiring people in the community driving change.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Gio spoke to one couple about their fight for equality in healthcare and their dream of growing their family. Hi, Gio. What a great story.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240710ek6j0000l\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 RISE OF "QUIET VACATIONING" THE NEW TREND AS SOME REMOTE WORKERS ARE CLOCKING IN FROM PICTURESQUE DESTINATIONS\b0\par\par\uc2 805 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 June 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASS SHOOTINGS\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, SPLASH PAD, JAMES, BOUCHARD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MULTIPLE PEOPLE SHOT AT MICHIGAN SPLASH PAD PARK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST NINE PEOPLE INJURED INCLUDING CHILDREN, SUSPECT LATER FOUND DEAD\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, JUNETEENTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY SHOOTING AT TEXAS JUNETEENTH EVENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST TWO KILLED, MULTIPLE OTHERS INJURED FOLLOWING ALTERCATION\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRES, WINDS, EVACUATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILDFIRES PROMPTS EVACUATIONS IN CALIFORNIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FUELED BY WIND GUSTS OVER 50 MPH, AT LEAST 10,500 ACRES SCORCHED\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, HEAT, TRACK, FORECAST\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, TRUMP, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIVALS ON THE ROAD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN ATTENDS STAR-STUDDED FUNDRAISER IN CALIFORNIA\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, TRUMP, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, AID, SKAU, SIEGEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IDF ANNOUNCES "TACTICAL PAUSE" IN GROUND OFFENSIVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TO ALLOW FOR MORE HUMANITARIAN AID TO ENTER THE STRIP\par \par \uc2 SOMALIA, \uc2 ISIS\uc2 , AIRSTRIKE, MUMIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. OFFICIALS: TOP ISIS LEADER WAS TARGET OF SOMALIA AIRSTRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NOT YET KNOWN WHETHER U.S. ATTACK SUCCEEDED\par \par \uc2 NHL, STANLEY CUP FINALS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STANLEY CUP FINAL: OILERS TAKE GAME FOUR FROM PANTHERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EDMONTON NOW TRAILS FLORIDA THREE GAMES TO ONE\par \par \uc2 PICKLE, RESCUE, CPR\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "INSIDE OUT 2"\par \par \uc2 HOBERG, GAMBLING, PASSAN, MARCANO\par \par \uc2 QUIET VACATIONING, FISH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RISE OF "QUIET VACATIONING"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE NEW TREND AS SOME REMOTE WORKERS ARE CLOCKING IN FROM PICTURESQUE DESTINATIONS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the trend being called quiet vacationing. If you think that a co-worker is just working from home, they might be a lot farther away than you imagine. ABC's Will Ganss, he is not quiet vacationing. He joins us now. You've been looking into this, Will? Good morning.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Gio, it's fair to say I'm not quiet, period. I think it's interesting that I was assigned this story, but let's move on anyway. A recent study found that about half of American workers are not using all of their vacation days possibly because they're afraid of being perceived as lazy or unproductive. But now, there's a workaround that has people working from the beach.\par \par \uc2 TIKTOK USER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Is this your current work location, but your company doesn't know about it?\par \par \uc2 VOICEOVER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Shh, we're quiet vacationing.\par \par \uc2 TIKTOK USER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 You just got to keep living, man. L-I-V-I-N.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's the trend that has remote employees working not from home, but from the beach, the pool, the ski chalet, or wherever their hush-hush holiday takes them.\par \par \uc2 MELANIE FISH (TRAVEL EXPERT EXPEDIA GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Americans say they feel they're vacation-deprived. So, people may be trying to fight that vacation deprivation by sneaking in more trips away.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Instead of taking paid time off, quiet vacationers are keeping their employers in the dark about their work from home plans and clocking in poolside.\par \par \uc2 VOICEOVER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 It's absolutely no one's business. If you see a virtual background, it's no one's business what room of your house you're in, what state you're in.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's the latest in a shift away from hustle culture, following quiet quitting, which has workers doing the bare minimum at work and nothing more. But experts warn that your quiet vacation might be louder than you think.\par \par \uc2 MELANIE FISH (TRAVEL EXPERT EXPEDIA GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Your manager and your coworkers are noticing that conference call camera off and other clues, so you really need to consider the risks, the rewards, and the ethics of taking downtime on the downlow.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) While working from the beach may sound like the best of both worlds, experts say, a loud vacation is better for your mental well-being. They say you're better off being fully present when you're on the clock and fully absent when you're on vacation. Which is why I would like to say right here, right now that I will not be on any Zoom calls for the rest of the day. So, don't even try, Gio.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're zooming out. This is why.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, hello.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, knees. Hey, knees.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Leg-zilla.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, boy. But I feel like Will has filed a report from a Mexican hotel.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He has. He has.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That was the quiet part of my vacation, this is the loud part.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Loud part. Okay. Perfect. Right on the mark.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, Will, as always. So much fun.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240709ek6g0000f\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WHERE ARE THE JOBS? BREAKING DOWN THE LATEST ENCOURAGING EMPLOYMENT NUMBERS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,037 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 June 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BACK HOME\par \par \uc2 HOSTAGES, ISRAEL, RAID, GAZA, CIVILIANS, DEAD, INJURED\par \par \uc2 CEASEFIRE, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , RAID, DEATH TOLL, HOSTAGE\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , CONVICTION, RALLY, PROBATION, BIDEN, WORLD WAR I\par \par \uc2 HEAT DOME, TEMPERATURES, RECORD, RIDGE\par \par \uc2 THUNDERSTORM CELL, AIRPLANE, DAMAGE, PASSENGERS\par \par \uc2 LANDSLIDE, WYOMING, HIGHWAY, TETON PASS, CLOSURE\par \par \uc2 EU ELECTIONS, FAR RIGHT, MACRON, CENTRISTS, ALLIES\par \par \uc2 NBA FINALS, CELTICS, MAVERICKS, MAZZULLA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "ST. ELMO'S FIRE"\par \par \uc2 CLARK, OLYMPICS, TEAM USA, \uc2 WNBA\uc2 , BRENNAN, SIDES\par \par \uc2 SHARK, ATTACKS, BEACH, CRAWFORD, CLOSURES\par \par \uc2 BULL, RODEO, ESCAPES, INJURIES, PATTON, CAPTURE\par \par \uc2 RACERS, COMPETITION, CARO, CELEBRATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN POTENTIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, RAID, PESSACH, LERNER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, TRIAL\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY, JOBS, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Going to take a look at today's job market right now. Our expert is right here at the desk, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) As luck would have it.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, the new jobs numbers came out Friday, surprisingly strong but unemployment also ticked up. So, where are the jobs now?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHERE ARE THE JOBS?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING DOWN THE LATEST ENCOURAGING EMPLOYMENT NUMBERS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, overall, if you look at the jobs market, it's mostly strong. There is hiring really across the board. But the strongest areas follow the money, where money is being infused.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Health care jobs, up 68,000. Government jobs, up 43,000. And then jobs in leisure and hospitality, up 42,000. And if you look especially at that leisure and hospitality number, and think about where you, as a consumer, might be spending your money this summer. You're probably traveling. A lot of people are. And that is why those leisure and hospitality jobs are climbing and are expected to climb throughout the summer. And still, even at this point where we've seen additions there, it still is behind where we were pre-pandemic.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Strong jobs, sign of a stronger economy, but also inflation.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right. And that's really what the Fed has been thinking about as they anticipate what's going to happen with prices.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EMPLOYMENT & ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT DOES STRONGER THAN EXPECTED JOB GROWTH MEAN FOR INFLATION?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) While they're not climbing as much as they were previously, they're still higher, so it really impacts Americans' budgets. And even though the jobs market is strong overall and even wages are now increasing faster than inflation, it can feel like you have less money given these increases. Again, that's where the Fed is on this, Michael.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And that's why the Fed is making decisions what about to do with interest rates. That's why interest rates are where they are and it cost 7% to get a fixed mortgage.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And when you're looking for a job, networking is very important. How do you network the right way?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO USE NETWORKING TO LAND A NEW JOB\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, I think what is really, unfortunately, problematic about technology now is people rely too heavily on it.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO FIND A JOB\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) They think, oh, if I do \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2 , if I do maximizing, optimizing my resume, that's going to make everything perfect. In person is still as important as anything. And staying in touch with those contacts, making sure that you make that contact and make the connection is almost more important in standing out nowadays because there just is so much more.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And I don't know if you guys have seen a resume recently or a cover letter. Don't overly rely on AI. I've been reading so many cover letters recently, and it sounds like a machine wrote them. You have to make sure that it's real.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And I like being in person. You see somebody, look them in the face, you get a feel for their personality and see if they really fit with the group.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you can use social media, too. Think about your social media as the face forward to people. Like it's not just the place to be social. You can make a connection there. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Social media, but don't be too social.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, don't overdo that. Bring 90% of yourself to social media.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, Rebecca. Coming up in our "GMA Morning Menu," we've got a big surprise ahead of tonight's Stanley Cup final game 2 between the Oilers and Panthers.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:12, STANLEY CUP FINAL SURPRISE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:21, INSIDE "TIANA'S BAYOU ADVENTURE"\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also ahead, a first look at the new attraction bringing "The Princess and The Frog" to life at Disney World and Disneyland.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:13, MODERN SPIN ON 80S FASHION\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus, we are putting a modern spin on '80s fashion. Lilliana Vasquez is here with Brat Pack-inspired looks and dos and don'ts to make them work. And Lara is with a very special guest. Hey, Lara.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:37, ANDREW MCCARTHY TALKS "BRATS"\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hi. Yeah, we're just taking this '80s thing very seriously.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW MCCARTHY (ACTOR & DIRECTOR "BRATS")\par \par \uc2 Very seriously.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The man, Andrew McCarthy, is with us. We're going to talk all about his new documentary, "Brats." It's all about the iconic group of '80s actors that came to be known as the Brat Pack. We're going to get into it coming up on "Good Morning America" with my friend. So happy you're here.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW MCCARTHY (ACTOR & DIRECTOR "BRATS")\par \par \uc2 Glad to be here.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240627ek6a0000k\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WORKERS VOTE TO STRIKE APPLE EMPLOYEES\b0\par\par\uc2 235 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Sunday\par \uc2 WNSU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OHIO OFFICER AMBUSHED\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, DERBIN, AMBUSH, SUSPECT, MULTI-AGENCY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRE, AIR QUALITY, CANADIAN, SMOKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AIR QUALITY CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRES, SMOKE, RAINFALL, FLOODING, WINDS\par \par \uc2 NORTHERN LIGHTS, SOLAR FLARES, SPECTACLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NORTHERN LIGHTS STILL VISIBLE\par \par \uc2 BRIDGE, DEMOLITION, LIGHTNING, POSTPONED, DALI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMOLITION OF BALTIMORE BRIDGE\par \par \uc2 STRIKES, RUSSIA, UKRAINE, KILLED, INJURED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MISSILE STRIKES RUSSIAN BUILDING\par \par \uc2 IDF, RAFAH, EVACUATION, PALESTINIANS, CEASEFIRE, BLINKEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IDF PUSHES DEEPER INTO RAFAH\par \par \uc2 COHEN, TESTIFY, TRUMP, DANIELS, HUSH MONEY, MENENDEZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MICHAEL COHEN SET TO TESTIFY\par \par \uc2 SCHOOLS, LAYOFFS, TEACHERS, FUNDING, CORNELL, PESKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SCHOOL DISTRICTS BRACING FOR LAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 APPLE, EMPLOYEES, UNION, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORKERS VOTE TO STRIKE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A lot of concern over this. Morgan, thank you. Next tonight, \uc2 Apple\uc2  employees at a retail store in Maryland have voted to authorize a strike, and could be the first walk-out by \uc2 Apple\uc2  employees in the US.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Talks between the union and the tech giant do continue. The union, which represents 100 workers at the store, was also the first to unionize.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There's still much more ahead on "World News Tonight" this Sunday. Tears and disappointment at a major university when not everyone is allowed into the commencement ceremonies. And two days after being hit in the head, one of the greats of tennis suffers another blow.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNSU000020240514ek5c0000b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WALL STREET RALLIES ON HOPES OF A RATE CUT DOW GAINS 450 POINTS FOLLOWING "GOLDILOCKS" JOBS REPORT\b0\par\par\uc2 704 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CATASTROPHIC FLOODING\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, STORMS, RIVER, FLOODING, TORNADOES, HAIL, RESIDENTS, HOMES, LAMBERT\par \par \uc2 CAMPUS, PALESTINE, PROTESTERS, \uc2 NYPD\uc2 , DAUGHTRY, VALDEZ, SHAFIK, COMMENCEMENT\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, HOSTAGE, CEASE-FIRE, DEAL, BURNS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, TESTIMONY, HICKS, DANIELS, COHEN, TAPE, "ACCESS HOLLYWOOD"\par \par \uc2 CONGRESS, CUELLAR, BRIBES, BANK, TEXTS, "EL JEFE"\par \par \uc2 SENTENCING, HAGERICH, TOURIST, AMMUNITION, LUGGAGE, AIRPORT, ISLAND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENTENCING HEARING FOR US TOURIST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LAWYERS ASKING FOR LIGHTER SENTENCE, FACING POSSIBLE 12 YEARS FOR AMMUNITION IN LUGGAGE\par \par \uc2 TEENS, BOAT, VIDEO, TRASH, ATLANTIC, OCEAN, FWC, FELONY\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, WINDS, HAIL, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 ANDREWS, CLARK, WNBA, \uc2 NBA\uc2 , CLIPPERS, MAVERICKS, MAGIC, CAVALIERS, \uc2 NUGGETS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 MOVIE CLIP FROM \uc2 WALT DISNEY\uc2  STUDIES, "UP"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 DISNEY\uc2  IS THE PARENT COMPANY OF ABC NEWS\par \par \uc2 CAMPUS, PROTESTS, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , IPSOS, VOTERS, BIDEN, ABORTION, TRUMP, HARRIS\par \par \uc2 FORECAST, HEAT\par \par \uc2 YOUTHFORIA, "SHARK TANK", CUBAN, MAKEUP, SHADE, BLACK, GEORGE, TIKTOK, FORD\par \par \uc2 "STAR WARS", SUPERFANS, MARATHONS, CHILDS, HAMILL, DEALS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER WREAKS HAVOC\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CATASTROPHIC FLOODING\par \par \uc2 FLOODING, TORNADO, STORM, WHITMORE, MCKINNEY\par \par \uc2 TURKS AND CAICOS, HAGERICH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENTENCING HEARING FOR U.S. TOURIST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LAWYERS ASKING FOR LIGHTER SENTENCE, FACING POSSIBLE 12 YEARS FOR AMMUNITION IN LUGGAGE\par \par \uc2 JOB REPORT, ECONOMY, INTEREST RATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WALL STREET RALLIES ON HOPES OF A RATE CUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOW GAINS 450 POINTS FOLLOWING "GOLDILOCKS" JOBS REPORT\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Turning now to the excitement on Wall Street and the rekindled hopes that an interest rate cut is coming. That is thanks to a lower-than-expected jobs report. ABC's Alexis Christoforous is here to break it all down. Good morning, Alexis.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JOBS REPORT\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hi, good morning, Janai. Wall Street applauded news of slower job growth, sending the Dow Jones industrial average rallying 450 points.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOW JONES CLOSING NUMBERS\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Traders are hopeful it might convince the Fed to cut interest rates sooner rather than later. Some economists are calling it a Goldilocks jobs report, not too hot, not too cold, but striking just the right balance, keeping hope alive that the Fed will cut rates this year which, of course, could lower the cost of mortgages, auto loans and credit cards. Employers added a solid 175,000 jobs in April, less than the 240,000 expected and well below the more than 300,000 jobs added in March.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ECONOMY EXAMINED\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The unemployment rate ticked up to 3.9%, but still remains below 4% for the 27th consecutive month.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNEMPLOYMENT RATE TICKED UP 3.9%, 27TH CONSECUTIVE MONTH BELOW 4%\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Industries that hired the most last month were health care, social assistance, transportation and warehousing. Wages also rose less than expected, up 3.9% from a year ago. That's the smallest gain in nearly three years.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Bad news for workers, but good news for the Fed and its fight against inflation since higher wages can be inflationary. This week, the Fed left interest rates unchanged once again, citing a lack of progress on inflation. Guys?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Alexis, thank you so much. Coming up in our "GMA Morning Menu," a new study on anger and heart health.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 3 MINUTES, GMA HEALTH ALERT\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) How it could increase the risk of heart deed. Dr. Sutton is live to break it all down.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEXT HALF HOUR, GETTING MET GALA GLAM\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Also ahead, celebrity makeup artist Patrick Ta's here. He's going to be getting stars ready for the Met Gala Monday. But this morning, he's giving us tips and tricks to get glammed up at home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 9 MINUTES, MOTHER'S DAY DEALS!\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. And Tory Johnson has special steals for the mom in your life. Whit and Gio, I'm a mom in your life, guys.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Yes, you are.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Start shopping. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Mama Janai.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240528ek540000j\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CALIFORNIA'S FAST FOOD STICKER SHOCK RESTAURANTS RAISING PRICES IN RESPONSE TO MINIMUM WAGE HIKE\b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY TORNADO OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 TORNADOES, DESTRUCTION, RESIDENTS, DEAD, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , GAZA, BLINKEN, CEASE FIRE, SIEGEL\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, COLLEGES, NATIONWIDE, WEHLE, ARRESTS, PRO-PALESTINIAN, ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, JURY, TESTIMONY, CONTEMPT\par \par \uc2 NOEM, DOG, SHOOTING, BOOK, BACKLASH\par \par \uc2 MINIMUM WAGE, CALIFORNIA, FAST FOOD, PRICES\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Jon an interesting one there. Thank you. We turn now to the fast food sticker shock in California after the minimum wage for workers out west was raised. Our chief business correspondent Rebecca Jarvis is here with the details. Good morning, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CALIFORNIA'S FAST FOOD STICKER SHOCK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RESTAURANTS RAISING PRICES IN RESPONSE TO MINIMUM WAGE HIKE\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Linsey. Yeah, I am hearing from customers every day who say they are already feeling that sticker shock. Restaurants have been warning about this since September when California voted to increase large fast food chains minimum wage by 25% from $16 to $20 an hour. In that time restaurants in the state have increased prices by 10% faster than all other states according to data essential.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The wage increase is meant to give more financial security to the more than 500,000 people who work in fast food restaurants in California and are not teenagers, but adults working to support their families. The \uc2 California Restaurant Association\uc2  says the price hikes were entirely predictable, results of the minimum wage increase.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Since it took effect, job losses reduced working hours, restaurant closures, and higher prices for California's inflation weary customers have been on going, the group said. And, guys, this is something all the consumers who are facing it now are now facing a choice of whether or not to trade down. Many of them I hear are doing just that. Spending less because they have to spend more. Gio.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240521ek4t00030\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TENNESSEE VOLKSWAGEN WORKERS VOTE TO JOIN UNION MARKING THE FIRST NON-UNION FACTORY IN THE SOUTH TO ORGANIZE\b0\par\par\uc2 567 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OPENING STATEMENTS SET TO BEGIN: TRUMP ON TRIAL\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, CRIMINAL, COURTHOUSE, FIRE\par \par \uc2 TIKTOK, ISRAEL, UKRAINE, TAIWAN, FOREIGN, BILL, AID\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN, DE-ESCALATION\par \par \uc2 STUDENT, SHOOTING, MANIFESTO, ATTACK, SCHOOL\par \par \uc2 ATTACK, CAMPUS, ROBBERY\par \par \uc2 VOLKSWAGEN\uc2 , TENNESSEE, UNION\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the groundbreaking vote overnight, workers at \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  in Tennessee giving a thumb's up to join the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2 , a first for the union outside of Detroit. ABC's Morgan Norwood has the details. Morgan, this is a big deal.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, that's right. Good morning to you, Janai. It's a seismic victory for the \uc2 United Auto Workers Union\uc2  in the south and for \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  workers, this could mean better pay and benefits down the line, right, but for now, this win is a part of a larger push to organize 13 automakers across the country.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Overnight, employees at \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2 's factory in Tennessee overwhelmingly voting to join the \uc2 United Auto Workers Union\uc2 , marking the first non-union factory in the south to organize.\par \par \uc2 SHAWN FAIN (PRESIDENT UNITED AUTO WORKERS)\par \par \uc2 The people have spoken.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Nearly three-quarters of workers voting to join.\par \par \uc2 VICKY HOLLOWAY (EMPLOYEE VOLKSWAGEN IN CHATTANOOGA)\par \par \uc2 It's the greatest feeling that I've felt, like, in 13 years.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The victory coming after two failed attempts; one in 2019, the other in 2014.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL REAM (EMPLOYEE VOLKSWAGEN)\par \par \uc2 Workers, the people that do the job, build the cars, you know, our voices need to be heard and we need to be treated fairly.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The vote a successful test of the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2 ' new push to organize non-union factories.\par \par \uc2 WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 To the other elected officials who are afraid of unions, I just want to say don't be afraid of people power, don't be afraid of people coming together to say that we should be treated as human beings. That's what a union ensures.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 UAW\uc2 's President, Shawn Fain celebrating the win, but warning the battle is far from over.\par \par \uc2 SHAWN FAIN (PRESIDENT UNITED AUTO WORKERS)\par \par \uc2 The real fight begins now. The real fight is getting your fair share. The real fight is the fight for our union contracts.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Last fall, uaw workers in Detroit launched a series of strikes against the big three automakers. President Biden even showing support at the picket line. The strikes ending with generous new contracts for union workers, increasing wages by a third.\par \par \uc2 SHAWN FAIN (PRESIDENT UNITED AUTO WORKERS)\par \par \uc2 Workers are fed up in this country. They're fed up with being left behind, and, obviously, you know, with our win in big three bargaining, I think that motivated a lot of workers to realize there's better for them.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, in a statement, \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  thanking its Chattanooga workers for voting, saying they're awaiting certification of those results. Workers at Mercedes factories in Alabama, well, they're up next and will vote on uaw representation in May. Guys.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, it could really make such a difference. All right, thank you so much, Morgan.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240515ek4k0002z\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ADMIRAL JOHN KIRBY SEVEN WORLD CENTRAL KITCHEN WORKERS KILLED BY ISRAELI STRIKE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,975 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2024 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 ANDR\u201\'00\'C9S, \uc2 WCK\uc2 , WORKERS, \uc2 IDF\uc2 , DRONES, GAZA, BIDEN, NETANYAHU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD CENTRAL KITCHEN AID WORKERS KILLED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JACOB FLICKINGER, 33 - JOHN CHAPMAN, 57 - JAMES (JIM) HENDERSON, 33 - JAMES KIRBY, 47\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DAMIAN SOB\u211\'00\'D3L, 35 - LALZAWMI (ZOMI) FRANKCOM, 43 - SAIFEDDIN ISSAM AYAD ABUTAHA, 25\par \par \uc2 KIRBY, ANDR\u201\'00\'C9S, \uc2 WCK\uc2 , BIDEN, DRONES, WEAPONS, GAZA, WAR, TIMELINE\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM SATURDAY\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 (Inaudible) .\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A sea of protesters in Tel Aviv this weekend demanding new elections and calling for a deal to release hostages six months after the terror attack on October 7th. I'm joined now by White House National Security Communications Adviser, John Kirby. Good to see you, Admiral Kirby. And, and let's start with that interview with Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Andr\u233\'00\'E9s.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL/\uc2 HAMAS\uc2  WAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVEN WORLD KITCHEN WORKERS KILLED BY ISRAELI STRIKE\par \par \uc2 JOHN KIRBY (WHITE HOUSE NATIONAL COMMUNICATIONS ADVISER)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He says, this is a war against humanity, and things have to change now.\par \par \uc2 JOHN KIRBY (WHITE HOUSE NATIONAL COMMUNICATIONS ADVISER)\par \par \uc2 Our, our hearts continue to go out with Chef Andr\u233\'00\'E9s and his whole team at \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2 . As you know, the President spoke to him. The President shares that grief and sorrow. And as we have made clear, there's gonna have to be some changes to the way the \uc2 Israeli Defense Forces\uc2  are prosecuting these operations in Gaza to make sure that this doesn't happen again. And some of the changes we talked about, certainly more humanitarian aid and assistance getting in. But just as critically, Martha, there's got to be changes in the deconfliction process, the information flow between aid workers on the ground and the \uc2 IDF\uc2  and their headquarters so that, that this kind of targeting can't happen again.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: US WARNS OF POLICY CHANGES IF ISRAEL DOESN'T CHANGE APPROACH\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Are, are you satisfied with the investigation? He, he clearly wants to see more done. Would you like to a further investigation?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JOS\u201\'00\'C9 ANDR\u201\'00\'C9S CALLS FOR DEEPER PROBE INTO AID WORKER DEATHS\par \par \uc2 JOHN KIRBY (WHITE HOUSE NATIONAL COMMUNICATIONS ADVISER)\par \par \uc2 We're, we're looking at the investigation right now, Martha. We haven't come to any conclusions one way or another. This was an investigation that was done sort of akin to like an inspector general, so it was outside the chain of command. But again, we're working our way through that.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Andr\u233\'00\'E9s said he questioned the Israeli claim that the drones could not see the logo on top of the car. Is he right to question that?\par \par \uc2 JOHN KIRBY (WHITE HOUSE NATIONAL COMMUNICATIONS ADVISER)\par \par \uc2 I don't know. We haven't also seen, as far as I know, haven't seen any, any of the specific video evidence, so it's hard to know what their sight picture was at night. Now, certainly, operations at night can be more difficult. There's technology, though, that can allow you to burn through the darkness to, to see better.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In drones, right?\par \par \uc2 JOHN KIRBY (WHITE HOUSE NATIONAL COMMUNICATIONS ADVISER)\par \par \uc2 In, in, in drones and infra - infrared technology. But I just don't know what, I, I don't know what they were using in terms of their, their technology to look at this. But clearly, and they have admitted that they obviously made a mistake here. What really matters is that they take steps going forward to make sure it can't happen again and that they're transparent about those steps.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and I just want to talk about rules of engagement. The Israeli military says, it's a grave mistake. But that drone operator spotted who they said he thought it was a gunman get into one of those cars, and yet, even if it wasn't an aid convoy, they destroyed three cars. Is that legitimate rules of engagement?\par \par \uc2 JOHN KIRBY (WHITE HOUSE NATIONAL COMMUNICATIONS ADVISER)\par \par \uc2 I think, again, we're gonna have to work our way through this investigation and the decision-making process that goes in, not just one, but then three strikes and what the, what the intelligence was telling them, at least what they believed it was. We know from our own experience that the intelligence you get and you process and you analyze may not always be accurate, and you act on that intelligence. So, again, we just have to learn a lot little bit more about this investigation to, to see.\par \par \uc2 JOHN KIRBY (WHITE HOUSE NATIONAL COMMUNICATIONS ADVISER)\par \par \uc2 But as I said, I don't want to sound like a broken record, but what really matters is they make the deconfliction changes and the communication changes so that this doesn't happen again. I mean, we've already seen it, Chef Andr\u233\'00\'E9s is concerned, of course, about operating on the ground. Other aid organizations are probably making these difficult decisions, and we got to make sure that they feel safe and secure getting into Gaza and distributing that aid.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You, you said the US position towards Israel could change if there is not a dramatic increase in humanitarian aid and a reduction of the violence against civilians. What will the consequences be if they don't do that?\par \par \uc2 ANTONY BLINKEN\uc2  (SECRETARY OF STATE)\par \par \uc2 Well, I don't want to get ahead of the President or close down his decision space, but you heard us say, and Secretary Blinken as well...\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What does that mean, "Decision space"?\par \par \uc2 JOHN KIRBY (WHITE HOUSE NATIONAL COMMUNICATIONS ADVISER)\par \par \uc2 If their, if, well, that we, we need to see change over time. So, these announcements, Martha, they're very welcome, and they're good. And they are some of the things that the President asked specifically for Prime Minister Netanyahu to do, in terms of opening up more additional crossings, allowing more trucks in, getting the deconfliction process in place. But now, we have judge it over time. We have to see, not pass, passed the announcements and see if they actually meet these commitments over time, in a sustained and verifiable way so that confidence can be restored, not just between aid workers and the \uc2 IDF\uc2 , but between the, the people of Gaza and the, and, and Israel.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Would you rule out slowing down or pausing weapons transfers if this does not happen?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL THE US PLACE RESTRICTIONS ON ARMS TO ISRAEL?\par \par \uc2 JOHN KIRBY (WHITE HOUSE NATIONAL COMMUNICATIONS ADVISER)\par \par \uc2 It's not my place to rule anything in or out today. What I can tell you is that, as the President made clear to Prime Minister Netanyahu, we've got to see some changes in the way they're prosecuting these operations, or we're gonna have to think about making changes in our own policy towards Gaza.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, let's...\par \par \uc2 JOHN KIRBY (WHITE HOUSE NATIONAL COMMUNICATIONS ADVISER)\par \par \uc2 Israel has a right to defend itself. And I think it's important to also remember, they live in a tough neighborhood. We're all focused on the fight in Gaza as we rightly should be. But they're facing threats from Iran and from Iran-backed groups all throughout the region, and we've got to make sure that they're ready that as well.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL - \uc2 HAMAS\uc2  WAR TIMELINE\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And quite a threat right now. But I want to show you a timeline, Admiral Kirby, and wonder why things might change this time. November 6th, death toll in Gaza passes 10,000. November 10th, Secretary Blinken, "Far too many Palestinians have been killed." December 12th, Biden says, "Israel is losing support to indiscriminate bombing." December 22nd, death toll in Gaza passes 20,000.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) February 8th, President Biden calls a response in Gaza "over the top." February 29th, death toll in Gaza passes 30,000. March 2nd, Vice President Harris said, "There must be an immediate ceasefire for at least the next six weeks." April 1st, \uc2 IDF\uc2  strike kill seven \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  aid workers. So, why do you think anything will change?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP: THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE\par \par \uc2 JOHN KIRBY (WHITE HOUSE NATIONAL COMMUNICATIONS ADVISER)\par \par \uc2 I'm glad you brought that timeline up because it shows the degree, the growing degree of frustration that we've had with the way these operations are being prosecuted and the way that the Israelis are acting on the ground in terms of civilian casualties. So, it, we have been increasingly frustrated. And again, that was a core message that the President delivered to Prime Minister Netanyahu in their phone call this week, this past week, that they've got to do more, they've got to make changes. Now, the Prime Minister assured the President that he would do that. We've seen some announcements in those early hours. That's welcome. We've got to see more. We've got to see it over time.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the Israeli media is reporting this morning that the \uc2 IDF\uc2  withdrew ground troops from southern Gaza. They've been fighting there in Khan Younis for four months. What, what does that tell you?\par \par \uc2 ANTONY BLINKEN\uc2  (SECRETARY OF STATE)\par \par \uc2 Well, it doesn't, it's hard to know exactly what that tells us right now. This was just an announcement that they made. I'd certainly let them speak to their operations as we understand it and through their public announcements. It is really just about rest and refit for these troops that have been on the ground for four months, and not necessarily, that we can tell, indicative of a some coming new operation for these troops. They've been on the ground for four months. The, the, the word we're getting is they're tired. They need to be refit.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and, and just one final question. There's, there's such a dramatic disagreement between what the Israelis say and what they say in Gaza about what is happening on the ground. Obviously, we've seen some video of that. Why hasn't the US insisted on more on the ground accountability? Why aren't we, and I'm not saying in a combat position, on the ground accounting for this ourselves to make sure the rules of law are followed?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TODAY MARKS SIX MONTHS SINCE START OF ISRAEL-\uc2 HAMAS\uc2  WAR\par \par \uc2 ANTONY BLINKEN\uc2  (SECRETARY OF STATE)\par \par \uc2 Well, the President's been very clear. We're not going to have US boots on the ground in Gaza fighting in that war, involved in that conflict. What we will do is make sure that they have the tools and capabilities they need to defend themselves. And what we will also do, and the President made this clear, is hold Israel accountable for the way in which they're conducting these operations. You heard it from Chef Andr\u233\'00\'E9s, and he's not wrong, you can do both. You can be a good friend of Israel, as we are in helping them defend themselves. At the same time, holding them to an appropriate standard of accountability and effectiveness from a military perspective where they are protecting civilians.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay. Thanks so much for coming in this morning. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 ANTONY BLINKEN\uc2  (SECRETARY OF STATE)\par \par \uc2 Yes, ma'am.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Up next, a very personal reunion. Twenty years after the siege of Sadr City in Iraq, my conversation with the soldiers who fought there about their long road home. We're back in a moment.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020240417ek4700003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 JOSE ANDRES SPEAKS OUT AFTER DEADLY ISRAELI STRIKE SAYS AID WORKERS WERE TARGETED "SYSTEMATICALLY, CAR BY CAR"\b0\par\par\uc2 567 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SMITH, TRAVEL, STORM, FLOODING, POWER OUTAGE\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPRING SNOWSTORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE THAN THREE FEET EXPECTED IN SOME PARTS OF NEW ENGLAND\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, NOR'EASTER\par \par \uc2 EARTHQUAKE, TAIWAN, SEARCH, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEARCH FOR SURVIVORS AFTER DEADLY EARTHQUAKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEATH TOLL RISES AS CREWS RACE TO FREE PEOPLE TRAPPED IN THE RUBBLE\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, WAT, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ANDRES, FALK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JOSE ANDRES SPEAKS OUT AFTER DEADLY ISRAELI STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SAYS AID WORKERS WERE TARGETED "SYSTEMATICALLY, CAR BY CAR"\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now we have the fallout after the deadly Israeli airstrike that killed seven aid workers in Gaza. The incident is threatening to make the humanitarian crisis there even worse. Britt Clennett is on the scene in Jerusalem. Good morning, Britt.\par \par \uc2 BRITT CLENNETT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Robin. Yeah, pressure is mounting on Israel ahead of President Biden's expected call with Israeli Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 . It's their first direct contact since the airstrike that killed seven aid workers, including a dual US citizen.\par \par \uc2 BRITT CLENNETT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, renowned chef and \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  founder Jose Andres speaking out after seven of his staffers bringing aid into Gaza were killed by an Israeli airstrike.\par \par \uc2 JOSE ANDRES (FOUNDER / CHEF WORLD CENTRAL KITCHEN)\par \par \uc2 They were targeting us in a de-conflicting zone, in an area controlled by the \uc2 IDF\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 BRITT CLENNETT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Andres claiming the \uc2 IDF\uc2  targeted systematically, car-by-car, humanitarian vehicles.\par \par \uc2 JOSE ANDRES (FOUNDER / CHEF WORLD CENTRAL KITCHEN)\par \par \uc2 It was over 1.5, 1.8 kilometers with a very defined humanitarian convoy that had signs in the top, in the roof.\par \par \uc2 BRITT CLENNETT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Prime Minister Netanyahu says Israel deeply regrets the incident.\par \par \uc2 BRITT CLENNETT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Those vehicles were clearly marked. These were three cars in a row travelling in a convoy that were targeted. What do you say to that?\par \par \uc2 OPHIR FALK PHD (FOREIGN POLICY ADVISER FOR PRIME MINISTER NETANYAHU)\par \par \uc2 That's absurd. The last thing that we would want in the world is to endanger civilian lives. This war is a complex war. The incident happened in the middle of the night. It was a complex situation. It should not have happened.\par \par \uc2 BRITT CLENNETT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (CO) This satellite photos shows the destroyed vehicles on the road for humanitarian aid, stretching a mile and half apart.\par \par \uc2 JOSE ANDRES (FOUNDER / CHEF WORLD CENTRAL KITCHEN)\par \par \uc2 If we were targeted this way, I need to understand that this was (inaudible). I need to understand that this was not by somebody that is above law and order that decided just to kill us because, I don't know, maybe because I made a tweet that was very strong against President Netanyahu. I don't know.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD CENTRAL KITCHEN AID WORKERS KILLED\par \par \uc2 BRITT CLENNETT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Among those killed, a Palestinian, three British citizens, an Australian, a Polish national, and a dual American-Canadian citizen Jacob Flickinger.\par \par \uc2 BRITT CLENNETT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, Biden's call with Netanyahu is coming as tensions in the region flair up. Israel on high alert after Iran vowed revenge after an attack that killed one of its top commanders. The \uc2 IDF\uc2  now pausing leave for all of its combat units amid the possible escalation. George?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Britt, thanks.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240424ek440002y\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WH: "OUTRAGED" OVER AID WORKER DEATHS ISRAEL CRITICIZED FOR AIRSTRIKE THAT KILLED SEVEN IN GAZA\b0\par\par\uc2 484 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADO\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , KIRBY, NETANYAHU, BLINKEN, AIRSTRIKES, WAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: W.H.: "OUTRAGED" OVER AID WORKER DEATHS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The major story overseas tonight, the deadly Israeli airstrike killing seven aid workers delivering food to Gaza. One of the workers, a US citizen. You will see the images here tonight, what was left behind. You can actually see the convoy clearly marked. It was struck three times. They had alerted the Israelis beforehand. The White House tonight saying, it is outraged. Prime Minister Netanyahu calling it unintentional, saying it happens in war, drawing outrage for his words, too. Britt Clennett from Israel tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL CRITICIZED FOR AIRSTRIKE THAT KILLED SEVEN IN GAZA\par \par \uc2 BRITT CLENNETT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, Israel facing mounting questions over why three clearly marked aid vehicles from the \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  were targeted in an IDF airstrike, killing seven workers delivering supplies. The aid group says the workers coordinated their movements with the Israeli military and were traveling in a three-car convoy in an area deemed safe after unloading more than 100 tons of food to this warehouse brought to Gaza. ABC News confirming the convoy was then struck three times. A charred van, another with a large hole in the roof where you can clearly see their logo, are the images now sparking worldwide criticism.\par \par \uc2 BRITT CLENNETT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  calling the incident unforgivable and immediately halting operations. The victims, a Palestinian, a US-Canadian dual citizen, three from the UK, Lalzawmi Frankcom from Australia, and Damian Sobol from Poland. In his first comments following the attack, Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  launching an investigation, but saying it was unintentional and that it, quote, "happens during war." Hours later, taking a softer approach, saying their hearts go out to their families and home countries. Tonight, the White House outraged.\par \par \uc2 JOHN KIRBY (WHITE HOUSE NATIONAL SECURITY COMMUNICATIONS ADVISER)\par \par \uc2 This incident is emblematic of a larger problem, and evidence of why distribution of aid in Gaza has been so challenging.\par \par \uc2 ANTONY BLINKEN\uc2  (SECRETARY OF STATE)\par \par \uc2 These people are heroes. They run into the fire, not away from it.\par \par \uc2 BRITT CLENNETT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Despite the deepening tensions between President Biden and Netanyahu, just days ago, Biden approved the transfer of additional weapons to Israel, including 2,000-pound bombs, which have been connected to mass casualties.\par \par \uc2 BRITT CLENNETT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, David, just coming in now, the \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  releasing these images of all seven victims of that aid attack. You see them there, including the US dual citizen. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They do extraordinary work, the bravery of these aid workers trying to get food in not only in Gaza, but around the world. Britt Clennett tonight, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240404ek4200004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FAST FOOD MINIMUM WAGE HIKE TAKES EFFECT WHAT CALIFORNIA PAY BUMP COULD MEAN FOR JOBS & PRICES\b0\par\par\uc2 423 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR STORM\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, FLOODING, HIGHWAY, EROSION\par \par \uc2 BRIDGE, COLLAPSE, WRECKAGE, CREWS, BROWN, BUTTIGIEG\par \par \uc2 CALIFORNIA, PAY HIKE, FAST FOOD, \uc2 AT&T\uc2 , DATA BREACH\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It certainly will. Okay, Terry, thanks very much. There were two big consumer headlines overnight. The California minimum wage bump for fast food workers, and a major \uc2 AT&T\uc2  data breach. Chief business correspondent Rebecca Jarvis is here tracking both stories. Good morning, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FAST FOOD MINIMUM WAGE HIKE TAKES EFFECT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT CALIFORNIA PAY BUMP COULD MEAN FOR JOBS & PRICES\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. Hi, guys. And beginning this morning more than half a million fast food workers in California will get that big pay raise, a $4 increase from $16 an hour to $20 an hour. That's 25% more in their pay checks. Advocates say it's about time, given the high cost of living and inflation.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The new law only affects fast food workers at chains with at least 60 locations nationwide. But some small business owners are feeling the pressure to compete, and this could also mean higher prices for consumers because they'll want to cover those costs.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Rebecca, 73 million consumers hit by this \uc2 AT&T\uc2  data breach.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR \uc2 AT&T\uc2  BREACH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE THAN 70 MILLION CURRENT & FORMER ACCOUNT HOLDERS AFFECTED\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is just gigantic that we're hearing about this morning. One in five Americans impacted. 73 million people had their data, including social security numbers, pass codes, birthdates, leaked on the dark web. And you don't even have to be a current \uc2 AT&T\uc2  customer to be impacted. The company says 90% of the people hit are former account holders with data from 2019 and earlier. =\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The company says it's reaching out to people impacted, resetting pass codes for current account holders, and working with cyber security experts. Personal call history and financial information was not included in the leak. And \uc2 AT&T\uc2  says it's launched a robust investigation. =\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Guys, I just want to say here, too, be careful because sometimes the scam artists come out when there's a breach like this and they send fake email, fake letters. So really check the origin of that note to you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240423ek410002w\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FAST FOOD MINIMUM WAGE RAISE $20 PER HOUR AS OF TOMORROW IN CALIFORNIA\b0\par\par\uc2 621 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 March 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOW, WIND, RAIN & TORNADO THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EASTER SUNDAY STORMS\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TRACK\par \par \uc2 POPE FRANCIS, EASTER SUNDAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EASTER AROUND THE WORLD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLY CELEBRATIONS FOR CHRISTIANS IN JERUSALEM\par \par \uc2 BRIDGE, COLLAPSE, CLEANUP, MOORE, DESANTIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CREWS BEGIN CUTTING APART COLLAPSED BRIDGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HULL OF SHIP SAID TO BE DAMAGED BUT INTACT\par \par \uc2 BUTTIGIEG, BRIDGE, COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRANSPORTATION SECRETARY BUTTIGIEG ON BRIDGE COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CRANES ARRIVE & CREWS BEGIN CUTTING TO REMOVE THE WRECKAGE\par \par \uc2 PLANE, CRASH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY CALIFORNIA PLANE CRASH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST TWO KILLED IN SMALL PLANE ACCIDENT IN TRUCKEE\par \par \uc2 WAGES, LOGAN, SAVORY, JOHNSON, HOWIE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FAST FOOD MINIMUM WAGE RAISE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: $20 PER HOUR AS OF TOMORROW IN CALIFORNIA\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. Well, now to the higher minimum wage going into effect tomorrow for some fast-food workers in California, and what it could mean for franchise owners and customers. ABC's Jaclyn Lee joins us live in Los Angeles with the details about that. Good morning, Jaclyn.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Janai, good morning. Advocates argue that this is a step in the right direction given just how expensive it is to live in California. But others argue, this is bad for business and the increase cost will pass to the consumer.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, some fast-food workers in California will soon be making at least $20 an hour, the highest minimum wage within the restaurant industry, set to begin Monday.\par \par \uc2 JOHN LOHAN PHD (PROFESSOR OF LABOR & EMPLOYMENT STUDIES SFSU)\par \par \uc2 This is a start to improve the wages and also improve the working conditions in the industry.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This is a $4 increase from the current minimum wage in the Golden State, meaning some workers will make 25% more on their paychecks. Advocates say it's about time given the extremely high cost of living and inflation.\par \par \uc2 DILLON SAVORY (EXEC DIR FRESNO-MADERA-TULARE-KINGS CLC CA LABOR FED)\par \par \uc2 More and more folks are unable to raise bigger families or at least, you know, put themselves in a position to retire effectively.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW MINIMUM WAGE\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The new law impacts more than half a million workers in California and only affects fast food chains with at least 60 locations nationwide. Some small business owners worry they won't be able to compete with the wage increase.\par \par \uc2 ALEX JOHNSON (CEO PRETZEL POWER INC)\par \par \uc2 That's going to impact us by an increase of $470,000 annually across those ten stores. It means that we have to raise prices, which we don't want to do.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Two Pizza Hut franchises in California reportedly laid off 1,200 in-house delivery drivers in preparation for the new minimum wage hike. Kerri Harper-Howie owns 21 McDonald's and says she does not anticipate closing any locations.\par \par \uc2 KERRI HARPER-HOWIE (MCDONALD'S FRANCHISEE)\par \par \uc2 The bottom line is, everyone is not going to be able to afford even the measured and carefully thought-out price changes that we are going to be implementing as a necessary part of us responding to the increase.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  saying in a statement they plan to offset the minimum wage increase by changing their pricing as well as other efficiencies in their stores. \uc2 McDonald\uc2 's saying they'll provide price recommendations. Now, this law goes into effect tomorrow. There are some exceptions for bakeries and those smaller fast-food stores that you find inside airports and grocery stores. Gio?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Jaclyn, thank you so much for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240422ek3v00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ALL EYES ON NEW JOBS REPORT EXPECTED TO SHOW SLOWER BUT STILL STRONG HIRING IN FEBRUARY\b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 March 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF THE UNION\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, SPEECH, DEMOCRACY, PUTIN, IMMIGRATION, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, SPEECH, BRITT, REPUBLICANS, HECKLING\par \par \uc2 GAZA, US TROOPS, PORT, HUMANITARIAN AID\par \par \uc2 UNITED, PLANE, TIRE, MIDAIR, HYNEK, FLAMES, \uc2 FAA\par \par \uc2 JOBS REPORTS, UNEMPLOYMENT, SALARIES, FED\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Kayna, thanks. Now to the new jobs numbers this morning. Elizabeth Schulze is tracking the data. Good morning, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON NEW JOBS REPORT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPECTED TO SHOW SLOWER BUT STILL STRONG HIRING IN FEBRUARY\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, George. And this jobs report is gonna tell us if companies are slowing down what's been an incredibly fast pace of hiring. It's expected to show that 198,000 jobs were added to the American workforce in February. That would be less than the blockbuster 353,000 number in January.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But this is still a healthy job market. And you can really see that when you look at the unemployment rate there at 3.7%. That's near a five decade low. And what that means is that people out looking for work are generally able to find a job right now. When you look at the industries that are hiring, it's health care, hospitality, state and local government.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And people in those jobs are also seeing their salaries go up right now. This report today is important for the Fed as it thinks about cutting interest rates. We know that it was planning to do that the spring. But if hiring keeps defying expectations, that might not happen until later in the year. That means you might have to wait a little bit longer to see your credit card borrowing cost or your mortgage rate go down, guys.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240320ek3800006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TENTATIVE DEAL REACHED IN NEWTON TEACHER STRIKE AGREEMENT ANNOUNCED AFTER STRIKE KEPT CHILDREN OUT OF CLASS FOR TWO WEEKS\b0\par\par\uc2 148 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 February 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: US HIT TARGETS IN SYRIA AND IRAQ: STRIKING BACK\par \par \uc2 SYRIA, IRAQ, US, AIRSTRIKES, DRONE, ATTACK\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, US, SYRIA, IRAQ, RESPOND, AIRSTRIKES, DRONE, ATTACK\par \par \uc2 CALIFORNIA, ATMOSPHERIC, STORM, INTENSE\par \par \uc2 SENATE, BIPARTISAN, BORDER, UKRAINE, ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, CAMPAIGN, 2024, SOUTH CAROLINA\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, SHOOTING, DELIBERATIONS, TRIAL, JURY\par \par \uc2 OHIO, TRAIN, HEALTH, EFFECTS, TOXIC, DERAILMENT\par \par \uc2 NEWTON, TEACHERS, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It is back to school for teachers and students in Newton, Massachusetts. The Newton Teachers Association announcing Friday night they have reached a tentative agreement on a new four-year contract with the Newton School Committee. The teachers strike kept children out of the classroom for more than two weeks in one of Massachusetts' largest school districts. Union and city officials say classes will resume on Monday. Gio.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240221ek2300009\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 US EMPLOYERS ADDED 353,000 JOBS IN JANUARY UNEMPLOYMENT RATE HOLDS STEADY AT HISTORICALLY LOW 3.7 PERCENT\b0\par\par\uc2 414 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 February 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: US HIT TARGETS IN SYRIA AND IRAQ: STRIKING BACK\par \par \uc2 SYRIA, IRAQ, US, AIRSTRIKES, DRONE, ATTACK\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, US, SYRIA, IRAQ, RESPOND, AIRSTRIKES, DRONE, ATTACK\par \par \uc2 CALIFORNIA, ATMOSPHERIC, STORM, INTENSE\par \par \uc2 SENATE, BIPARTISAN, BORDER, UKRAINE, ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, CAMPAIGN, 2024, SOUTH CAROLINA\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, SHOOTING, DELIBERATIONS, TRIAL, JURY\par \par \uc2 OHIO, TRAIN, HEALTH, EFFECTS, TOXIC, DERAILMENT\par \par \uc2 NEWTON, TEACHERS, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 JOBS, JANUARY, UNEMPLOYMENT\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Whit. To the economy now and the latest jobs report was a shocker, even for the experts with double the expected growth in hiring. ABC's Alexis Christoforous is here now to break it all down. Good morning, Alexis.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Gio. You're right, that blockbuster jobs report even took many Wall Street pros by surprise. The economy added 353,000 jobs in January, twice as many as expected. The unemployment rate held steady at 3.7 percent. Job gains for November and December were also revised upwards, meaning more jobs were added in those months than previously thought. All this despite higher interest rates. Economists say the hot jobs report throws cold water on the idea of a March interest rate cut from the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOT JOBS MARKET CHILLS INTEREST RATE CUTS. FED FEARS SLASHING RATES TOO FAST COULD SPARK INFLATION\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) If the Fed makes it cheaper to borrow money too quickly, it risks a run-up in consumer spending on things like homes and cars, and that could spark a rebound in inflation just as prices are cooling off. Once again, workers' wages outpaced inflation rising, 4.5 percent compared to a year ago, giving consumers more buying power. That hiring boom, it took place across a bunch of different industries led by professional and business services, health care once again, retail, and government. The hiring spree comes even as other industry, like media and tech get hit with major layoffs. Companies, including \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 , and \uc2 Google\uc2  are tightening their belts after record hiring during the pandemic. Those high-profile job cuts are now starting to chip away at workers' confidence. The number of Americans quitting their jobs is now at the lowest level in three years. Guys.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. It is so good to see people getting those much-needed jobs. Alexis, thank you for bringing that to us.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240221ek230000a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ALL EYES ON NEW JOBS REPORT EXPECTED TO SHOW STRONG HIRING DESPITE RECENT HIGH-PROFILE LAYOFFS\b0\par\par\uc2 647 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 February 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ON THE MOVE\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, FLOODING, SNOW, MUDSLIDES\par \par \uc2 SOLDIERS, ATTACK, RETALIATION, AUSTIN, MILITANTS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, CAMPAIGN, TRUMP, SENATE, HOUSE, BIPARTISAN\par \par \uc2 PLANE CRASH, HOMES, FIRE, FATALITIES, RENNE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, TRIAL, TESTIMONY, SHOOTING, JOURNAL\par \par \uc2 SUPER BOWL, VEGAS, JOFFRAY, CHIEFS, 49ERS, USHER, TIESTO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR STORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "GROUNDHOG DAY"\par \par \uc2 APPLE, VISION PRO SPATIAL, O'BRIEN, APPS, BROWNLEE\par \par \uc2 SPRING BREAK, MIAMI, CRACKDOWN, MEINER, DESANTIS\par \par \uc2 MEDICAL DEBT, LAMONT, RELIEF, ELIGIBILITY, CANCEL\par \par \uc2 GROUNDHOG DAY, SPRING, TRADITION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EL NINO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEBRUARY - APRIL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BACK-TO-BACK STORMS: ON THE MOVE\par \par \uc2 NWS\uc2 , STORM, DANGEROUS, RAIN, FLOOD\par \par \uc2 JOBS, HIRING, LAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, now to a workforce reality check. The new jobs report is expected to be strong even as some industries, like tech, tighten their payrolls. Elizabeth Schulze joins us with where you can find a new job if you're looking. Good morning, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Eva. Despite those layoffs in several high-profile industries so far this year, the American jobs market overall is in solid shape. This morning's job report is expected to show that employers added 185,000 jobs to their payrolls in January. On average, every month last year 225,000 jobs were added, which is a historically strong pace. You can think about it this way, right now there are 1.5 jobs available for every one person looking for work. These are the industries that are hiring the most; health care, hospitality, construction, and local government. It is a different picture than those recent job cuts in industries like media, retail and tech, companies including \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 , and \uc2 Google\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Analysts say some of what's going on there is that those firms are slimming down after record hiring during the pandemic. But still, there are signs that Americans are feeling less optimistic about their job prospects. The number of people quitting their jobs is now at the lowest number in three year, which is a sign that people are worried that they won't be able to find a new or better job if they leave their current ones. Guys.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:10 APPLE CEO TIM COOK LIVE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Elizabeth, thanks. And coming up in our "gma" Morning Menu, Michael's made his way to the \uc2 Apple\uc2  store in New York City for his exclusive with CEO \uc2 Tim Cook\uc2  on the new Apple Vision Pro.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hi, Michael.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:14 POP NEWS\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Inaudible) Michael. And also ahead, Taylor, Miley and SZA could make history at the Grammys. Sam, you're gonna tell us what to watch for on music's biggest night.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:30 USHER ONE-ON-ONE\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, buckle up. I get to sit in for "Pop News." That's never good. Plus, Usher is going to tell us how he's getting ready to perform before the biggest audience of the year when he headlines the Super Bowl halftime show. Will it be the biggest audience ever for a Super Bowl? We'll see.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:19 DEALS AND STEALS!\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Tory is upstairs. Tory, I know you've got some special guests. Good morning.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I do, Sam. We are celebrating black history month with these awesome business owners bringing us beauty, baby accessories, and Oprah's favorite hot sauce, all at fantastic prices. That's coming up next right here on "gma."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA, FRIDAY, FEB 2\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And welcome back to "gma." We want to go straight to Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240220ek220000h\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TEACHERS STRIKE ENTERING SECOND FULL WEEK WHAT WALKOUT IN MASSACHUSETTS COULD MEAN NATIONALLY\b0\par\par\uc2 369 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 January 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 FLOODING, STORM, WEATHER, TRACK, SNOW\par \par \uc2 PATRICK, IMMIGRATION BORDER, SCHUMER, MAYORKAS, TRUMP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BORDER BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW DETAILS ON POTENTIAL SECURITY DEAL AS BIDEN & SPEAKER JOHNSON AT ODDS\par \par \uc2 PRIMARY, ELECTION, TRUMP, BIDEN, HALEY, HARRIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAMPAIGN SHIFTS TO NEVADA & SOUTH CAROLINA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN, VP HARRIS & TRUMP ALL HIT THE TRAIL AS NEVADA UP NEXT IN REP PRIMARIES\par \par \uc2 BROWN, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, HOUTHIS, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING FEARS OF ESCALATION IN THE MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. CONTINUES STRIKES AGAINST MILITANTS AS HOUTHI MISSILE HITS SHIP IN GUL OF ADEN\par \par \uc2 TEACHERS, STRIKE, MASSACHUSETTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEACHERS STRIKE ENTERING SECOND FULL WEEK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT WALKOUT IN MASSACHUSETTS COULD MEAN NATIONALLY\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to a major teachers strike entering its second full week now. The walkout in Newton, Massachusetts is the state's longest strike in decades, 12,000 students caught in the middle, and the teachers' union may face big fines. ABC's Reena Roy is here with more on that. Good morning, Reena.\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Gio, good morning to you. Thousands of students are still out of school as the teacher strike in Newton, Massachusetts continues. And this is having a major impact with some families struggling to find child care.\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) With teachers on the picket line, about 12,000 students are out of class, as you said. The school committee and teachers' union struggling to agree on compensations for teachers among other demands like class size and mental health resources for students. The union saying, teachers desperately want to be back in school, but that they need the school to work with them. School officials calling the strike unnecessary saying, the union rejected a proposal to continue negotiations. And just some context here, strikes amongst public employees like teachers are actually illegal in Massachusetts. And this strike is just the latest that we're seeing.\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Larger school districts in places like Los Angeles and Portland dealing with similar issues last year as teachers fight for better wages and benefits. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240212ek1s00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MOTHER'S FIGHT TO WORK REMOTELY POPULAR COMPANY FACING BOYCOTT AFTER DENYING EMPLOYEE'S REQUEST\b0\par\par\uc2 766 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 January 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PRIMARY, ELECTION, TRUMP, HALEY, RAMASWAMY\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, PRIMARY, POLLING, NEW HAMPSHIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLE FOR NEW HAMPSHIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHERE THE POLLS STAND & WHAT TO WATCH FOR IN CRUCIAL PRIMARY\par \par \uc2 HOUTHIS, IRAN, YEMEN, AIRSTRIKES\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, FLOODING, TRACK, STORM, TRAVEL, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WICKED WINTER WEATHER WREAKING HAVOC\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLOODING EMERGENCY IN WEST AS SNOW & ICE HIT THE HEARTLAND\par \par \uc2 WAVE, MARSHALL ISLANDS, SIENKIEWICZ, MORGAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTREME WAVE CRASHES INTO U.S. MILITARY BASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VIDEO CAPTURES SUDDEN DESTRUCTION & FLOODING\par \par \uc2 OSCARS, NOMINATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO THE OSCAR NOMINATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHO WILL VIE FOR HOLLYWOOD'S BIGGEST PRIZE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "BARBIE"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, TRIAL, MYRE, MCDONALD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SCHOOL SHOOTER'S MOM ON TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHARGED WITH INVOLUNTARY MANSLAUGHTER FOLLOWING DEADLY 2021 RAMPAGE\par \par \uc2 WILLIS, HASTINGS, WADE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GEORGIA DA IN TRUMP CASE UNDER SCRUTINY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FANI WILLIS FACING ALLEGATIONS OF ROMANTIC RELATIONSHIP WITH TOP PROSECUTOR\par \par \uc2 WILLIS, WADE, CRUMBLEY, TRIAL\par \par \uc2 KYTE BABY, HUGHES, LIU, BOYCOTT, APOLOGY\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And back now on "GMA" with the controversy over the popular baby clothing company, Kyte Baby. Lara is here with the story of a new mom who was fired from the company with her baby still in the NICU. Lara, good morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MOTHER'S FIGHT TO WORK REMOTELY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POPULAR COMPANY FACING BOYCOTT AFTER DENYING EMPLOYEE'S REQUEST\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Mary. That is right. Kyte Baby, known for infant clothing and sleep sacks, well, this morning, they are responding to massive backlash because of their treatment of that new mom who shared her story on social media requesting to work remotely to care for her newly adopted son, and then was fired.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, a popular baby clothing company is facing a consumer boycott after an employee's request to work remotely while her newborn is in the hospital was denied.\par \par \uc2 MARISSA HUGHES (MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 Hey, everyone.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Marissa Hughes of Texas adopted a son in December when she worked for Kyte Baby, a company that sells infant sleep sacks and clothing. Hughes' premature baby is hospitalized in the neonatal intensive care unit nine hours away from her home in Dallas. She says her request to work remotely was denied and she was fired after not returning from her allotted two-week maternity leave. Hughes sharing her story online, and the backlash was swift. Other parents sharing videos tossing their Kyte Baby products and vowing not to support the company.\par \par \uc2 TIKTOK INFLUENCER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I will never give Kyte Baby another dime of my money.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, the CEO of Kyte Baby has posted two apology videos after her first was criticized as being insincere.\par \par \uc2 YING LIU (CEO KYTE BABY)\par \par \uc2 I wanted to hop on here to sincerely apologize to Marissa.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In her new apology video, the CEO offering Hughes a new position with the company in addition to announcing policy changes.\par \par \uc2 YING LIU (CEO KYTE BABY)\par \par \uc2 It was scripted. I memorized it. I just basically just read it. It wasn't sincere. This was a terrible decision. I was insensitive, selfish.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But Hughes responding, saying it would not be appropriate for her to return to the company.\par \par \uc2 MARISSA HUGHES (MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 We're really encouraged to hear that there will be some changes made for current and future employees at the company.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, you heard it there, the CEO of Kyte Baby Ying Liu admitting in her second video apology that the first one was scripted and that it missed the mark. And she agreed with people who said Kyte Baby should be setting the example, not playing catchup, considering they are a woman-led company that sells baby products. The company's policy is changing for the better as of February 1st. So, that young woman\u8230\'20\'26.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So they got to the right choice eventually, yeah.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yep.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good to hear they're making changes. But still, I know a lot of moms, a lot of parents are talking about this one.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Lara, thank you for bringing that to us. But you're not going anywhere. You're sticking around for her "Play of the Day." So, you don't go anywhere either. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240206ek1n0000e\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MACY'S\uc2  ANNOUNCES BIG JOB CUTS RETAILER TO LAY OFF 2,350 EMPLOYEES, CLOSE FIVE STORES\b0\par\par\uc2 343 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 January 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, COLD, ICE, WIND CHILL, FIGHTS, HYPOTHERMIA\par \par \uc2 STORM, BUFFALO, SNOW, BILLS, AVERAGE\par \par \uc2 STORM, COLD, SNOW, ICE, TEMPS\par \par \uc2 PRIMARY, TRUMP, HALEY, DESANTIS, VOTERS\par \par \uc2 DOJ, UVLADE, FAILURES, REPORT, GARLAND, RUBIO, MATA\par \par \uc2 MIDDLE EAST, TENSIONS, US, STRIKES, HOUTHI\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, STUDENTS, DEBT, RELIEF, CANCELED\par \par \uc2 MACY'S\uc2 , LAYOFFS, EMPLOYEES, STORES\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Selina Wang, thank you so much. We're going to turn now to a couple of major business headlines this morning. Mortgage rates dropping and layoffs at one of the nation's top retailer. We're gonna begin here with Elizabeth Schulze with details on those job cuts. Good morning to you, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 MACY'S\uc2  ANNOUNCES BIG JOB CUTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RETAILER TO LAY OFF 2,350 EMPLOYEES, CLOSE FIVE STORES\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Gio. And this is a significant round of layoffs at an iconic American retailer. \uc2 Macy's\uc2  confirming it will cut more 2,300 jobs, accounting for 13% of its corporate staff, 3.5% of its overall work force. The retailer also says it will shut down five of its more than 700 store locations as it tries to adapt to a changing market place online.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 Macy's\uc2  is now the latest high profile company to announce job cuts this year, joining the ranks of \uc2 Google\uc2 , \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , \uc2 Apple\uc2  and Citi Group. But when you take a step back and look at the broader jobs market, layoffs are at a historically low rate. New government data shows that the number of Americans filing for unemployment benefits is at a 60-month low.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And industries like health care, hospitality are adding thousands of workers to their payrolls every month. So big picture, isolated layoffs in the tech sector last year did not stop the jobs market from powering forward. Many economists are hopeful that that trend can continue in 2024. George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240202ek1j00009\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 2024 BEST JOBS REPORT THIS YEAR'S TOP-RATED PROFESSIONS FROM US NEWS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,060 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 January 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, STORM, SNOW, MURPHY\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, RAIN, SNOW, STORMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRACKING THE PATH & TIMING OF MAJOR STORMS ON THE MOVE\par \par \uc2 BOEING 737 MAX 9, SAUER, BARTLETT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGER PLANE BLOWOUT INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALASKA & \uc2 UNITED AIRLINES\uc2  REPORT FINDING LOOSE PARTS ON SOME BOEING 737 MAX 9 JETS\par \par \uc2 HOMENDY, BOEING 737 MAX 9\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NTSB CHAIR ON PASSENGER PLANE BLOWOUT INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT'S BEEN LEARNED SO FAR ABOUT ALASKA AIRLINES INCIDENT?\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS, CAMPBELL, 2024 ELECTION, HALEY, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SIX DAYS TO IOWA CAUCUSES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CANDIDATES BATTLE THE ELEMENTS IN SCRAMBLE TO GAIN GROUND ON TRUMP\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, TRIAL\par \par \uc2 AUSTIN, RYDER, KIRBY, HOSPITALIZATION, SURGERY, HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, REUM, GARCIA, DE LA TORRE\par \par \uc2 REDDEN, HOLTHUS, DANIELS, ATTACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAN WHO ATTACKED JUDGE BACK IN COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEFENDANT WHO LEAPED OVER BENCH SENTENCED IN ORIGINAL CASE\par \par \uc2 COLLEGE FOOTBALL, CORUM, HARBAUGH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MICHIGAN'S CROWNING MOMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOLVERINE'S COMPLETE PERFECT SEASON & WIN FIRST NATIONAL TITLE SINCE 1997\par \par \uc2 RETIREMENT, MASTERSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, BLIZZARD, TORNADO, FLOOD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTREME WEATHER TAKES AIM ACROSS AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRACKING THE PATH & TIMING OF MAJOR STORMS\par \par \uc2 BLOWOUT, PLANE, ACCIDENT, ALASKA AIRLINES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGER PLANE BLOWOUT INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALASKA & \uc2 UNITED AIRLINES\uc2  REPORT LOOSE PARTS\par \par \uc2 HOTEL, EXPLOSION, FORT WORTH, INJURIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS HOTEL EXPLOSION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFICIALS SAY GAS LEAK LIKELY CAUSED BLAST\par \par \uc2 SCREEN TIME, BABIES, SENSORY DIFFERENCES, STUDY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY ON CHILDREN & SCREEN TIME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ASSOCIATION WITH SENSORY DIFFERENCES UNDER TWO\par \par \uc2 FINANCES, DECLUTTER, MONEY, ADVICE, SACKS, TU, DUNLOP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DECLUTTER YOUR FINANCES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO CUT COSTS & MAKE MONEY IN THE NEW YEAR\par \par \uc2 JOBS, "US NEWS", REPORT, GIOVANETTI\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And now for the financial decluttering, Michael.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 2024 BEST JOBS REPORT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS YEAR'S TOP-RATED PROFESSIONS FROM US NEWS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, yeah, we're going to tell you about jobs, Robin. Attention job seekers, let's look at this year's job report or job market with the "US News and World Report" 2024 best jobs list. Joining us is their loan expert, Erika Giovanetti. And Erika, thank you for joining us. Tell us how you came up with this year's report and which jobs made the cut.\par \par \uc2 ERIKA GIOVANETTI ("US NEWS & WORLD REPORT")\par \par \uc2 So, for our best jobs rankings, they are intended to help job seekers at every level achieve their career goals, whether you are a college student trying to decide between a degree, or whether you're just trying to go for a new career and make a switch. So, but whatever stage you're at in your career, there are a few things that are universally desired out of a job. And we use these factors to rank jobs based on, based on data from the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 . We looked at five main categories, including future growth, wage potential, employment, job safety and stability and work/life balance. So, you're really going to want to find something that has a little bit of everything in a foundation that you can kind of, you know, grow and make your own and use that as a way to cater your career desires for what you want.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You even have a list of jobs that, if you don't have a degree, jobs without a degree. Can you tell us what jobs in that, in that realm made the list?\par \par \uc2 ERIKA GIOVANETTI ("US NEWS & WORLD REPORT")\par \par \uc2 Yeah, so, the, we have several lists. We have our highest paying jobs without a degree and our best overall without a degree. And our rankings kind of go to prove that you don't need to have a four-year bachelor's degree in order to make a healthy living and earn a salary. So, out of the top 10 we have for highest paying, it's not really a surprise to see a lot of the trades on there. We have electricians, steel worker, but some of them were a little more surprising to me. So, we had\u160\'00\'A0flight attendant was number three, which...\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Really?\par \par \uc2 ERIKA GIOVANETTI ("US NEWS & WORLD REPORT")\par \par \uc2 Yeah, I mean, that's a solid job that if you want to enter a job with a low barrier to entry, you can go straight out of high school and learn on the job with training. Number one was executive assistant. And these are the right hand to the company leaders. And although they do make the most money out of any of the jobs that we ranked, they didn't perform as well for upward mobility, which is why you'll want to look at the overall best jobs, not just which ones pay the most, but the ones that allow you to grow in your position.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, which is important, which is very important. So, someone looking for a new career path or just for a new job, what do you suggest that they focus on?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOP OPPORTUNITIES FOR JOB SEEKERS IN THE NEW YEAR\par \par \uc2 ERIKA GIOVANETTI ("US NEWS & WORLD REPORT")\par \par \uc2 So, you know, the job search is always going to be so uniquely special from one person to the next, but there is, you know, there's still some advice that I think that everybody can take to heart. And if you're, I guess, trying to find what your calling is, or at least have a little bit of general direction for a field, start with your talents and what you're good at because you might find if you like doing something, you might be able to get paid to do it. If you are looking to make a switch later in your career life, you'll want to ask and, you know, kind of find your why and take stock. So, what was it in your current job that you're not receiving that you would like to get in your future job? And that's a really good place to start.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, that's some good advice, and that's a good start. Thanks to you. Erika, thank you so much. The "US News and World Report" 2024 best jobs list, it is out today.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240122ek190003e\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FINAL JOBS REPORT OF 2023 DUE THIS MORNING CAPS OFF A YEAR OF STRONG HIRING THAT DEFIED EXPECTATIONS\b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 January 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WINTER STORM\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, SNOW, ICE, TORNADO\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, STUDENTS, RICHARDS, IOWA\par \par \uc2 EPSTEIN, DOCUMENTS, MAXWELL, UNSEALED, CHURCHER\par \par \uc2 DEMOCRATS, HOUSE, TRUMP, MILLIONS, FOREIGN\par \par \uc2 MIDDLE EAST, BLINKEN, AID, DRONE, RYDER, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, CAMPAIGN, DEMOCRACY, SPEECH, TRUMP\par \par \uc2 JOBS, HIRING, ECONOMY, FEDERAL RESERVE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mary Bruce, thanks. Now to the new jobs numbers, they're out this morning. Elizabeth Schulze is tracking what this could mean for the economy and the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's next move in interest rates. Good morning, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FINAL JOBS REPORT OF 2023 DUE THIS MORNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAPS OFF A YEAR OF STRONG HIRING THAT DEFIED EXPECTATIONS\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. And this is the final jobs report for 2023, and it caps off a year of strong hiring that defied expectations. Analysts predict that 170,000 jobs were added to the workforce in December. If that proves true, the economy created a solid 2.7 million jobs last year, industries that hired the most workers include health care and hospitality.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now this morning's report is crucial for the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  as it considers cutting interest rates as soon as the spring. Stronger-than-expected job and wage growth could prompt the Fed to hold off on those rate cuts until later in the year. Not that of course matters if you are buying a car or a home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JOBS & INTEREST RATES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STRONG NUMBERS COULD DELAY THE FEDERAL RESERVE'S EXPECTED RATE CUTS\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) New data shows that the average rate on a 30-year fixed mortgage just ticked up slightly to 6.2%. So what does that mean in real terms? If you are taking out a $400,000 mortgage, your monthly payment right now is about $2,500. So that's less than last fall, but it is still higher than a year ago. Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240120ek1500008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW LAWS FOR THE NEW YEAR CHANGE TO GUNS, MINIMUM WAGE & INCLUSION PROGRAMS\b0\par\par\uc2 594 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 January 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TERROR THREAT, CAR CRASH, SHALVOY, EVANS\par \par \uc2 PLANE, CRASH, JAPAN, EARTHQUAKE, SEARCH, RESCUE, JONES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIERY COLLISION ON TOKYO RUNWAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIREFIGHTERS BATTLE FLAMES ON PLANE WITH 400 PASSENGERS ABOARD\par \par \uc2 IMMIGRATION, JOHNSTON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CRISIS AT THE BORDER SPREADS TO CITIES ACROSS THE COUNTRY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAYORS DEMANDING ACTION AS TEXAS SENDS MIGRANTS NORTH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RISING TENSIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IRAN REPORTEDLY DEPLOYING WARSHIP AFTER U.S. STRIKE ON HOUTHI REBELS\par \par \uc2 2024 ELECTION, PRIMARY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TWO WEEKS UNTIL THE IOWA REPUBLICAN CAUCUSES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CANDIDATES MAKING FINAL PITCHES TO VOTERS\par \par \uc2 POWERBALL, JACKPOT, LOTTERY, MICHIGAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JACKPOT!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: $842 MILLION TICKET SOLD IN MICHIGAN\par \par \uc2 COLLEGE FOOTBALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COLLEGE FOOTBALL NATIONAL CHAMPIONSHIP GAME SET\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MICHIGAN TO FACE WASHINGTON FOR THE TITLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 ZIERING, BRAWL\par \par \uc2 SHARK, ATTACK, CARTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY HAWAII SHARK ATTACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 39-YEAR-OLD SURFER KILLED IN ENCOUNTER IN HAWAII\par \par \uc2 TEPPER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAROLINA PANTHERS OWNER IN HOT WATER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BILLIONAIRE DAVID TEPPER APPEARS TO TOSS DRINK ONTO OPPOSING FANS\par \par \uc2 RENNER\par \par \uc2 COMET THE DOG, EHRICHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, JEAN-PIERRE, POLITICS, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IRAN NOW SENDS A WARSHIP TO THE RED SEA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY ON THE MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 LAWS, 2024, GUNS, MINIMUM WAGE, INCLUSION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW LAWS FOR THE NEW YEAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHANGE TO GUNS, MINIMUM WAGE & INCLUSION PROGRAMS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, all right, thank you so much, George. Now to the new state law that took effect when the calendar turned to 2024, from guns to minimum wage to inclusion programs. Chief White House correspondent Mary Bruce is here now to tell us all about them. Good morning, Mary.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Michael. Well, with the new year comes a new slate of state laws across the country that are having an immediate impact on Americans' lives. So, first up, gun reforms. You know, despite a historic number of mass shootings last year, Congress remains deadlocked on this issue, so states are now taking action instead.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERAL STATES ENACT WEAPON BANS\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) California now taking the biggest step, barring guns in most public places, including libraries, public parks, churches and sports venues, while Illinois is also banning high-powered semiautomatic rifles and high-capacity magazines. And Colorado is getting rid of those ghost guns, those do-it-yourself, homemade guns.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MANY STATES RAISE MINIMUM WAGE\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next, the federal minimum wage. It hasn't actually been raised in nearly 15 years now, still stuck at $7.25 an hour. But once again, we are seeing states taking matters into their own hands. Twenty-two states are raising their minimum wage. Many workers, that means, will now be making $15 an hour or more. Now, we know the states have also been the battleground for divisive social issues.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW RULES ON SOCIAL ISSUES IN SOME STATES\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In Louisiana and West Virginia, new restrictions on gender transition care for younger people are in place. And in Texas, they have now banned offices and programs that promote diversity, equity and inclusion at publicly funded colleges and universities. Conservative lawmakers there arguing that those programs stoke racial divisions or push liberal agendas on campuses. Lots of changes across the country, Eva.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Mary Bruce, so nice to have you here in studio in New York with us today.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240112ek120000j\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MINIMUM WAGE HIKES FOR THE NEW YEAR WORKERS IN 22 STATES SEE PAY RAISES AT START OF 2024\b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ROGUE WAVE\par \par \uc2 STORM, WAVE, SWELLS, INJURIES, PACIFIC\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, AIRLINES, ROADS, TSA, TRAFFIC\par \par \uc2 STORM, WEST COAST, RAIN, EAST COAST, TEMPS\par \par \uc2 SECURITY, TIMES SQUARE, NYE, HART, ADAMS, \uc2 FBI\uc2 , \uc2 NYPD\par \par \uc2 MAINE, TRUMP, BALLOT, BELLOWS, HALEY, CIVIL WAR\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, ATTACKS, MISSILES, DRONES, DEAD, INJURED\par \par \uc2 MINIMUM WAGE, HIKES, STATES, WORKERS\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A reminder that war is far from over. Marcus Moore for us there in London. Thank you, Marcus. Well now to millions of workers getting a pay raise in the new year. Minimum wage workers in 22 states are in for a pay bump to kick off 2024. Morgan Norwood is here with the details. Good morning, Morgan.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MINIMUM WAGE HIKES FOR THE NEW YEAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORKERS IN 22 STATES TO SEE PAY RAISES AT START OF 2024\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Eva. While our economy defied odds, despite rising inflation and cost of living increases, those who, of course, have lived on minimum wage, have had a much harder time paying rent, buying groceries, the essentials there. Campaigns like fight for 15 have been advocating for higher minimum wage for more than a decade.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And starting January of next year, close to 10 million workers across 22 states will have more money in their paychecks. And that's all thanks to a boost in minimum wage. Let's talk about this, more than half of those workers are in California, Hawaii, New York, all states where the cost of living is especially high.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The pay bump will be massive for Maryland, Hawaii, and Nebraska. Pay also going up for their minimum wage workers by at least $1.50, Hawaii $2. Despite this progress, though, there are still more than 17 million workers earning less than $15 an hour, and actually 20 states still use the federal minimum wage of $7.25.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But there is good news for millions more workers. Three more states plus DC are due to raise their minimum wage later on in the year. Guys.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240111ejct00008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PORTLAND TEACHERS' STRIKE ENDS UNION & DISTRICT REACH TENTATIVE DEAL AFTER THREE-WEEK WALKOUT\b0\par\par\uc2 401 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLDING ON\par \par \uc2 CEASE FIRE, HOSTAGES, FREED, BIDEN, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 MISSILES, \uc2 US NAVY\uc2 , VESSEL, TENSIONS, HIJACKING\par \par \uc2 KIRBY, CEASE FIRE, HOSTAGES, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , EXTENSION\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, PALESTINIAN, ARREST, STUDENTS, INJURED, HATE CRIME\par \par \uc2 STORM, TRAVEL, AIRPORTS, DISRUPTION\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, WIND CHILL, TEMPERATURES\par \par \uc2 SANTOS, HOUSE, EXPULSION, VOTE, ETHICS\par \par \uc2 CARTER, CELEBRATING, LEGACY, PUBLIC, CEREMONIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FROSTY WEST COAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "FROZEN"\par \par \uc2 SCOBIE, "ENDGAME", HARRY, WILLIAM, RACISM, KING CHARLES\par \par \uc2 CRUISE, THREE YEARS, SHAY, CANCELED, WHITMAN, UGURLU, KOSCIOLEK\par \par \uc2 SHOPPING, ONLINE, DEALS, TECH, BEAUTY, CLOTHING, FINKELSTEIN, WARD\par \par \uc2 NFL\uc2 , EAGLES, HURTS, BILLS, VIKINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, MOR, HAND, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8\par \par \uc2 TEACHER'S STRIKE, DEAL\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to a tentative deal back here to end Portland's first-ever teachers strike that led to 11 days of cancelled classes. Stephanie Ramos joins us with more. Good morning, Stephanie.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PORTLAND TEACHERS' STRIKE ENDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNION & DISTRICT REACH TENTATIVE DEAL AFTER THREE-WEEK WALKOUT\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Juju, good morning. This morning, nearly 45,000 students in Oregon's largest school district are heading back to school. A tentative contract deal has been reached between the teachers' union and Portland school district, ending the three-week strike.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROPOSED DEAL WITH PORTLAND SCHOOL TEACHERS\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The new contract is worth $175 million over the next three years and includes a nearly 14% cost of living increase for teachers, improve class sizes, more built-in lesson planning time and teaching time, an expedited teacher hiring process and $20 million to correct building and maintenance issues prioritized by the teachers. Portland is just one of the districts where teachers went on strike this year but one of the largest in recent years with thousands more in California threatening to walk off of the job. And while this deal is good news, it's not a done deal yet.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The teachers' union still needs to vote on the contract and the school board needs to sign off. But schools are expected to open up this morning and teachers and students will be able to make up the days missed during the strikes. Linsey?\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, headed back to the classroom. Stephanie, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231221ejbr0008u\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2  "RED CUP REBELLION" BARISTAS SET TO STRIKE TODAY BETTER WAGES & BENEFITS\b0\par\par\uc2 584 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PROTEST, WAR, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL, SHERMAN\par \par \uc2 CONRICUS, SHEFLER, NEGOTIATIONS, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 DRONE ATTACK, YEMEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. WARSHIP SHOOTS DOWN DRONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFICIALS SAY THE YEMEN-LAUNCHED CRAFT WAS HEADED TOWARD NAVY SHIP\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, CHINA, XI, SUMMIT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH-STAKES SUMMIT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN MEETS WITH CHINSE LEADER XI IN SAN FRANCISCO\par \par \uc2 SUMMIT, KIRBY, CHINA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN ON THE WORLD STAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOP WHITE HOUSE OFFICIAL ON HIGH-STAKES MEETING WITH CHINA'S LEADER\par \par \uc2 AIR TRAVEL, STAFF SHORTAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THANKSGIVING TRAVEL ALERT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW REPORT SOUNDS THE ALARM ON AIR TRAFFIC CONTROLLER SHORTAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HEUERMANN, ELLERUP, TIERNEY, BROWN, MITEV, TRIAL\par \par \uc2 FERRY ACCIDENT, SCHISSEL, SKIPPINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INVESTIGATION INTO BAHAMAS FERRY ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICAN WOMAN DIES AFTER BOAT SINKS IN ROUGH WATER\par \par \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , PROTEST, "REP CUP REBELLION", BAIER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2  "RED CUP REBELLION"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BARISTAS SET TO STRIKE TODAY BETTER WAGES & BENEFITS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now the latest on the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers heading to the picket line this morning. Rebecca Jarvis has more on the red cup rebellion.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  baristas around the country are seeing red.\par \par \uc2 DAISY FEDERSPIEL-BAIER (BARISTA / SHIFT SUPERVISOR SEATTLE)\par \par \uc2 Take away the profits for the company to put pressure on them.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Planning a strike on one of the company's biggest days of the year. Employees say they're not equipped to handle the huge crowds expected during today's annual red cup promotion when the company hands out reusable cups with the purchase of a holiday drink. One supervisor in Seattle told us, in the past, these kinds of promotional days have brought up to 220 transactions every half hour. A 40% boost in business.\par \par \uc2 DAISY FEDERSPIEL-BAIER (BARISTA / SHIFT SUPERVISOR SEATTLE)\par \par \uc2 They told us they try to stock the floor as much as possible, but baristas were incredibly stress. Our mental health is declining and we even sustained some physical injuries, which was not good.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The union is demanding a new contract with better pay, staffing and more local control, including the right to turn off mobile orders. In response, \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  says the workers union hasn't agreed to meet for contract bargaining in more than four months and says, "We, again, call on Workers United to fulfill their obligations and engage in the work of negotiating."\par \par \uc2 DAISY FEDERSPIEL-BAIER (BARISTA / SHIFT SUPERVISOR SEATTLE)\par \par \uc2 I really wish that I could be in there serving you coffee. I do. Unfortunately, we have to push for better, and we aren't getting that from \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  right now.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  tells us it creates store schedules three weeks in advance based on employee availability and provides additional staffing on promotional days. Of the thousands of stores across the country, the company says there are 30 on strike. And, guys, I can tell you, there are a lot of workers working hard at this \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  in New York City behind me.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They always do. They always do. Rebecca, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 7:42, TO RECLINE OR NOT TO RECLINE?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up next, the holiday travel season already expected to be a record breaker, which means full flights. Gio is going to be back with one of the biggest questions for travelers, to recline or not to recline? That is the question.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231214ejbg0000c\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2  WORKER WALKOUT? UNION CALLING FOR "RED CUP REBELLION" THURSDAY\b0\par\par\uc2 369 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL RAIDS GAZA HOSPITAL\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, GAZA, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , AL-SHIFA, SINGH, PROTESTS, CIVILIANS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, XI, SUMMIT, TENSIONS, RELATIONS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, XI, SUMMIT, TRUST\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, BILL, DEMOCRATS, GOP, SENATE, TENSIONS\par \par \uc2 VOLCANO, ERUPTION, ICELAND, EVACUATIONS\par \par \uc2 CRASH, BUS, SEMI, CHAIN REACTION, DEAD, BOSLER\par \par \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , WORKERS, WALKOUT, UNION, RED CUP\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Unfortunate tragedy there, Alex, thank you very much. We're going to turn now to thousands of \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers who are set to strike at hundreds of stores across the country. Whit Johnson is at the Times Square location with more on what's being called the red cup rebellion. Good morning, Whit.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2  WORKER WALKOUT?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNION CALLING FOR "RED CUP REBELLION" THURSDAY\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Michael, good morning to you. It's expected to be the biggest strike ever for unionized \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  baristas. That red cup rebellion is you mentioned, is planned tomorrow on red cup day, a massively popular promotional event when \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  gives out those holiday themed reusable cups. Typically one of the most profitable days of the year for the company.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thousands of unionized workers from hundreds of locations across the country are set to walk off the job. They're accusing \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  of refusing to bargain over staffing and other issues at a time when the company announced record sales. The union representing the baristas is demanding \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  turn off mobile ordering on future promotion days, saying the influx of customers without additional staffing creates unnecessarily stressful working conditions.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  releasing a statement saying, "We are aware that Workers United has publicized a day of action at a small subset of our US stores this week. We remain committed to working with all partners." And alleging that "Workers United hasn't agreed to meet to progress contract bargaining in more than four months."\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So both sides blaming each other. And this, of course, comes on what has been a record year for organized labor, from the auto industry to actors and writers in Hollywood, workers across the country demanding change. Robin.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231214ejbf00030\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  BOARD VOTES ON TENTATIVE AGREEMENT WHAT'S IN THE DEAL THAT ENDED THE 118-DAY WALKOUT\b0\par\par\uc2 726 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL-\uc2 HAMAS\uc2  WAR: CRITICAL CONDITION\par \par \uc2 GAZA, HOSPITALS, ATTACKS\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, DIPLOMATS, WARNING, IMAGE, XI\par \par \uc2 ADAMS, \uc2 FBI\uc2 , SEARCH, SEIZURE, PHONE, IPAD, FUNDRAISING\par \par \uc2 U.S., CREDIT RATING, MOODY'S, NEGATIVE, DOWNGRADES\par \par \uc2 MCSALLY, ATTACK, INVESTIGATION, HENTON\par \par \uc2 HARBOUGH, BANNED, LAWSUIT, MICHIGAN, WALTERS, THAMEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MICHIGAN TAKES LEGAL ACTION AFTER BIG TEN SIDELINES COACH: UNIVERSITY FILES FOR TEMPORARY RESTRAINING ORDER FOR HARBAUGH SUSPENSION\par \par \uc2 LUDWIG, SHOOTING, STRAY BULLET, TAYLOR, FRESHMAN\par \par \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 , \uc2 AMPTP\uc2 , DRESCHER, CRABTREE-IRELAND, SALLOUM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  BOARD VOTES ON TENTATIVE AGREEMENT: WHAT'S IN THE DEAL THAT ENDED THE 118-DAY WALKOUT\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's go to Hollywood now, ready for lights, camera, action, of course, because the \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  board members voting in favor of a tentative contract with the major studios following that 118-day strike. Now it goes to a vote by union members. ABC's Jaclyn Lee joins us now from Los Angeles with the new details about what's in the deal. Jaclyn, good morning.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Whit, good morning. The \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  national board voted to approve the agreement with \uc2 AMPTP\uc2  with an 86% yes vote after the actors' longest strike in the union history. It's a welcome relief for those working in the industry.\par \par \uc2 RYAN REYNOLDS ("DEADPOOL 2")\par \par \uc2 Leonard, hit it.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Hollywood is back and open for business. On Friday, the \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  board approved the monumental three-year contract deal with Hollywood studios.\par \par \uc2 FRAN DRESCHER (PRESIDENT OF \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 We began this journey, the largest entertainment union in the world and we finish it the most powerful.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  CONTRACT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VALUED AT MORE THAN $1 BILLION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ADDITIONAL COMPENSATION FOR STREAMING SHOWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MINIMUM WAGE INCREASE TOTALING 11%\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AI PROTECTIONS: ACTORS WILL BE PAID FOR ANY DIGITAL REPLICA OF THEIR WORK\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) So, what's in the deal? Valued at more than one billion dollars, additional compensation for successful streaming shows and a minimum wage increase totaling 11% within a year. And, protection surrounding artificial intelligence. Actors will now be informed and paid if studios make any digital replica of their work.\par \par \uc2 DUNCAN CRABTREE-IRELAND (CHIEF NEGOTIATOR \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Our members remain actively involved in the movement to protect all individuals' rights to their likeness.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP: STRANGER THINGS"\par \par \uc2 PAUL REISER ("STRANGER THINGS")\par \par \uc2 Without you, we can't win this war.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) About two dozen TV shows going back to production right after Thanksgiving...\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP: ABBOTT ELEMENTARY\par \par \uc2 QUINTA BRUNSON ("ABBOTT ELEMENTARY")\par \par \uc2 I will be having a third talk with your mom about what you're watching at home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLLYWOOD GETS BACK TO BUSINESS: WHEN YOUR FAVORITE SHOWS & NEW MOVIES RETURN\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...like "Abbott Elementary" and "Grey's Anatomy." Movie sequels like Ridley Scott's highly anticipated "Gladiator 2," starring Denzel Washington, shut down midway through the strike, now set to be released in November 2024.\par \par \uc2 RYAN REYNOLDS ("DEADPOOL 2")\par \par \uc2 Hey, Hugh, you want to play Wolverine one more time?\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And don't worry Marvel fans, "Deadpool 3," starring Ryan Reynolds, promises to hit the box office next July. Actors saying this deal was all the motivation they needed.\par \par \uc2 ANDREA SALLOUM (SAG-AFTRA MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 The idea to make actors crawl their whole life doesn't work anymore. It's time that we are respected and paid. Then, we do a really great job on TV.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And as for what's next the more than 160,000 \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  members have to vote to ratify the agreement and of course, there will be information sessions throughout the coming weeks to share more details about that agreement. Guys?\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Jaclyn, thank you so much. Glad there's a resolve there.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up, what's ahead in Washington as the divided Congress faces another possible government shutdown.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP: FACING A SHUTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP: INTO THE BURN ZONE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And "GMA" heading into Maui's burn zone with the \uc2 Army Corps of Engineers\uc2 . Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORY SYNOPSES\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231212ejbb00032\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HOLLYWOOD ACTORS STRIKE ENDS \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  REACHES TENTATIVE DEAL WITH STUDIOS TO END 118-DAY WALKOUT\b0\par\par\uc2 488 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 DESANTIS, RAMASWAMY, HALEY, SCOTT, CHRISTIE, DEBATE\par \par \uc2 AIRSTRIKE, SYRIA, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. LAUNCHES STRIKES AGAINST IRAN-BACKED FORCES IN SYRIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RETALIATION FOR SERIES OF ATTACKS ON U.S. FORCES IN MIDEAST\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, NEGOTIATIONS, NAIM, NETANYAHU, POLIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT HOSTAGE NEGOTIATIONS AS FIERCE FIGHTING RAGES IN GAZA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORTS: TALKS ONGOING TO POTENTIALLY RELEASE SOME CIVILIANS HELD BY \uc2 HAMAS\par \par \uc2 WAR, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUMANITARIAN CRISIS GROWING IN GAZA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INSIDE AN ISRAELI CHECKPOINT INSPECTING AID HEADED TO STRIP\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, KIRBY, HOSTAGES\par \par \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 , DEALS, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLLYWOOD ACTORS STRIKE ENDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  REACHES TENTATIVE DEAL WITH STUDIOS TO END 118-DAY WALKOUT\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, the breaking news overnight after 118 days, an end to the Hollywood strike. \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  reached a tentative deal with the studios. Jamie Lee Curtis posting in celebration writing, "Perseverance pays off." Whit Johnson is in Times Square, has those details for us. Good morning, Whit.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Robin, good morning to you. Hollywood is back in business now. Overnight, \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  sent an email to its members saying, our strike is officially suspended.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENTATIVE AGREEMENT WORTH $1 BILLION+\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 's negotiating committee unanimously approving the historic three-year contract. It says it's worth more than $1 billion. The deal establishes participation bonuses for streaming, a salary hike that reportedly includes most minimum wages to increase by 7%. That's 2% more than those received by the writers and director's guild, and the first ever protections for actors against artificial intelligence, a major sticking point for the union. \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  president and star of "The Nanny" Fran Drescher celebrating on \uc2 Instagram\uc2  saying, "New ground was broke everywhere." The studio alliance group saying in statement, it looks forward to the industry resuming the work of telling great stories.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, we won't know full details until the tentative agreement is reviewed by the \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  national board on Friday. Guys?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whit, thanks very much.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IVANKA TRUMP TAKES THE STAND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT'S DAUGHTER QUESTIONED IN NY CIVIL FRAUD TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up, \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  takes the stand in the civil fraud trial that threatens the family's business.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WEIGHT LOSS GAME CHANGER?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FDA\uc2  APPROVES NEW OBESITY DRUG FROM \uc2 ELI LILLY\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Plus, the new weight loss drug just approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2 . But why it could be a game changer. And Dr. Ashton is here with those details.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTRY MUSIC'S BIGGEST NIGHT!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIG WINNER & BUZZIEST MOMENTS FROM THE CMA AWARDS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And we have the biggest winners, the amazing performances, and Lara's backstage interviews from the CMA Awards.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231211ejb900007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BREAKING NEWS ACTORS UNION REACHED TENTATIVE DEAL WITH STUDIOS\b0\par\par\uc2 112 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 , DEAL, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good evening. Thank you for joining us. We have breaking news tonight. \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  has reached a tentative deal with the major film and TV studios, which would bring to an end the longest actors strike in Hollywood history.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The package is said to include a bump-up in residual payments and minimums, and sets rules for the use of AI technology, which has been a major sticking point in negotiations. The deal is expected to be ratified in enough time to salvage the current television season.\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020231110ejb800002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ONE YEAR OUT YOUR VOICE, YOUR VOTE 2024\b0\par\par\uc2 1,700 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, WORKERS, PROTESTS, LAROCK, CROCAMO, BUGLIO, COOK, NORDEN\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's Election Day in America. Polls have closed, and ABC News projects that Democrats can count wins in two key races, an abortion rights measure in Ohio, and the Governor's race in Kentucky. But some of those in charge of ensuring our votes get cast and counted say they fear for their lives in an increasingly divisive political climate. Part of our series "Your Voice, Your Vote: One Year Out".\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE YEAR OUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUR VOICE, YOUR VOTE 2024\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM ABC NEWS COVERAGE, 2020\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 A city is suppressed with the population.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Stop the steal! Stop the steal!\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Stop the count!\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Election workers under threat.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, an open carry state, a judge ruling guns are allowed at polling places.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The keepers of our democracy facing harassment...\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM GOOD MORNING AMERICA, 2022\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Election officials are warning right now of urgent security concerns.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...some getting death threats, all for just doing their jobs. Across the country, this largely mundane role has now become a sometimes dangerous one. Some having to go to great lengths, like wearing bullet-proof vests, to keep themselves safe...\par \par \uc2 ELECTION WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I wear one pretty much every single day.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...and investing millions in plexiglass, security cameras, and other safety measures.\par \par \uc2 SUE LAROCK (JUDGE OF ELECTION/LUZERNE COUNTY PA)\par \par \uc2 People are very distrustful. People are almost mean. We get a lot of accusations hurled at us.\par \par \uc2 ROMILDA CROCAMO (LUZERNE COUNTY MANAGER PA)\par \par \uc2 We are preparing for the worst possible scenario.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Romilda Crocamo is the County Manager in Luzerne County, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 ROMILDA CROCAMO (LUZERNE COUNTY MANAGER PA)\par \par \uc2 If we have an event at a polling location, we have a plan for them to, to be able to go to a different site and vote. We've worked with the District Attorney, our sheriff's department, our county detectives, our emergency management, 911. We're all ready in case something happens.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) What's happening in the swing county of over 300,00 people is also playing out across America. The high-alert environment could be a sign of things to come in 2024.\par \par \uc2 LAWRENCE NORDEN (SR DIR/ELECTIONS & GOVT/BRENNAN CENTER FOR JUSTICE)\par \par \uc2 I'd say elections were under siege in 2020, and I have high concern about 2024.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It could happen again?\par \par \uc2 LAWRENCE NORDEN (SR DIR/ELECTIONS & GOVT/BRENNAN CENTER FOR JUSTICE)\par \par \uc2 It could happen again.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In Luzerne County, today is their test run.\par \par \uc2 LOGAN BUGLIO (JUDGE OF ELECTION/LUZERNE COUNTY PA)\par \par \uc2 So it's just about 5:30 here in the morning, Luzerne County, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And Logan Buglio is already hitting the ground running.\par \par \uc2 LOGAN BUGLIO (JUDGE OF ELECTION/LUZERNE COUNTY PA)\par \par \uc2 I recruited my two sisters. So, we're just about ready to leave the house, go over to a polling place, set up, and be ready for seven o'clock when the voters come.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) He's one of hundreds of thousands of election workers across the country getting ready for an almost 20-hour day so that voters can cast their ballots today.\par \par \uc2 ELECTION WORKER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 As an officer of election...\par \par \uc2 ELECTION WORKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 As an officer of election...\par \par \uc2 LOGAN BUGLIO (JUDGE OF ELECTION/LUZERNE COUNTY PA)\par \par \uc2 That's a commitment that needs to be made, to keep elections on this the right track and, and allow your neighbors to come in and vote.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Luzerne is still reeling from the last presidential election.\par \par \uc2 EMILY COOK (DEPUTY DIRECTOR OF ELECTIONS/LUZERNE COUNTY PA)\par \par \uc2 It has been a very chaotic several years. It's just been one crazy moment after the next.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Emily Cook is the county's deputy director of elections. At just 26 years old, she's among the most senior members of her department.\par \par \uc2 EMILY COOK (DEPUTY DIRECTOR OF ELECTIONS/LUZERNE COUNTY PA)\par \par \uc2 We do have a, a frequently revolving door within the Elections Office. It's pretty reflective of what election offices across the country are looking like post-2020. A lot of that is due to the climate that we're in now in relation to elections, which I can tell you firsthand is hostile.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Last year during the midterm elections when Cook was on the job for just two months, polling locations in the county were running low on paper ballots. The shortage corrected later that day. Turned out to be an administrative oversight by a new team, but conspiracy theories spread like wildfire.\par \par \uc2 EMILY COOK (DEPUTY DIRECTOR OF ELECTIONS/LUZERNE COUNTY PA)\par \par \uc2 I did start receiving death threats. Sitting in a room with detectives and the sheriff and being told there, there are people that want you to die, there are people that are saying you should be drawn and quartered.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Emily says the experience has left her forever changed.\par \par \uc2 EMILY COOK (DEPUTY DIRECTOR OF ELECTIONS/LUZERNE COUNTY PA)\par \par \uc2 I'm a lot more hesitant to go really anywhere by myself. Just because you, you don't know who's out there. What keeps me up at night is not knowing if somebody's threatening me, and then go and do something to members of my family, that is definitely one of the things that, that is part of my recurring nightmares relating to this job.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) According to a survey by the Brennan Center for Justice, nearly three in four election officials feel that threats against them have gone up in recent years. And 30 percent say they have personally been abused, harassed, or threatened because of their job.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What changed in America that that became fashionable to attack election workers?\par \par \uc2 LAWRENCE NORDEN (SR DIR/ELECTIONS & GOVT/BRENNAN CENTER FOR JUSTICE)\par \par \uc2 We have leaders falsely saying the system is rigged. They're promoting claims that are untrue about the way the system works.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When I hear you say leaders, I hear you say \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Is that who you're referring to?\par \par \uc2 LAWRENCE NORDEN (SR DIR/ELECTIONS & GOVT/BRENNAN CENTER FOR JUSTICE)\par \par \uc2 There's no question \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is part of this. And I do have concerns that we're, we're going into a season where he is on trial, so all of the stuff that we've heard about, about what happened in 2020, is gonna be brought up again. He's not acting alone. And, and if he was the only one who was saying this, I don't think it would get the same traction that it's gotten.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The harassment so pervasive, the Department of Justice launched a task force to look into the threats in 2021, so far resulting in nine convictions. Back in Luzerne, Romilda Crocamo says she won't allow anything to happen on her watch.\par \par \uc2 ROMILDA CROCAMO (LUZERNE COUNTY MANAGER PA)\par \par \uc2 No one is going to be able to abuse our election workers. They're our neighbors. They're the people who sit next to you in church. They're the ones who are at your little league games. And I am not gonna let anyone do anything to put them in harm's way.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM 2020\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 USA! USA!\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Despite this heightened threat environment, experts say there is a silver lining.\par \par \uc2 LAWRENCE NORDEN (SR DIR/ELECTIONS & GOVT/BRENNAN CENTER FOR JUSTICE)\par \par \uc2 We're better prepared than we were in 2020. Over the past few years, there's been an infrastructure that has been built. There are, there's something called the Committee for Safe and Secure Elections, which is a cooperation committee between law enforcement and election officials.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A number of people across the country have lost faith in our election process. What can you say here, now, to reassure them that our process, while not perfect, is still functional?\par \par \uc2 LAWRENCE NORDEN (SR DIR/ELECTIONS & GOVT/BRENNAN CENTER FOR JUSTICE)\par \par \uc2 The thing that people aren't aware of in our system is how many checks there are along the way. You have Republicans and Democrats not only present when people are voting, but present in the counting, present when their, the ballots are being ordered, when we're checking over the ballots to make sure that it's designed correctly, checking signatures. All of that is done in a bipartisan way in this country.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) While many election workers have left since 2020, some are still hopeful for our democracy.\par \par \uc2 LAWRENCE NORDEN (SR DIR/ELECTIONS & GOVT/BRENNAN CENTER FOR JUSTICE)\par \par \uc2 One of the things that's been very inspiring to me is, people have come up and they've taken the place of these election officials who have left. We've seen hundreds of new people joining to, to, to learn their jobs, to learn about being good election officials. They're committed to ensuring that their communities have free and fair elections.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And like Emily, many have risen to the challenge.\par \par \uc2 EMILY COOK (DEPUTY DIRECTOR OF ELECTIONS/LUZERNE COUNTY PA)\par \par \uc2 I was born and raised here in Luzerne County. This is where I first registered to vote. I've lived here my whole life. And so, that's part of what keeps me here, wanting to help right the ship, making sure that, that things do get better. Being part of the election process is what I always wanted to do.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEXT ON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MEGAN FOX\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 When we come back, actress Megan Fox's dark secrets revealed in a new book of poems. Why she says she had to write it.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020231109ejb700002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PORTLAND TEACHERS ON STRIKE ROUGHLY 45,000 STUDENTS OUT OF SCHOOL AS LABOR DISPUTE ENTERS SECOND WEEK\b0\par\par\uc2 415 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP TAKES THE STAND\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, TRIAL, FRAUD, TESTIFY, JAMES, NAWADAY\par \par \uc2 POLL, BIDEN, TRUMP, ELECTION, REPUBLICANS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, ELECTION, BATTLEGROUND, TRUMP, POLLS\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, GAZA, \uc2 IDF\uc2 , \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , CIVILIANS, HUMANITARIAN\par \par \uc2 BLINKEN, MIDDLE EAST, TENSIONS, ISRAEL, GAZA\par \par \uc2 HAMLIN, CINCINNATI, FOUNDATION, SCHOLARSHIPS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEMPERATURE WHIPLASH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, MURDER, ARMSTRONG, WILSON, JONES, STRICKLAND, TESTIMONY\par \par \uc2 MICHIGAN, CHEATING, FOOTBALL, STALIONS, SCANDAL, THAMEL\par \par \uc2 MANI, AI, NUDE IMAGES, HIGH SCHOOL, FRANKS\par \par \uc2 NYC MARATHON, RELAY, ABC NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLOOD THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, TRIAL, CIVIL FRAUD\par \par \uc2 TEACHERS, STRIKES, \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But now to the teachers strike in Portland, Oregon. About 45,000 students are out of school this morning as the strike enters a second week. And in Las Vegas, hotel chains are bracing for a possible walkout this week. Kayna Whitworth has that story for us. Good morning, Kayna.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PORTLAND TEACHERS ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ROUGHLY 45,000 STUDENTS OUT OF SCHOOL AS LABOR DISPUTE ENTERS SECOND WEEK\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, Robin, good morning. So, all across the west, tens of thousands of workers are voicing demand for better pay and better working conditions starting with teachers there in Portland, Oregon, that are taking to the picket lines again today.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) They're asking for a 20% pay increase. They want smaller class sizes and more planning time, among other things. This as Las Vegas is bracing for what could be the largest hospitality workers strike in US history, as more than 35,000 members of the culinary union are set to strike Friday if a resolution isn't met.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WALKOUT ON THE LAS VEGAS STRIP?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABOUT 35,000 MEMBERS OF CULINARY WORKERS UNION PREPARE TO STRIKE FRIDAY\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And if that happens, it would be just days before the long-anticipated Las Vegas Grand Prix.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON THE SAG-AFTRA STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACTORS' UNION REVIEWING STUDIOS' "LAST, BEST AND FINAL OFFER"\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And then here in Los Angeles, the actors union is reviewing what studios have called their last best and final offer to end the strike that has lasted here more than 100 days.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Linsey, as you know, that is certainly a critical moment in those negotiations.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Certainly is. Kayna, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231206ejb60000h\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 LATEST JOBS NUMBERS SHOW GROWTH SLOWING 150,000 JOBS ADDED IN OCTOBER, UNEMPLOYMENT RATE RISES 3.9%\b0\par\par\uc2 1,015 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL DISMISSES HUMANITARIAN PAUSE\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, PAUSES, GAZA, DRONES, HOSTAGES, BLINKEN, NETANYAHU, JORDAN\par \par \uc2 NUCLEAR PLANT, SECURITY, WHISENHUNT, CRENSHAW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, MAINE, VICTIMS, SHOOTINGS, CARD, GUN, LAWS, SCHEMENGEES, TEXTS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, CIVIL, FRAUD, TRIAL, TESTIMONY\par \par \uc2 NURSING HOME, DEATHS, PRESSDEE, INSULIN, HENRY, BOWER, PEIRCE\par \par \uc2 PORTLAND, TEACHERS, STRIKE, PAY, STUDENTS\par \par \uc2 JOBS, REPORT, WAGES, WALL STREET, STOCKS, INTEREST, RATES, MORTGAGE\par \par \uc2 FORECAST, COLD, TEMPERATURE, HIGHS\par \par \uc2 SIMS, OHIO STATE, \uc2 PENN STATE\uc2 , "COLLEGE GAMEDAY"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM PERFORMANCE BY MISSY ELLIOTT\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, ABORTION, GUNS, BIDEN, TRUMP, TUBERVILLE, MILITARY\par \par \uc2 FORECAST, NORTHWEST, RAIN, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 ELLIOTT, HIP-HOP, ROCK & ROLL HALL OF FAME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM THE ROCK 'N' ROLL HALL OF FAME INDUCTION CEREMONY\par \par \uc2 STUART, TOLKMIT, DELTA, PILOTS, REUNION, \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 , PHOTO\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK CITY, MARATHON, RUNNERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 WAR, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL, NETANYAHU, BLINKEN\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY, JOBS, INTEREST RATES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LATEST JOBS NUMBERS SHOW GROWTH SLOWING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 150,000 JOBS ADDED IN OCTOBER, UNEMPLOYMENT RATE RISES 3.9%\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And turning now to the economy and a rally on Wall Street following the latest jobs report. But what could this mean for interest rates and your wallet? ABC's Alexis Christoforous joins us now with details on that. Hey, Alexis, good morning again.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Gio. It's being called a Goldilocks job report for the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 . An economy that's adding jobs, but not too many. Wages that are rising but not by too much.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OCTOBER JOBS REPORT\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The Labor Department saying, the US added a less than expected 150,000 jobs in October while the unemployment rate inched up to 3.9% and wage growth slowed. The economy also added about 100,000 fewer jobs in August and September than first thought.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The most jobs were added in health care, government, construction and leisure and hospitality, but manufacturing lost 35,000 jobs thanks to last month's striking auto workers.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WALL STREET REACTS TO UNEMPLOYMENT FIGURES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOW HAS ITS REST WEEK IN A YEAR, INVESTORS HOPE FED WILL SUSPEND RATE HIKES\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, Wall Street applauded this October jobs report, sending the Dow up more than 200 points yesterday to cap the best week for stocks in about a year. Investors are betting the soft job numbers will convince the Fed to stop raising interest rates.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDERAL RATE HIKES/INFLATION\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The Central Bank has hiked rates 11 times in the past year and a half to slow spending and tame inflation. And so far, it appears to be working. Inflation has gone from 9% more than a year ago to 3.7% today.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INTEREST RATES\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) At the same time, though, home buyers have seen mortgage rates more than double to around 8%. Credit card interest rates have climbed to a record of 21%. And this week, the Fed left interest rates unchanged for the second straight time as it waits for more proof that the economy is slowing. Economists say the October jobs report could be that proof. And some say the Fed's next move may be to cut interest rates, how about that, by the summer. Guys?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's get those numbers down.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Some people will be on board for that. Yes.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely. Alexis, thank you for that.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 3 MINUTES, HOW TO PREP FOR DAYLIGHT SAVING TIME\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up here on our "GMA Morning Menu," turning the clocks back. The change from Daylight Saving Time and what every parent needs to know to get the best rest possible.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 10 MINUTES, DEALS & STEALS: HOLIDAY HOSTING!\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Also ahead, it's time. Tory Johnson is here with "Deals & Steals" to help you entertain for the holidays.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 41 MINUTES, JANAI'S BABY SHOWER!\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And ooh, baby, baby. Right? How many times are we going to say that today? Janai's baby shower is still ahead. We're going all out getting ready for the newest member of our "GMA" family. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Can't wait.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BORN TO RUN, COMING UP\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back to "GMA." Coming up, born to run. Will Ganss is live from the New York City Marathon finish line with our "GMA" mascot. Oh.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I love that.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, my goodness. From group runs to what to wear during the race, Will, you really hit the ground running for this story. How is it out there? What is Ray doing?\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is a warmup that I never knew I needed. But if it's working for Ray, it's work in for me. Here's what I've learned. The best part of the marathon, in my opinion, is carb loading. This year, there's going to be 33,000-plus bagels ready to go for runners here at the New York City Marathon. And I think Ray and I are going to have just a couple dozen of them maybe ourselves? That's what this is for.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, my goodness. You guys are having too much fun. All right, Will and Ray, better get running back to the studio now. We will see you soon. But for now, we'll head over to Whit with our cover story.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's like doing the hula-hoop dance but without the hula-hoop itself. So, at least they're getting warmed up. That's good. Thank you, guys.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231205ejb40003b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 LATEST JOBS NUMBERS SHOW GROWTH SLOWING 150,000 JOBS ADDED IN OCTOBER, UNEMPLOYMENT RATE RISES TO 3.9%\b0\par\par\uc2 452 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL DISMISSES HUMANITARIAN PAUSE\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, PAUSES, GAZA, DRONES, HOSTAGES, BLINKEN, NETANYAHU, JORDAN\par \par \uc2 NUCLEAR PLANT, SECURITY, WHISENHUNT, CRENSHAW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, MAINE, VICTIMS, SHOOTINGS, CARD, GUN, LAWS, SCHEMENGEES, TEXTS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, CIVIL, FRAUD, TRIAL, TESTIMONY\par \par \uc2 NURSING HOME, DEATHS, PRESSDEE, INSULIN, HENRY, BOWER, PEIRCE\par \par \uc2 PORTLAND, TEACHERS, STRIKE, PAY, STUDENTS\par \par \uc2 JOBS, REPORT, WAGES, WALL STREET, STOCKS, INTEREST, RATES, MORTGAGE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Turning now to the economy and a rally on Wall Street following the latest jobs report. But what could this mean for interest rates and your wallet? ABC's Alexis Christoforous joins us now with more on what this means in the details. Alexis, good morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JOBS REPORT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LATEST JOBS NUMBERS SHOW GROWTH SLOWING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 150,000 JOBS ADDED IN OCTOBER, UNEMPLOYMENT RATE RISES TO 3.9%\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Whit. That hiring frenzy that we saw post-pandemic appears to be over. The Labor Department saying the US added a less than expected $150,000 jobs in October, while the unemployment rate ticked up to 3.9 percent and wage growth slowed. The economy also added about 100,000 fewer jobs in August and September than first thought.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WALL STREET REACTS TO EMPLOYMENT FIGURES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOW HAS ITS BEST WEEK IN A YEAR, INVESTORS HOP FED WILL SUSPEND RATE HIKES\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Wall Street applauded the October jobs report, sending the Dow up more than 200 points yesterday to cap the best week for stocks in about a year. Investors are betting that soft job number will convince the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  to stop raising interest rates.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDERAL RATE HIKES/INFLATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INTEREST RATES\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The Fed has hiked rates 11 times in the past year and a half, to slow spending and tame inflation. So far, it's working. Inflation has gone from more than 9 percent more than a year ago to 3.7 percent today. At the same time, home buyers have seen mortgage rates more than double to around 8 percent, while credit card interest rates have climbed to a record 21 percent.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This week, the Fed left interest rates unchanged for the second straight time as it waits for more proof that the economy is slowing. Economists say the October jobs report could be that proof.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And some say the Fed's next move may actually be to cut interest rates before June. Guys?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That would absolutely be some welcome news, Alexis. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231205ejb400030\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PORTLAND TEACHERS' STRIKE ENTERS DAY FOUR ABOUT 49,000 STUDENTS IMPACTED AS TEACHERS DEMAND BETTER PAY, SMALLER CLASS SIZES\b0\par\par\uc2 380 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL DISMISSES HUMANITARIAN PAUSE\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, PAUSES, GAZA, DRONES, HOSTAGES, BLINKEN, NETANYAHU, JORDAN\par \par \uc2 NUCLEAR PLANT, SECURITY, WHISENHUNT, CRENSHAW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, MAINE, VICTIMS, SHOOTINGS, CARD, GUN, LAWS, SCHEMENGEES, TEXTS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, CIVIL, FRAUD, TRIAL, TESTIMONY\par \par \uc2 NURSING HOME, DEATHS, PRESSDEE, INSULIN, HENRY, BOWER, PEIRCE\par \par \uc2 PORTLAND, TEACHERS, STRIKE, PAY, STUDENTS\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This morning, tens of thousands of students in Portland, Oregon, are waiting to see if they'll be back at school next week as a teacher strike there enters day four. ABC's Melissa Adan is here now with the latest on the impacts to those nearly 50 thousand students. Melissa, good morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PORTLAND TEACHERS' STRIKE ENTERS DAY FOUR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABOUT 49,000 STUDENTS IMPACTED AS TEACHERS DEMAND BETTER PAY, SMALLER CLASS SIZES\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Janai, good morning. So many kids, right? Public schools in Portland are now on break indefinitely. All 81 of Portland's public schools are closed and teachers are on an historic strike.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) All of this sending about 49,000 students home as they enter the fourth day of their strike. Now, the district and teachers coming to the bargaining table yesterday. After not reaching an agreement, both say they're willing to negotiate through the weekend. So, what are teachers looking for? Well, the Portland Association of Teachers are calling for higher wages, about a 20 percent pay increase, smaller class sizes and more planning time.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, those demands coming with a $220 million price tag for the district. And the district says they do not have the funds to meet the union's current demands because the state has not given them the budget. Well, the Governor telling the school district to work with the resources that they do have right now. But look, on the weekdays it's a scramble for families to just figure out where to send their kids.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And of course, Whit, all of this with a looming concern of what will happen come Monday. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Melissa Adan, thanks so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231205ejb40002z\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PORTLAND, OREGON TEACHERS ON STRIKE SCHOOLS CLOSED FOR 45,000 STUDENTS\b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 OKUMURA, BESEISO, ZIND, WAR, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL, EVACUATIONS, GAZA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, FREEZE ALERTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD-BREAKING COLD BLAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EARLY FREEZE FOR MILLIONS FROM DEEP SOUTH TO NORTHEAST\par \par \uc2 SANTOS, EXPULSION, LAWLER, TUBERVILLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GEORGE SANTOS SURVIVES HOUSE EXPULSION VOTE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MEASURE TO KICK OUT EMBATTLED CONGRESSMAN FAILS TO WIN TWO-THIRDS MAJORITY\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, CIVIL FRAUD, TRIAL\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, WAGE, TEACHERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PORTLAND, OREGON TEACHERS ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SCHOOLS CLOSED FOR 45,000 STUDENTS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to the latest strike to hit our country. Excuse me. Teachers in Portland, Oregon walking off the job, 45,000 students will be home again from school this morning. And Faith Abubey joins us with more. Good morning, Faith.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Rebecca. This is the first time in Portland's history that educators in the state's largest school districts are on strike, forcing about 45,000 students to stay home for a second day without classroom instructions. Just in the last day, nearly 4,000 teachers have walked off the job.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Portland Association of Teachers is demanding, among other things, better pay and smaller class sizes. But district officials say they don't have the funds to meet the union's current demands. And now, thousands of families across the state are scrambling to adjust their day-to-day schedules, worried about their kid missing more class time, especially on the heels of the COVID pandemic.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The school board is putting pressure on the state legislature to find a solution here. The union and the district will be back at the bargaining table tomorrow. Robin?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hopefully, a solution can be found quickly. All right, Faith, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231204ejb200006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 UAW\uc2  ESCALATES STRIKE AGAINST \uc2 GENERAL MOTORS\uc2  MORE WORKERS WALK OFF JOB AFTER FORD & \uc2 STELLANTIS\uc2  DEALS\b0\par\par\uc2 551 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHAOS AT THE AIRPORT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GAZA GROUND OPERATIONS EXPAND\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, RUSSIA, GAZA, BOMBARDMENTS, TOUMA, HUMANITARIAN\par \par \uc2 KIRBY, ISRAEL, GAZA, HUMANITARIAN, ANTI-SEMITIC\par \par \uc2 PERRY, DEATH, TRIBUTES, "FRIENDS", ADDICTION\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, CARD, VICTIMS, MOURNING, WARNINGS, ST. PIERRE\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, GAG ORDER, CHUTKAN, ATTACKS, IVANKA\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , \uc2 STELLANTIS\uc2 , FORD, DEAL, STRIKE, \uc2 GM\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We did see that, Aaron, thank you so much for your reporting. Now to \uc2 General Motors\uc2 , on the clock this morning after striking autoworkers reached a tentative contract with Chrysler's parent company. This follows Ford's deal to end the month and a half long strike. Our senior national correspondent Terry Moran has the latest. Good morning, Terry.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UAW ESCALATES STRIKE AGAINST \uc2 GENERAL MOTORS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE WORKER WALK OFF JOB AFTER FORD & \uc2 STELLANTIS\uc2  DEALS\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Robin. And then there was one. This morning the \uc2 UAW\uc2  is raising the pressure on the last holdout among the big three American car companies, \uc2 General Motors\uc2 . The \uc2 UAW\uc2  is now calling on workers at a \uc2 GM\uc2  SUV plant in Tennessee to walk off the job. And that will make about 18,000 workers on strike at the largest US automaker.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And that follows, what they're trying to do here is pressure \uc2 GM\uc2  to agree to the same kind of contract that has already been reached with \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and Ford. Over the weekend, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , which owns brands like Chrysler and \uc2 Jeep\uc2 , came to agreement on a contract that mirrors the one that was reached with Ford last week. And that includes a 25% pay raise over four years, cost of living adjustments to protect against inflation.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) More paid time off, including two weeks of paid family leave. Big gains on pensions, and guarantees to keep certain factories open. Now those are really big wins for workers. And the \uc2 UAW\uc2  is saying that this fight is far from over. They are hoping that this strike, which began on September 15th, will help them unionize other car companies like, say, \uc2 Tesla\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And even encourage workers in other industries to organize and flex their muscle, with the \uc2 UAW\uc2  President Shawn Fain saying last night, that he hopes this strike will, quote, "Be a call to action to workers to rise up, organize and fight for a better life." Guys.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MATTHEW PERRY IN HIS OWN WORDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIS PRIVATE STRUGGLE WITH ADDICTION & LEGACY BEYOND "FRIENDS"\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We will see what happens there, Terry, thank you. Coming up, Matthew Perry, in his own words, about his struggles and his hope to help others.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR FDA WARNINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEE ALERTS ABOUT CERTAIN EYE DROPS & POPULAR BABY FOOD\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also ahead, two big FDA warnings about a popular baby food, and another one about more than two dozen over the counter eye drop products.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: APPLE EXPANDING "PAY LATER" FEATURE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT TO KNOW ABOUT "BUY NOW, PAY LATER" OPTION\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we'll tell you what you need to know before using the new \uc2 Apple\uc2  pay later feature. Right now let's go to Ginger.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231130ejau0005r\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TENTATIVE DEAL TO END \uc2 UAW\uc2  STRIKE \uc2 UAW\uc2 : OFFICIALLY SUSPENDING STRIKE AGAINST THE BIG THREE\b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WAR, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , DERMER, MAGIDISH, \uc2 OKAL\par \par \uc2 GOLDSTEIN, HOCHUL, ANTISEMITISM, ISLAMOPHOBIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FBI\uc2  INVESTIGATES THREATS AT CORNELL\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , \uc2 GENERAL MOTORS\uc2 , STRIKE, FAIN, MARSHALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENTATIVE DEAL TO END UAW STRIKE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to the strike against the big three automakers in this country. The \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  announcing a deal tonight with \uc2 General Motors\uc2 , tentatively ending the strike against all three. Tonight, what those workers will now get. Here's our chief business correspondent Rebecca Jarvis now.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 UAW\uc2 : OFFICIALLY SUSPENDING STRIKE AGAINST THE BIG THREE\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, breaking the stalemate, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and the \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  reaching an agreement.\par \par \uc2 SHAWN FAIN (UAW PRESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 We're officially suspending our stand-up strike against each of the big three.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 GM\uc2 , the final holdout, now joining Ford and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , the maker of \uc2 Jeep\uc2 , which made deals with the \uc2 UAW\uc2  this past week. After a brutal and costly six-week strike, this is what the auto workers are getting.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 UAW\uc2  AGREEMENTS WITH AUTOMAKERS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A 25%-wage increase over the next four-and-a-half years with 11% immediately coming once the deal is signed. A cost-of-living adjustment and boost to retirement income, including 401 (k) contributions.\par \par \uc2 SHAMMIRA MARSHALL (UAW MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 We need this wage increase. Christmas, Thanksgiving, the new year. That'll help.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The bitter 40-day battle between the \uc2 UAW\uc2  and the big three cost the industry an estimated $9.3 billion.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, David, while this strike is over, the workers still need to vote to ratify the deals. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rebecca Jarvis with us tonight here. Rebecca, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020231101ejau0002w\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 UAW\uc2  REACHES TENTATIVE AGREEMENT WITH FORD DEAL COMES NEARLY SIX WEEKS AFTER START OF AUTOWORKER STRIKE\b0\par\par\uc2 509 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HUTCHINSON, MANHUNT, LEVESQUE, SHOOTING, SAUSCHUCK, CARD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 16 KILLED IN MAINE SHOOTING RAMPAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE MANHUNT FOR "ARMED AND DANGEROUS" PERSON OF INTEREST\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, MANHUNT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 16 KILLED IN MAINE SHOOTING RAMPAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOZENS INJURED IN ATTACK; URGENT MANHUNT UNDERWAY FOR SUSPECT\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, GUN VIOLENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 16 KILLED IN MAINE SHOOTING RAMPAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE MANHUNT FOR "ARMED AND DANGEROUS" PERSON OF INTEREST\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, SPEAKERSHIP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICANS ELECT NEW HOUSE SPEAKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REP MIKE JOHNSON TAKES THE GAVEL AFTER WEEKS OF CHAOS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, CIVIL FRAUD, TRIAL, FINE, GAG ORDER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP TAKES THE STAND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUDGE FINES FORMER PRESIDENT $10,000 FOR VIOLATING GAG ORDER\par \par \uc2 WAR, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , NETANYAHU\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , \uc2 FORD MOTORS\uc2 , DEAL, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 UAW\uc2  REACHES TENTATIVE AGREEMENT WITH FORD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEAL COMES NEARLY SIX WEEKS AFTER START OF AUTOWORKER STRIKE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we're going to turn to the tentative deal to end the auto workers strike against Ford. The two sides reaching an agreement overnight. Our chief business correspondent Rebecca Jarvis is here now with more. Good morning, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Michael. And it has been six weeks since the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  began selective strikes at facilities of all three major US automakers. Now the job action is over against one of those companies.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT'S IN PROSPECTIVE CONTRACT\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The \uc2 UAW\uc2  and Ford both confirming a tentative deal has been reached. The union is calling it a major victory, saying the prospective contract calls for raises of about 25% over four years. It will raise the top wage to more than $40 an hour, including an increase of 68% for starting wages to more than $28 an hour. There will be other benefit increases as well. And Ford says it's looking forward to getting three of its truck plants back up and running and getting its 20,000 employees back to work. A majority of the 57,000 rank-and-file Ford employees will have to approve the proposal for it to become official.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And those strikes against \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and Chrysler parent company \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  remain ongoing, but the Ford deal could provide a framework in negotiations to end those strikes as well. Guys?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT DEAL COULD MEAN FOR WORKERS AT GM & STELLANTIS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Rebecca, thanks very much. Coming up, more on the mass shooting in Maine. The suspect is still at large.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MONSTER HURRICANE SLAMS MEXICO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAT 5 STORM IS MOST POWERFUL EVER TO HIT COUNTRY'S PACIFIC COAST\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Plus, the latest on recovery in Mexico after a monster category 5 hurricane made landfall near Acapulco.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UBER LAUNCHES DRIVERLESS RIDES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PARTNERING WITH WAYMO TO OFFER AUTONOMOUS CAR OPTIONS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And Gio is bringing us a first look at Uber's new self-driving rides.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231128ejaq00030\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DETROIT CASINO WORKERS ON STRIKE 3,700 EMPLOYEES CALLING FOR BETTER PAY & BENEFITS\b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WAR, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , BIDEN, PROTESTS, LEBANON\par \par \uc2 FINER, WAR, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , BIDEN, AID, HOSTAGES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN BROKERS HUMANITARIAN AID DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOP WHITE HOUSE OFFICIAL ON PRESIDENT'S TRIP TO ISRAEL & RISING MIDEAST TENSIONS\par \par \uc2 JORDAN, VOTE, BACON, MCHENRY, WOMACK, MOLINARO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JIM JORDAN FALLS SHORT IN SECOND HOUSE SPEAKER VOTE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOP CONGRESSMAN VOWS TO KEEP FIGHTING AS REPUBLICAN DIVIDE DEEPENS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, CASINO WORKERS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to Detroit where casino workers have joined autoworkers, actors and so many others on the picket lines. It's the latest in a wave of union strikes. Alex Perez is tracking it all. Good morning, Alex.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DETROIT CASINO WORKERS ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 3,700 EMPLOYEES CALLING FOR BETTER PAY & BENEFITS\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, George. No doubt this has become the year of strikes. And, yes, now casino workers are the latest to hit the picket lines and it's the first time they've gone on strike.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, some 3,700 Detroit-area casino workers are now on strike, impacting three casinos in the Motor City. The group is composed of five unions and includes dealers, custodians, food workers, engineers, and more. Collectively, the unions say they are calling for higher wages, better health care, retirement security and other benefits, and argue that, while casino revenue has reached record highs and surpassed pre-pandemic levels, compensation has not kept up. The casino workers now join autoworkers, hospitality workers and actors who are also on strike.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 3,700 EMPLOYEES JOIN AUTOWORKERS, ACTORS & OTHERS ON PICKET LINES\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In fact, this year, there have been 317 strikes across the country involving some 450,000 workers. For now, those casinos remain open, but it's unclear how long this strike will last. Guys?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Alex, thanks so much. There's a lot of frustration out there.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mm-hmm.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231109ejaj00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FORD EXECUTIVE CHAIR CALLS FOR END TO AUTOWORKER STRIKE LOSSES FROM \uc2 UAW\uc2  WALKOUT CLIMBING INTO BILLIONS\b0\par\par\uc2 376 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, ISRAEL, BIDEN, BLINKEN\par \par \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, ISRAEL, SCHEM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 HAMAS\uc2  RELEASES VIDEO OF HOSTAGE BEING HELD IN GAZA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REGION BRACING AS ISRAELI FORCES PREPARE FOR GROUND INVASION\par \par \uc2 BUCK, JORDAN, DIAZ-BALART, BACON, REPUBLICAN PARTY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE SET FOR KEY VOTE IN SPEAKER BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OHIO REPUBLICAN JIM JORDAN SCRAMBLING TO SHORE UP SUPPORT\par \par \uc2 GAG ORDER, TRUMP, ELECTION INTERFERENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP HIT WITH LIMITED GAG ORDER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUDGE IN FEDERAL ELECTION INTERFERENCE CASE IMPOSES PARTIAL SPEECH RESTRICTION\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 UAW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORD EXECUTIVE CHAIR CALLS FOR END TO AUTOWORKER STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOSSES FROM \uc2 UAW\uc2  WALKOUT CLIMBING INTO BILLIONS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the autoworkers strike. With losses climbing into the billions for the big three automakers, the executive chair of Ford is calling for the \uc2 UAW\uc2  to reach an agreement. Alex Perez joins us with the latest. Good morning, Alex.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, Robin. The strike is now in its fifth week and the tensions between the union auto workers and the automakers shows no point of easing at this point. No signs of easing at this point.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  is escalating what it calls its targeted strike against the big three automakers, putting an additional squeeze on Ford, having some 9,000 employees walk off the job at Ford's lucrative Kentucky truck plant last week. In rare public comments, Ford executive chair Bill Ford called on the union to reach an agreement and unite to counter the growth of foreign automakers. But the union fired back saying, if Ford wants to be the all-American auto company, they can pay all-American wages and benefits. The autoworkers are seeking a 40% pay raise, union representation at new electric battery plants, increased benefits and more. Losses from the ongoing strike are estimated to have now reach a $7.7 billion cost.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PEREZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) About 34,000 union autoworkers are on strike at more than 40 facilities across the country. Michael?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, I hope they're going to reach an agreement soon. Alex, thank you very much for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231030ejah0005q\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MAJOR ESCALATION IN AUTOWORKERS STRIKE THOUSANDS WALK OFF THE JOB AT KENTUCKY FORD PLANT\b0\par\par\uc2 486 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NETANYAHU, BARAKA, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WEISS, ZAKEN, WAR\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, IBRAHIM, KIRBY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DESTRUCTION & DEATH TOLL MOUNTING IN GAZA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ENTIRE NEIGHBORHOODS DESTROYED WITH HOSPITALS OVERWHELMED\par \par \uc2 WAR, HEZBOLLAH, ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL'S NORTHERN THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENS OF THOUSANDS OF TROOPS MOVE TO BORDER OVER CONCERN ABOUT HEZBOLLAH\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, WAR, BLINKEN, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECRETARY OF STATE BLINKEN ARRIVES IN ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SET TO MEET WITH PRIME MINISTER NETANYAHU & ISRAELI LEADERS\par \par \uc2 STRIKES, \uc2 UAW\uc2 , \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR ESCALATION IN AUTOWORKERS STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS WALK OFF THE JOB AT KENTUCKY FORD PLANT\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And let's turn now to the latest on the strikes across this country. Talks have been suspended in the actors' strike. Plus, there was a surprise move from thousands of auto workers overnight. Andrew Dymburt is here tracking it all. Good morning, Andrew.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Linsey. Thousands of auto workers unexpectedly walked off the job last night at one of Ford's most profitable truck plants. It's a major escalation in the fight between the \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  and big three car makers.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This particular Ford plant in Kentucky makes trucks an SUVs and employs around 8,700 \uc2 UAW\uc2  members. The walkout catching Ford by surprise. The facility is Ford's largest and brings in about $25 billion in revenue a year. The union cites a lack of progress in contract talks as a reason for the latest walkout. Ford says the decision by \uc2 UAW\uc2  to strike at its Kentucky truck plant without warning is, quote, "grossly irresponsible."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORD STATEMENT\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 UAW\uc2  has been on strike against Ford, \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and \uc2 General Motors\uc2  for about a month now. Linsey?\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. And, Andrew, what can you tell us about the latest as far as negotiations between actors and studios?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TALKS SUSPENDED IN ACTORS' STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDIO SAYS "CONVERSATIONS ARE NO LONGER MOVING US IN A PRODUCTIVE DIRECTION"\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, those talks are said to have completely broken down and both sides remain far apart, that being studio and the 160,000 members of the \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  guild. Guys?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Andrew, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE REPUBLICANS BACK SCALISE FOR SPEAKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PARTY DIVISIONS ON DISPLAY WITH FINAL VOTE STILL UP IN THE AIR\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And coming up, we have the search for the speaker of the House.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EX-GIRLFRIEND TESTIFIES IN CRYPTO FRAUD TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAROLINE ELLISON SAYS SAM BANKMAN-FRIED TOLD HER TO SEND "DISHONEST" INFO TO LENDERS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And former crypto billionaire Sam Bankman-Fried's former partner and girlfriend testifying about his inner circle, how they used disappearing messages to communicate.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231026ejac00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WALGREENS WALKOUT? PHARMACY EMPLOYEES CITE HARSH WORKING CONDITIONS\b0\par\par\uc2 524 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL AT WAR\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ATTACK, HOSTAGES, KATSMAN, BLINKEN, ASHER\par \par \uc2 ATTACK, FESTIVAL, ISRAEL, MANKET, MAYER, POLIN, DOR\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, SUPPORT, ISRAEL, NETANYAHU, CARRIER\par \par \uc2 FINER, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, IRAN, AMERICANS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COLDEST AIR OF THE SEASON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 EARTHQUAKE, SEARCH, AFGHANISTAN, VILLAGES\par \par \uc2 HOSTAGES, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , GAZA, ISRAEL, FAMILIES, DNA\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , SIEGE, GAZA, HOSTAGES, IRAN\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPEAKER, CHAOS, REPUBLICANS, ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 NFL, KELCE, EAGLES, 49ERS, COLLEGE, OKLAHOMA, COLORADO\par \par \uc2 BILES, CHAMPIONSHIP, GYMNASTICS, MEDALS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TROPICAL UPDATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL, WAR, SHEM TOV\par \par \uc2 SECURITY, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL, WAR\par \par \uc2 HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES, SPEAKER\par \par \uc2 WALGREENS, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 DEMARCO MORGAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  pharmacy employees signaling a possible strike on the horizon, citing harsh working conditions. Will Reeve is back with the latest and how it's impacting prescription. Will, good morning.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning again, DeMarco. Pharmacy employees at some \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  across the country are planning on walking out this morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WALGREENS WALKOUT?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PHARMACY EMPLOYEES CITE HARSH WORKING CONDITIONS\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Walkout organizers telling ABC News that more than 700 employees from the company's 9,000 stores are planning on participating, hoping to improve what they're calling understaffing and poor working condition. One employee telling ABC News, employees are overworked juggling vaccine appointments, filling prescriptions, answering phones and, as a result, in some cases, are seeing prescriptions going unfilled. ABC News has reached out to \uc2 Walgreens\uc2 . The company telling WSIL, it recognizes that the last few years have been challenging and is committed to ensuring the team has support and resources, including making investments in pharmacist wages and hiring bonuses in some locations.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, the walkout is expected to last through Wednesday. The organizers plan to do another one this month if needed. Guys?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Will, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:13, NEW A.I. LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up in our "GMA Morning Menu," the new lawsuit against law enforcement using AI to identify suspects, charging that the tech misidentifies people of color, leading to wrongful arrests.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:31, JULIA FOX TALKS NEW MEMOIR\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Also ahead, actress and fashion designer Julia Fox on her no holds barred memoir on life before stardom and her relationship with Kanye West.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:21, POP NEWS\par \par \uc2 DEMARCO MORGAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Well, it's the WNBA super team showdown and the stars in the crowd in Vegas. That's just ahead in "Pop News." And speaking of "Pop News," Lara is here with a very special guest.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:34, FALL COMFORT COOKING WITH JESSIE JAMES DECKER\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I sure am. Jessie James Decker is with us today. Delicious, easy recipes coming your way from her new cookbook. And now, you can shop for all the ingredients that you need to make these recipes on goodmorning.com. How great is that? And it's all coming up on "GMA." Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231023eja90000j\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HISTORIC HEALTH CARE WORKER STRIKE ENTERS THIRD DAY UNION THREATENS LONGER WALKOUT IF NO CONTRACT IS REACHED\b0\par\par\uc2 719 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OCTOBER FREEZE\par \par \uc2 TEMPERATURES, ALERTS, FREEZE, RAINFALL\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 KAISER PERMANENTE\uc2  , WORKERS, PATIENTS, AUTOWORKERS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we see that fog behind you as well, Ginger, this morning. Thanks for being with us. We turn now to the third day of the largest health care workers strike in US history. The job action at \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  is set to end tomorrow, but the union is threatening a longer strike if a new contract cannot be reached. Chief national correspondent Matt Gutman is in Los Angeles. Good morning, Matt.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HISTORIC HEALTH CARE WORKER STRIKE ENTERS THIRD DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNION THREATENS LONGER WALKOUT IF NO CONTRACT IS REACHED\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, Rebecca. Just to give you a sense of the national importance of this strike. At one point earlier this week acting Labor Secretary Julie Su was acting as a mediator between Kaiser and the union shuttling between them. At this point talks have completely broken down and what could be just the first round of the largest health care workers strike in US history.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) With both sides dug in, the largest health care workers strike in US history entering its third day.\par \par \uc2 WORKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 What do we want?\par \par \uc2 WORKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 (Inaudible)\par \par \uc2 WORKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 When do we want it.\par \par \uc2 WORKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Now.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) More than 75,000 workers across the nation picketing \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  , the largest nonprofit health care provider in the US. The unions are demanding pay increases and fighting what they call unfair labor practices and unsafe staffing levels.\par \par \uc2 DAVID BOSTON (RESPIRATORY THERAPIST KAISER)\par \par \uc2 We're working, you know, one respiratory therapist that should be doing the job of two or three.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The strike has limited elective and nonemergency procedures, affecting patients like Nicole and her dad.\par \par \uc2 NICOLE CORSI (FATHER'S KAISER APPOINTMENT WAS CANCELED)\par \par \uc2 When we showed up, they said he didn't have an appointment. So that was kind of surprising. We didn't know there was a strike going on. And so they were able to accommodate us with a different nurse.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Kaiser saying they've reached a number of tentative agreements with the unions on a minimum wage for employees, but Roscio Chicon (PH) a union rep in those marathon negotiations, saying Kaiser never actually presented the deal to the union.\par \par \uc2 UNION REP (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Don't go out to the press. And don't send an email saying that you have, when I haven't even seen it.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The hospital system overnight reiterating its commitment to reaching a deal. "We are coordinating with coalition leaders to reconvene bargaining as soon as possible."\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And union leaders are telling me that if progress isn't made in the coming days, they will come back, quote, "Longer and stronger, striking again in the first week of November. This time for five days." And at this point this year nearly half million Americans have taken part in labor strikes, from the auto industry, the entertainment industry and, of course, the health care industry, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, of course, those autoworkers have now been on strike for three weeks, Matt.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AUTOWORKERS ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNION PRESIDENT TEASING ANNOUNCEMENT AMID ONGOING TALKS\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They have. But there might be some progress. \uc2 GM\uc2  saying that it made a counter offer to the \uc2 UAW\uc2  . Ford reportedly saying that it's narrowed differences on key sticking points with the \uc2 UAW\uc2  . And perhaps most tellingly, very playfully the President of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  , Shawn Fain, posted a picture of the "Bachelorette" ahead of his press conference today.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But instead of the faces of the men, he posted the logos of \uc2 GM\uc2  , \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and Ford saying we'll have to tune in to see which one of them got the rose, I guess that will mean which one they've made progress with. Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, and a lot of lives hang in the balance. Matt Gutman, thank you. George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231019eja600003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ALL EYES ON NEW JOBS REPORT HIRING EXPECTED TO COOL AS THE FEDERAL RESERVE WEIGHS AN INTEREST RATE HIKE\b0\par\par\uc2 297 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OCTOBER FREEZE\par \par \uc2 TEMPERATURES, ALERTS, FREEZE, RAINFALL\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 KAISER PERMANENTE\uc2  , WORKERS, PATIENTS, AUTOWORKERS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2  , PRATT, CLASSIFIED, NUCLEAR SUB, SPECIAL COUNSEL\par \par \uc2 JORDAN, HOUSE, SPEAKER, TRUMP, GOP\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, BALL, BORDER, FUNDS, MIGRANTS, JEAN-PIERRE\par \par \uc2 STABBING, CARSON, DOWLING, RANDOM, COURT\par \par \uc2 JOBS REPORT, FED, INTEREST RATE, MORTGAGES\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Really tough story. Okay, Trevor, thank you. We turn now to the eagerly awaited September jobs report. A cooling labor market could have a big impact on the Fed's next interest rate decision. Elizabeth Schulze is in Washington with more. Good morning, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON NEW JOBS REPORT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIRING EXPECTED TO COOL AS THE FEDERAL RESERVE WEIGHS AN INTEREST RATE HIKE\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Rebecca. And this is a critical report for the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  . Analysts expect that 170,000 jobs were added to the economy in September. That is still a strong pace of hiring. But it would be a slowdown from August. Now a stronger than expected report this morning could put even more pressure on the Fed to keep raising interest rates.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And already Wall Street and American consumers are feeling the impact of those higher rates. Mortgage rates just hit a new 23-year high. So today's average, 7.5% rate for a 30 year fixed mortgage. Your monthly payment on a $400,000 home loan is about $300 more than it would have been just at the start of this year. So this jobs report, along with the inflation data next week, are key for the Fed as it determines where borrowing costs go from here. Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231019eja600008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CRASH INVOLVING MENENDEZ'S WIFE PROBED NJ OFFICIALS INVESTIGATING IF ANY PRESSURE WAS APPLIED\b0\par\par\uc2 787 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, HEAT, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, TRUDEAU, CORAZZIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "ARMED AND DANGEROUS" MANHUNT\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, SNOWLING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHILLING VIDEO OF DEPUTIES SHOOTOUT\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, JORDAN, GAETZ, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP ENDORSES JORDAN FOR SPEAKER\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, BORDER WALL, LOPEZ, ADAMS, IMMIGRATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN ON WALL: "I HAD NO CHOICE"\par \par \uc2 MENENDEZ, UPTION, CAR CRASH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CRASH INVOLVING MENENDEZ'S WIFE PROBED\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next, tonight, the new investigation involving the wife of New Jersey Senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2 . Prosecutors are asking whether any influence was exerted after a fatal car crash with Nadine Menendez at the wheel. The crash was mention in a recent federal indictment of the senator and his wife because the co-defendant is accused of giving her a new Mercedes. Here's ABC's senior investigative reporter Aaron Katersky.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NJ OFFICIALS INVESTIGATING IF ANY PRESSURE WAS APPLIED\par \par \uc2 AARON KATERSKY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, the New Jersey Attorney General's Office is investigating whether there was any pressure applied in the police handing of a fatal car crash involving the wife of Senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 NADINE MENENDEZ (WIFE OF SENATOR BOB MENENDEZ)\par \par \uc2 Why was the guy in the middle of the street?\par \par \uc2 AARON KATERSKY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In 2018, Nadine Menendez, who was dating the senator at the time, struck and killed 49-year-old father Richard Koop, as seen in this surveillance video.\par \par \uc2 NADINE MENENDEZ (WIFE OF SENATOR BOB MENENDEZ)\par \par \uc2 He jumped on my windshield.\par \par \uc2 AARON KATERSKY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Bogota Police dash cam video shows an officer talking to Menendez, who declined to have her phone examined and was released without a sobriety test. She was never charged. But the victim's family won an insurance claim against Nadine Menendez. The crash is referenced in the recent indictment that charges the senator, his wife, and three businessmen with bribery and extortion conspiracy. Nadine Menendez allegedly texted one of the co-defendants after the crash about her lack of a car. Months later, prosecutors say she bought a $60,000 Mercedes convertible with money supplied in exchange for the senator's intervention in a criminal case.\par \par \uc2 AARON KATERSKY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Senator Menendez has called the crash a tragic accident. He and his wife have each pleaded not guilty to the federal corruption charges. And, Whit, Menendez has been resisting widespread calls by Democrats for his resignation. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Aaron Katersky, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLOCKBUSTER JOBS REPORT\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to that strong and surprising jobs report. Employers creating 330,000 new jobs in September, nearly double the 170,000 predicted.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JOBS REPORT\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Unemployment reins unchanged at 3.8%. President Biden touting the numbers today, pushing back on why Americans aren't feeling the benefits of a strong economy.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 I think that the American people are smart as hell and know what their interests are. I think they know they're better off financially than they were before. It's a fact.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) These jobs numbers are encouraging, but they could also put pressure on the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  to continue raising interest rates to keep inflation in check.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL STRIKES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UAW DECIDES NOT TO EXPAND STRIKE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, the \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  is reporting progress in their negotiations, saying that GM has agreed to place their electric battery manufacturing under the union's master agreement, a key part of the industry's future.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And more than 75,000 union workers at \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  health care facilities return to work tomorrow after a three-day strike, but they are threatening a longer walkout next month if they haven't reached a deal.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALABAMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COURT ORDERS NEW VOTING MAP\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next tonight, a federal court selected a new congressional map for Alabama with two districts where black voters are a majority.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Republican-controlled legislature had twice redrawn the map with just one majority black district, though more than a quarter of the population is black. In June, the Supreme Court found that a violation of civil rights law was included. A federal appeals court appointed a special master to devise the new map. It will be in effect for the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we come back tonight, the grim discovery in Colorado, 115 bodies found improperly stored at a funeral home. Authorities now trying to identify those bodies. And the massive candy recall with Halloween just around the corner.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020231010eja600007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MASSIVE HEALTH CARE STRIKE TALKS END WITHOUT DEAL AFTER 75,000 WORKERS WALK OFF THE JOB\b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY, JORDAN, SCALISE, MCHENRY, GRAVES, MCCAUL\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, STABBING, CARSON, KENNY, HOLDEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT MANHUNT FOR BROOKLYN STABBING SUSPECT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRUTAL ATTACK ON SOCIAL JUSTICE ACTIVIST CAUGHT ON CAMERA\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2  , TRIAL, FRAUD, JAMES\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, STUDENT LOAN, IMMIGRATION, BORDER WALL\par \par \uc2 KAISER PERMANENTE\uc2  , STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE HEALTH CARE STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TALKS END WITHOUT DEAL AFTER 75,000 WORKERS WALK OFF THE JOB\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, George, now to the massive health care worker's strike. Tens of thousands of workers are walking the picket lines across the country, impacting millions of patients. Chief national correspondent Matt Gutman is in California with the latest more for us. Good morning, Matt.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, Robin. Both sides reporting overnight that they are deadlocked. Now, they've been negotiating at a San Francisco hotel for days, but that is on pause right now. That means we will see health care workers back out here picketing again today for the second consecutive day.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, the union representing them saying this is the largest health care worker strike in US history, 75,000 workers. Now, overnight Kaiser saying that it is still committed to reaching a new agreement with the unions. They also said that they reached some tentative agreements on employee pay and they are assuring the public that patient care has not been compromised.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They brought in enough temporary workers to fill the gap. Now, the coalition of unions is saying that they are still waiting on a meaningful response from Kaiser on staffing levels and employee pay that would reflect the rising cost of living. Now, they plan this to be a three-day strike, today is the second day. And they're warning that if progress isn't made, they will come back, quote, "longer and stronger" for another strike in November. Michael?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Definitely affecting a lot of patients there. Matt, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231018eja50005q\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MAJOR HEALTH CARE WORKER STRIKE 75,000 \uc2 KAISER PERMANENTE\uc2  EMPLOYEES SET TO WALK OFF JOB\b0\par\par\uc2 483 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MCCARTHY OUSTED IN HISTORIC MOVE\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY, HOUSE, OUSTED, CHAOS, GAETZ, DEMS\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY, HOUSE, OUSTED, REPUBLICANS, DEMOCRATS\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, INJURED, HBCU, STUDENTS, SCOTT\par \par \uc2 WALL STREET, STOCKS, INTEREST RATES, JOBS\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, KAISER, EMPLOYEES, LUCAS, NEGOTIATIONS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is a bright spot. But as you always tell us, Wall Street does not like uncertainty, and that's what we're experiencing right now. All right, Rebecca, thank you, as always. Now another major strike set to hit our nation this morning. This time the largest strike of health care workers in US history. Mola Lenghi is in Englewood, Colorado with those details. Good morning, Mola.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR HEALTH CARE WORKER STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 75,000 \uc2 KAISER PERMANENTE\uc2  EMPLOYEES SET TO WALK OFF JOB\par \par \uc2 MOLA LENGHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Robin. Yeah, that walkout officially beginning this morning with tens of thousands of \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  workers demanding higher pay and increased staff. And unless a deal is reached, they plan to continue their strike through the week.\par \par \uc2 MOLA LENGHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, roughly 75,000 health care workers in eight states are about to go on strike.\par \par \uc2 KAISER PATIENT COORDINATOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 You see the patient, and it's hard not to get emotional.\par \par \uc2 MOLA LENGHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Priscilla Aubeabs (PH) is a patient coordinator at a Kaiser hospital east of San Francisco, she's one of thousands of support staff, nurses, radiologists and lab techs, set for a three day walkout after their contract expired this past Saturday.\par \par \uc2 CAROLINE LUCAS (EXEC DIR COALITION OF \uc2 KAISER PERMANENTE\uc2  UNIONS)\par \par \uc2 What we want is simple. We want Kaiser executives to listen to front line health care workers and bargain in good faith.\par \par \uc2 MOLA LENGHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The union wants a starting wage of $25 an hour, $4 more than Kaiser is offering. They also want annual raises between 6% and 7%. Kaiser's proposed increase would cap out at 4%. Workers also demanding an increase to staffing levels after the pandemic decimated nursing ranks.\par \par \uc2 MOLA LENGHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Negotiations are ongoing and \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  says, "A strike is not inevitable and it is certainly not justified and their goal is to reach a fair and equitable agreement that strengthens \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  as a best place to work."\par \par \uc2 CAROLINE LUCAS (EXEC DIR COALITION OF \uc2 KAISER PERMANENTE\uc2  UNIONS)\par \par \uc2 Kaiser executives can solve this if they show up with a sense of urgency, a mind towards solutions to really do deep investment in work force infrastructure that is needed.\par \par \uc2 MOLA LENGHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A strike could impact some 13 million patients, though hospitals and ER's would remain open, nonemergency procedures likely face delays.\par \par \uc2 MOLA LENGHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, Kaiser telling us overnight that several provisions have been agreed upon as negotiations are ongoing. George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231018eja400006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 LARGEST US HEALTH CARE STRIKE 75,000+ \uc2 KAISER PERMANENTE\uc2  WORKERS WALK OUT\b0\par\par\uc2 417 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, STABBING, CARSON, KENNY, HORNER\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, SHOOTING, WORLEY, SCOTT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT SEARCH AFTER UNIVERSITY SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 JORDAN, SCALISE, GRAVES, BIDEN, HOUSE SPEAKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLE FOR HOUSE SPEAKER\par \par \uc2 FRAUD, TRIAL, TRUMP, JAMES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NY AG: "I WILL NOT BE BULLIED"\par \par \uc2 ROSS, SENA, BROWN, ABDUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KIDNAPPING SUSPECT'S "SON" SPEAKS\par \par \uc2 KAISER PERMANENTE\uc2  , STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LARGEST U.S. HEALTH CARE STRIKE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to a new strike here in the US, and it is sweeping tonight. More than 75,000 health care workers for \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  walking off the job in several states and Washington, DC. Kaiser provides care for nearly 13 million Americans. Here's Matt Gutman.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 75,000+ \uc2 KAISER PERMANENTE\uc2  WORKERS WALK OUT\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, more than 75,000 health care workers walking off the job in multiple states. The union coalition calling it the largest health care worker strike in US history.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Why are we here?\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Patient care.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) They're picketing \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  , the company that provides health care for nearly 13 million people.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Whose got the power?\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Workers from California, Oregon, and Washington state, to Colorado and Virginia and Washington, DC, are fighting for increased pay and against what they say are unfair labor practices and unsafe staffing levels. Respiratory therapist David Boston (PH) telling me...\par \par \uc2 RESPIRATORY THERAPIST (MALE)\par \par \uc2 We're working, you know, one respiratory therapist that should be doing the job of two or three.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Crystal Dunn (PH) works in the optometry department. She says she has to work side jobs to make ends meet.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I can't even cover outside of my rent. Everything else that I need, groceries and food, to toiletries, different things like that.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The strike set to last for three days in the west, and one day in the east. Doctors are not striking, though, and Kaiser is using temporary workers in place of its employees who are.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) David, Kaiser says even though those temporary workers have stepped in, that hasn't compromised patient care. Kaiser also says that it is committed to reaching a new agreement. I'm told both sides negotiating around the clock. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Matt Gutman right there with the picket lines behind him. Matt, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020231006eja400007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BACK ON THE AIR LATE-NIGHT TALK SHOWS RETURN AFTER END OF WRITERS' STRIKE\b0\par\par\uc2 777 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY, GAETZ, GOOD, BURCHETT, ROY\par \par \uc2 SENA, ROSS, HOCHUL, ALLEN, KIDNAPPING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MISSING GIRL FOUND ALIVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 9-YEAR-OLD RESCUED, SUSPECT IN CUSTODY AFTER URGENT 48-HOUR SEARCH\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, FRAUD, TRIAL, JAMES, COHEN\par \par \uc2 CARJACKING, CUELLAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CONGRESSMAN CARJACKED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS REP CUELLAR ROBBED AT GUNPOINT NEAR DC RESIDENCE\par \par \uc2 PASSPORT, PROCESSING TIME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSPORT WAIT TIMES REDUCED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRST DECREASE SINCE POST-PANDEMIC TRAVEL BOOM\par \par \uc2 IPHONE 15, APPLE, OVERHEATING, PARMAR\par \par \uc2 KIMMEL, WGA, \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 , STRIKE, SCHWARZENEGGER\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, we're going to go down to the return of late-night television.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BACK ON THE AIR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LATE-NIGHT TALK SHOWS RETURN AFTER END OF WRITERS' STRIKE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Shows were back on the air overnight with the writers back at work while the actors are back at the negotiating table working towards their own deal. Kayna Whitworth is in Los Angeles. Good morning, Kayna.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Michael, good morning to you. So, they're back at that negotiating table for the first time in two months. And actors on the picket lines tell us they're both excited and hopeful following what's widely seen as a win for the Writers Guild.\par \par \uc2 JIMMY KIMMEL\uc2  (HOST "JIMMY KIMMEL LIVE")\par \par \uc2 The thing is, the strike, you know, has been going on so long, I just don't know if I'll be back.\par \par \uc2 ARNOLD SCHWARZENEGGER (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 You'll be back.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Looks like Arnold was right. Late night talk shows finally returning following the end of the writers' strike.\par \par \uc2 JIMMY KIMMEL\uc2  (HOST "JIMMY KIMMEL LIVE")\par \par \uc2 In case you've forgotten, my name is Jimmy. I've been off the air for five months.\par \par \uc2 STEPHEN COLBERT (HOST "THE LATE SHOW WITH STEPHEN COLBERT")\par \par \uc2 We're back, baby. We're back.\par \par \uc2 JIMMY FALLON (HOST "THE TONIGHT SHOW STARRING JIMMY FALLON")\par \par \uc2 Seriously, we were off the air for so long, "The Bachelor" went from this to this. I mean, what happened?\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For five months, the WGA strike has crippled all corner of television, even daytime. Now, writers' rooms across Hollywood no longer empty. Writers negotiating a three-year agreement with studios to hearing increase compensation, residuals from streaming revenue and control of AI usage.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WGA THREE-YEAR AGREEMENT\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 (Inaudible).\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BACK TO THE BARGAINING TABLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TALKS RESUME TO SETTLE SAG-AFTRA STRIKE\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This as their sister union, \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 , pushes toward reaching a similar solution for actors, returning to the negotiation table this week with the major TV and film studio CEOs, all while remaining on the picket line.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 It's actually very inspiring knowing that WGA got their deal. And the most majority of things that they were talking about, we're talking about as well. So, it's promising.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL SCHNEIDER (TV EDITOR "VARIETY")\par \par \uc2 If the actors strike a deal then, by the end of October, cameras could start rolling again and some of your shows that weren't on in the fall will hopefully be back by mid-season.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And how about that? Now, he went on to say that many of those films that were delayed could also perhaps be in theaters as soon as next summer. Guys?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are hoping for that.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Mm-hmm.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JURY SELECTION BEGINS IN SAM BANKMAN-FRIED TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FTX\uc2  FOUNDER ACCUSED IN MULTI-BILLION DOLLAR FRAUD AFTER CRYPTO COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up, the trial of former crypto billionaire \uc2 Sam Bankman-Fried\uc2  set to begin. He's facing charges that he masterminded one of the biggest financial frauds in US history.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INSIDE THE INFERNO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THAT LATEST TECHNOLOGY HELPING WILDFIRE SAFETY RESEARCH\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And Matt Gutman is standing by in South Carolina with the biggest ember generator in the world and its use for wildfire safety research. Hey there, Matt.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Robin. This is where they study the science of wildfires. And they have fired up that ember generator. Those embers burning at 2200 degrees. In just a couple of minutes, I'm going to show you how embers like these can gather around your house and get into your house in ways you never imagined and some practical steps to try to protect your home coming right up.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, we're looking forward to that, Matt. And that's coming up.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231017eja300030\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HISTORIC HEALTH CARE STRIKE LOOMING? 75,000 \uc2 KAISER PERMANENTE\uc2  WORKERS COULD WALK OFF THE JOB\b0\par\par\uc2 370 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP IN COURT\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, FRAUD, TRUMP, JAMES, MINTZ, LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY, DEMOCRATS, REPUBLICANS, SHUTDOWN, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM, FEINSTEIN, BUTLER, SENATE, ACTIVIST, LGBTQ\par \par \uc2 MISSING, SEARCH, SENA, HOCHUL, CAMPING, MAZZONE\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 KAISER PERMANENTE\uc2  , NEGOTIATE\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are hoping for the best outcome. Stephanie, thank you. Now to a potential new strike with 75,000 health care employees in five states threatening to walk off the job this week. Rhiannon Ally has the latest. Good morning, Rhiannon.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HISTORIC HEALTH CARE STRIKE LOOMING?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 75,000 \uc2 KAISER PERMANENTE\uc2  WORKERS COULD WALK OFF THE JOB\par \par \uc2 RHIANNON ALLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Linsey. Yeah, the contract expired this weekend, setting the stage for what would be the largest health care strike in US history. We are talking 75,000 \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  employee in five states threatening to walk off the job this Wednesday. Healthcare workers in California, Oregon, Washington, Colorado, Virginia and Washington, DC.\par \par \uc2 RHIANNON ALLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A coalition of unions representing them said it remains far apart with the company on key issues. The workers are seeking pay raises, better pensions and protections against outsourcing. And, guys, the company says it will continue to negotiate in good faith.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TALKS RESUME IN SAG-AFTRA STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRST NEGOTIATIONS SINCE START OF WALKOUT\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, of course, Rhiannon, this is not the only strike making news. We know the Hollywood writers' strike ended, but production cannot resume on shows and movies until the actors strike is resolved. What's the latest with \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  ?\par \par \uc2 RHIANNON ALLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, the actors went on strike back in July, and they haven't been to the bargaining table with the studios since before the strike started. The end of the writers' strike last week was certainly a good sign. So they return to the bargaining table today and hopefully will have a much better idea of how close they really are to getting a deal done soon. Linsey.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, so many people hoping that that is over sooner than later. Thank you, Rhiannon. Gio.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231017eja200006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 UAW\uc2  EXPANDS STRIKE AGAINST AUTOMAKERS ADDITIONAL 7,000 WORKERS WALK OFF JOB, 2 MORE ASSEMBLY PLANTS IMPACTED\b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POTENTIAL IMPACTS: LOOMING GOVERNMENT SHUTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GOVERNMENT, SHUTDOWN, STOPGAP, WOMACK, MCCARTHY, BIDEN, FOWLER\par \par \uc2 MILITARY, GOVERNMENT, SHUTDOWN\par \par \uc2 EMERGENCY, NEW YORK, NEW JERSEY, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, FULTON, ELECTION, FRAUD, HALL, PLEA\par \par \uc2 FEINSTEIN, TRAILBLAZER, SENATOR, AIELLO, PELOSI, BIDEN, MCCONNELL\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE, PLANTS, AUTOMAKERS\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This morning, the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  strike against the big three automakers is expanding as parties from each side escalate their war of words. ABC's Alexis Christoforous is here now with the latest. Alexis, good morning.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Will. Another 7,000 \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  walked off the job Friday, bringing the total number on picket lines to 25,000. The strike now expanded to two more plants, a Ford plant in Chicago that builds the Explorer and Lincoln Aviator, and \uc2 GM\uc2 's Lansing Delta plant, which assembles the Buick Enclave and Chevy Traverse. The \uc2 UAW\uc2  says \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  was spared this time, citing progress in talks with the parent of Chrysler.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is the second escalation of strikes that began on September 15th. The union and the companies remain far apart on key issues. The uaw sticking with its demand for 40 percent pay hikes over a four-year contract. The automakers have offered pay increases of about 20 percent. And the workers want job guarantees at new electric vehicle battery plants that have yet to start production. But so far, the strike has had little impact on car shoppers. That's because automakers were well-supplied heading into the strike.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WALKOUT COULD LEAD TO HIGHER PRICES FOR NEW AND USED CARS\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But, if the walkout drags on through October, industry analysts tell me we could see higher prices for both new and used cars, and they say holiday incentives, like zero percent interest loans and cash-back offers will likely disappear. And you may feel the effects at the auto shop a lot sooner. Analysts say part shortages could make auto repairs take longer, so brace yourself. Janai.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, you could feel the impacts on the car lot, at the auto repair shops. Thank you, Alexis.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231016ej9u00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CALIFORNIA RAISES MINIMUM WAGE FOR FAST FOOD WORKERS WILL MAKE $20 PER HOUR STARTING NEXT APRIL\b0\par\par\uc2 241 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO SHUTDOWN\par \par \uc2 SHUTDOWN, HOUSE, MCCARTHY, SENATE, CUELLAR, PAYCHECKS\par \par \uc2 KIRBY, SHUTDOWN, REPUBLICANS, FURLOUGH, MILITARY UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 AUTOWORKERS, STRIKE, NEGOTIATIONS, WALKOUTS\par \par \uc2 FENTANYL, SEIZED, TRAFFICKERS, TARANTINO, SUBWAY\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, FLOODING, ALERTS\par \par \uc2 CALIFORNIA, GAS, PRICES, NEWSOM, REFORM\par \par \uc2 CALIFORNIA, MINIMUM WAGE, INCREASE, FAST FOOD\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, also on the West Coast, thank you, Zohreen. A law is hiking the minimum wage for fast food workers in California. Andrew Dymburt is tracking the latest there. Good morning, Andrew.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CALIFORNIA RAISES MINIMUM WAGE FOR FAST FOOD WORKERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL MAKE $20 PER HOUR STARTING NEXT APRIL\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Juju. It is now law in California. The new minimum wage for fast food workers in the state is $20 per hour, taking effect on April 1st of next year. About half a million workers will be affected by this increase. Critics say the wage hike will be a burden on businesses, which may then pass this cost on to the consumer.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  and proponents of the new law say this will help improve the lives of fast food employees and reward their sacrifice. $20 an hour by the way is just a starting point. The law also creates a council which could increase that wage each year through 2029. Guys.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231013ej9t00008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AUTOWORKERS STRIKE SET TO EXPAND MORE WALKOUTS EXPECTED AS NEGOTIATIONS WITH BIG THREE STALL\b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO SHUTDOWN\par \par \uc2 SHUTDOWN, HOUSE, MCCARTHY, SENATE, CUELLAR, PAYCHECKS\par \par \uc2 KIRBY, SHUTDOWN, REPUBLICANS, FURLOUGH, MILITARY UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 AUTOWORKERS, STRIKE, NEGOTIATIONS, WALKOUTS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Michael, thank you. We turn now to autoworkers on the picket line. The \uc2 UAW\uc2  is set to expand its strike this morning with negotiations stalled. And our senior national correspondent Terry Moran joins us with the very latest. Good morning, Terry.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AUTOWORKERS STRIKE SET TO EXPAND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE WALKOUTS EXPECTED AS NEGOTIATIONS WITH BIG THREE STALL\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Rebecca. This morning at car dealerships like this one in Frederick, Maryland, where I get my own Mustang serviced, they're bracing for a longer strike. It's day 14 of this strike. And all signs point to more plants and facilities shutting down as more workers hit the picket lines. \uc2 UAW\uc2  President Shawn Fain, will announce the union's next move at 10:00 AM this morning on a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  live.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Fain has warned that if serious progress has not been made by that point, this strike will widen. He's used that pressure tactic before. And now 3,400 \uc2 UAW\uc2  - makers at tractor-trailer manufacturer, Mac Trucks, they may go on strike as well. Their contract expires on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Out on the picket lines, it's getting tense. Fain has accused \uc2 GM\uc2  and Chrysler Stellantis of, quote, "Enabling violence," after several tense confrontations between strikers and employers going into workers going into work. The companies deny those charges, they blame the workers for what they call, quote, "Dangerous behavior."\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The auto strike is already hitting dealers like the Frederick Motor Company, where I am. They're expecting to see new car prices and used car prices go up. And also getting your car serviced, getting more costly, as those parts shortages grow more and more acute. Juju.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231013ej9t00004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 UAW\uc2  EXPANDS STRIKE FURTHER NEARLY 7,000 AUTO WORKERS WALK OFF JOB\b0\par\par\uc2 181 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TRAVEL, FLOODING, ADAMS\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 SHUTDOWN, MCCARTHY, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 FEINSTEIN, TRIBUTE, SCHUMER, PELOSI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATOR DIANE FEINSTEIN DIES AT 90\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, HALL, PLEA DEAL, ELECTION INTERFERENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRST PLEA DEAL IN GEORGIA ELECTION CASE\par \par \uc2 MILLEY, RETIREMENT, BROWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MILLEY REBUKES "WANNABE DICTATOR"\par \par \uc2 ARREST, SHAKUR, DAVIS, WOLFSON, JOHANSSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARREST IN TUPAC SHAKUR MURDER\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 UAW\uc2  EXPANDS STRIKE FURTHER\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  is now expanding its strike against Ford and \uc2 GM\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Nearly 7,000 more auto workers walking off the job now at Ford Chicago's assembly plant and \uc2 GM\uc2 's Lansing Delta assembly plant. The CEO of Ford tonight saying they were close to a deal, but accused the union of holding it up over jobs at electric vehicle battery factories.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we come back, the former football star made famous in "The Blind Side." He said that adoption was all a lie. What a judge has now decided tonight.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020231003ej9t00009\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HOLLYWOOD WRITERS BACK TO WORK UNION VOTES TO END 148 DAY STRIKE\b0\par\par\uc2 450 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 NORTH KOREA, KING, DMZ, EXPEL, US ARMY\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, FRAUD, JUDGE, BUSINESSES, ASSETS\par \par \uc2 SHUTDOWN, MCCARTHY, HOUSE, SENATE, REPUBLICANS\par \par \uc2 LOOTING, JUVENILES, RETAIL, SUSPECTS, IRIZARRY\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE, PICKET LINE, TRUMP\par \par \uc2 LAWSUIT, AMAZON, FTC, MONOPOLY, PARKS\par \par \uc2 WRITERS, STRIKE, VOTE, AGREEMENT, \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Like you said, a big if. Okay, Rebecca, thank you. Now to Hollywood. Writers going back to work this morning after a vote by leadership to end their 148-day strike. We're learning new details about their deal with the studios and streamers. Kayna Whitworth is in Los Angeles with those details. Good morning, Kayna.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLLYWOOD WRITERS BACK TO WORK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNION VOTES TO END 148 DAY STRIKE\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Robin, good morning to you. The Hollywood writers' strike is officially over. The nearly 150-day strike ending one minute after Midnight. And the union securing some major wins here. Details of this deal have been spare until now, but here's what we know so far. This three-year deal outlines a 12.5% pay increase starting with a 5% bump when the contract is ratified.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) One of the sticking points involved royalties. And the writers secured a 76% increase for their foreign streaming residuals, and they will also receive a viewership based streaming bonus. And another big win for these members, studios and streamers will have to hire a minimum number of writers on projects.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the final issue, arguably the most important, revolved around artificial intelligence, the two sides established a set of guidelines regarding the use of AI. But, you guys, of course, \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  still on strike. But a lot of people hope Hollywood is back up and running in some six to eight weeks here, guys.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FAMILY OF SLAIN SHERIFF'S DEPUTY SPEAKS OUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MOM & FIANC\u201\'00\'C9E BREAK THEIR SILENCE AFTER DEADLY AMBUSH\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Okay, Kayna, thanks very much. And Kayna is going to back with an ABC News exclusive. She spoke with the mother and the fianc\u233\'00\'E9e of the Los Angeles Sheriff's Deputy who was killed in an ambush.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STRIKE ON THE STRIP?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LAS VEGAS HOSPITALITY WORKERS VOTE TO AUTHORIZE STRIKE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also ahead, could 60,000 Las Vegas workers be heading to the picket lines?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WEIGHT LOSS WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PHARMACIES SOUND ALARM ON SITES SELLING DRUGS USED FOR WEIGHT LOSS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And that potential danger of buying popular drugs used for weight loss online. But first, good morning, Ginger.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231011ej9r00008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PRESIDENT ON THE PICKET LINE BIDEN VISITS STRIKING AUTOWORKERS: "STICK WITH IT"\b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 NORTH KOREA, KING, DMZ, EXPEL, US ARMY\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, FRAUD, JUDGE, BUSINESSES, ASSETS\par \par \uc2 SHUTDOWN, MCCARTHY, HOUSE, SENATE, REPUBLICANS\par \par \uc2 LOOTING, JUVENILES, RETAIL, SUSPECTS, IRIZARRY\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE, PICKET LINE, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Stephanie, thanks. Now to President Biden, he's on the picket line, unprecedented for a president, joining striking autoworkers during a visit to Michigan, encouraged the union to stick with it. Senior national correspondent Terry Moran is in Wayne, Michigan, with the latest. Good morning, Terry.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT ON THE PICKET LINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN VISITS STRIKING AUTOWORKERS: "STICK WITH IT"\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. It's day 12 of the autoworkers strike. And they're on the picket line 24/7 here at this Ford plant and at sites across the country. And now their cause has moved to the center of the presidential campaign. President Biden making history with that unprecedented show of solidarity with the striking autoworkers, joining the picket line at a \uc2 General Motors\uc2  facility just a few miles from here, and becoming the first president to stand with striking workers on a picket line.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Biden went further, he openly sided with the union and endorsed their demands for big wage increases and bigger benefits, declaring that workers, quote, "Deserved the significant raise that you need and other benefits to get back what we lost," unquote.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT ON THE PICKET LINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP TO MEET WITH UNION LEADERS ONE DAY AFTER BIDEN VISIT\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And today is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's turn. The Republican frontrunner is gonna be giving a speech to several, about 500 people, workers and Trump supporters at a nonunion auto parts facility north of Detroit. And Trump is actually skipping the Republican debate in California. He's ignoring his Republican rivals to go directly after Biden on the economy and on electric vehicles.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The Biden administration's policy is to shift the country to electric vehicles. That's a huge issue for many of the workers here who worry that that shift could cost them their jobs. Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231011ej9r00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 "SHARKS" BARBARA CORCORAN & DAYMOND JOHN LIVE! ANSWERING YOUR SMALL BUSINESS QUESTIONS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,479 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BIDEN, \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE, BECK, HALL\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, WGA, DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLLYWOOD ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WGA & STUDIOS REACH TENTATIVE DEAL TO END WRITERS' STRIKE\par \par \uc2 SHUTDOWN, MCCARTHY, GAETZ, COAKLEY, PRICE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO A SHUTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATE EYES STOPGAP AS HOUSE REPUBLICANS PUSH AHEAD WITH SPENDING BILLS\par \par \uc2 MENENDEZ, CORTEZ, UPTION, WILLIAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INDICTED SENATOR REFUSES TO STEP DOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW JERSEY DEMOCRAT BOB MENENDEZ VOWS TO FIGHT UPTION CHARGES\par \par \uc2 ABUSE, THOMPSON, LEE, FRAMPTON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATON ROUGE POLICE UNDER INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFICERS ACCUSED OF ABUSING DETAINEES IN A WAREHOUSE\par \par \uc2 LONG COVID, SYMPTOMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LONG COVID AFFECTING MILLIONS OF AMERICANS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CDC: NEARLY 7% OF ADULTS HAVE HAD SYMPTOMS FOR THREE MONTHS OR MORE\par \par \uc2 SALTWATER INTRUSION, WATER SUPPLY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW ORLEANS SALTWATER INTRUSION CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOUISIANA GOVERNOR REQUESTS FEDERAL EMERGENCY DECLARATION\par \par \uc2 FOOTBALL, SWIFT, \uc2 NFL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLE OF THE UNBEATENS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EAGLES DEFEAT BUCCANEERS 25-10 ON MONDAY NIGHT FOOTBALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TURBULENCE, JETBLUE, TAJER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUDDEN SEVERE TURBULENCE INJURES EIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JETBLUE FLIGHT TO FLORIDA RUNS INTO ROUGH AIR\par \par \uc2 STUDENT LOANS, SCAM, AIZPURU, TYRELL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT WARNING ABOUT STUDENT LOAN PAYMENT SCAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW CRIMINALS ARE TARGETING BORROWERS WITH THE FEDERAL PAUSE SET TO EXPIRE\par \par \uc2 PUMPKIN, MCCUAN, HUYCK, SCAVUZZO, STOCKEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DON'T BE CAUGHT OFF GOURD!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHY PUMPKINS MAY BE HARDER TO FIND & SMALLER THIS YEAR\par \par \uc2 ZACKL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ANTARCTIC SEA ICE\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE, BIDEN, FORD, PICKET LINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN TO JOIN STRIKING AUTOWORKERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT TRAVELS TO MICHIGAN TO JOIN PICKET LINE\par \par \uc2 SHUTDOWN, CONGRESS, SPENDING, GOVERNMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO A SHUTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATE EYES STOPGAP\par \par \uc2 SLIDER CRIME, WARNING, AUTHORITIES, SAFETY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "SLIDER" CRIME ON THE RISE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AUTHORITIES ISSUE NEW SAFETY WARNING\par \par \uc2 "SCARCITY BRAIN", BOOK, EASTER, CRAVINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HACKING OUR "SCARCITY BRAIN"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHY WE CRAVE THINGS WE KNOW ARE BAD FOR US\par \par \uc2 CORCORAN, JOHN, "SHARK TANK", SMALL BUSINESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "SHARKS" BARBARA CORCORAN& DAYMOND JOHN LIVE!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ANSWERING YOUR SMALL BUSINESS QUESTIONS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know this morning we are swimming with the Sharks this week. They're going to take a bite out of your financial woes. This morning, days before season 15 of "Shark Tank" premieres, Barbara Corcoran and Daymond John is here to answer your small business questions. Thank you both for always coming back and blessing us on the show, 15 seasons, 15, which is absolutely amazing. What can we expect this season?\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK")\par \par \uc2 Real life, right, you're going to see people talking about AI, employer retention, the fact that they can't get money anymore because the interest rates are so high. And they all got to find a way not to deal with Kevin.\par \par \uc2 BARBARA CORCORAN ("SHARK TANK")\par \par \uc2 What I love about this season, it's going to be our best season for one reason. We have scrappy entrepreneurs. We went back to our roots, dug up the people who had nothing in their hands. They need our money. They're desperate on the show. The passion is so intense. I think we tasted everybody there. But that's why we are on this show, to find these great people, and that's what you're going to see this year.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And let's get to our viewer questions. We have videos coming in from all over the country. First up, Gladys from Minneapolis, who is worried about a possible recession.\par \par \uc2 GLADYS (VIEWER)\par \par \uc2 What are the three things every entrepreneur should know to thrive and succeed during a recession?\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK")\par \par \uc2 Well, doing businesses all around, there are a couple of fundamentals, right. The only way to operate a business, you increase sales, or you reduce cost. The only way to deal with customers is always acquire new one, upsell a current one or make one buy more frequency. In a recession, you're not going to acquire new customers, so you've got to super-size everyone's fries unless what you're selling is something that sells in a recession that's probably not your core business.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Super-size the fries.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Super-size your fries. Okay, I like that. I like that. And the next video question from Nicole, who is from San Diego. She's the founder of Sash Bag, and it's about working from home.\par \par \uc2 NICOLE (VIEWER)\par \par \uc2 I have employees that can work from home, but I feel like we're missing out on something not working together in person. How do I manage my expectations while keeping everyone collaborative and happy at work?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good question.\par \par \uc2 BARBARA CORCORAN ("SHARK TANK")\par \par \uc2 You really ought to trust your gut. You're absolutely right, there's no way to build a powerful team unless you get people together. You need to find a way, and every great entrepreneur finds an excuse to get people together. In my company, I get people to meet on retreat every quarter, and I've done that since the first day I started my job. What you should do is invite the people in for a company-wide retreat and say it's all for brainstorming. It doesn't have to be expensive, but get them together, and make sure they drink a lot and have fun.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I like the way you think.\par \par \uc2 BARBARA CORCORAN ("SHARK TANK")\par \par \uc2 It's true, true.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Nothing like that collaboration in person. All right, our next question comes from Noah from Fort Collins, Colorado, and he posted this question. When the early excitement of starting the business runs out, and motivation seems to level off, how do you maintain consumer and employee belief in your company's purpose?\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK")\par \par \uc2 You have to really check yourself. Are you really doing something you love? You should be growing with the company. If, for some reason or another, the motivation is not there, something is happening where you're more probably doing it for money. When you first started, you were probably selling 1,000 units to 1,000 people. Now you have 10,000 units, 10,000 people. You're getting a lot back. You have to find ways to grow. If you don't grow, then you're still, you know, if you're working out, you're probably still doing Jazzercize or the thigh buster, right. You got to, you got to grow with it.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You made me think of the shake weight, too.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good analogy.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The shake weight, all kinds of stuff going on there. And before we go, Barbara, you posted a lovely message about your fellow Sharks. And let's take a look at what you said to say about Daymond. You said Daymond is the family favorite. His genuine desire to uplift others is truly inspiring. He's not just a Shark, he's a mentor to friends and entrepreneurs who walk through these, those door. Plus, he has the best dance moves in the Tank.\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK")\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, we found some video. We went back, yeah.\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK")\par \par \uc2 There we go.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Daymond, what do you think about that statement?\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK")\par \par \uc2 I think that's true. Look, I think three of my co-stars were on "Dancing with the Stars," and I would smoke them at any given time if I was on there.\par \par \uc2 BARBARA CORCORAN ("SHARK TANK")\par \par \uc2 Exaggerated (inaudible), hey, he's got the moves. But I just (inaudible)...\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK")\par \par \uc2 I used to breakdance right outside here, on 42nd Street, for...\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But you know what you just did? You threw that out. You're going to be asked to do "Dancing with the Stars."\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK")\par \par \uc2 Absolutely not because it's actually hard.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I agree with you. It's a lot of work. It's really hard. But you know what? You guys work really hard, helping other people, helping them get their businesses going, giving them great advice. We always appreciate, love having you here. Swimming with the sharks is not that bad, everybody. We survived.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's right.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you can see the premiere of "Shark Tank" this Friday at 8:00 Eastern, right here on ABC. And you can also see it the next day on \uc2 Hulu\uc2 . \uc2 Mark Cuban\uc2  and Lori Greiner will be here on Thursday, answering questions about marketing your business and yourself. You can send them, you can send those questions with the #askthesharks.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231010ej9q0000m\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BIDEN TO JOIN STRIKING AUTOWORKERS PRESIDENT TRAVELS TO MICHIGAN TO JOIN PICKET LINE\b0\par\par\uc2 501 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BIDEN, \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE, BECK, HALL\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we're going to begin with President Biden. He's heading to Michigan to join striking auto workers on the picket lines this afternoon, an unprecedented show of workers solidarity by a sitting president.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN TO JOIN STRIKING AUTOWORKERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT TRAVELS TO MICHIGAN TO JOIN PICKET LINE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Senior national correspondent Terry Moran is outside a Ford plant in Michigan. Good morning, Terry.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. For decades, when workers went on strike, presidents, Republican and Democrats, tried to stay above it all, not taking sides, urging negotiations and a fair deal. But today, at this Ford plant where workers have been on strike for 11 days now for better pay and benefits, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will break that tradition.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, the President will join striking auto workers on the picket line.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 I always support the \uc2 UAW\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will be making history. There is no record of any president walking a picket line until today. But in the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  expanding strike against the big three car companies, Biden says he stands with workers.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Take a look at the significant increase in salaries for the executives and growth in the industry, they should benefit from it.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But the White House insists that the details of any deal should be left up to the parties. A week and a half into this strike, those talks are inching closer as the \uc2 UAW\uc2  fights for a 40%-wage-increase and better benefits. Democrats are increasingly competing for union votes against Republicans like \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who will address a crowd of union members on Wednesday. Out on the picket lines, workers are holding strong.\par \par \uc2 MARISA BECK (UAW MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 We're looking forward to getting something fair negotiated with Ford.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But for some, like Mac Hall and his sons Steven and Chris, two generations of auto workers on strike together, this fight is about something bigger than politics as usual.\par \par \uc2 MAC HALL (UAW MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 Personally, Biden and Trump should stay home. I think we have enough millionaires and billionaires trying to determine what we get. You don't understand.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mac Hall and his sons also tell us they are grateful for any support from any quarter. But their point is, this isn't political. For the workers, it's not about politics. It's about getting a fairer balance between workers and management at this hugely profitable companies, and not just in the auto industry. Michael?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you're right about that, Terry. It's not political. It's all about their livelihoods. Thank you so much for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231010ej9q00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BIDEN TO JOIN STRIKING AUTOWORKERS PRESIDENT TRAVELS TO MICHIGAN TO JOIN PICKET LINE\b0\par\par\uc2 558 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BIDEN, \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE, BECK, HALL\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, WGA, DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLLYWOOD ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WGA & STUDIOS REACH TENTATIVE DEAL TO END WRITERS' STRIKE\par \par \uc2 SHUTDOWN, MCCARTHY, GAETZ, COAKLEY, PRICE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO A SHUTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATE EYES STOPGAP AS HOUSE REPUBLICANS PUSH AHEAD WITH SPENDING BILLS\par \par \uc2 MENENDEZ, CORTEZ, UPTION, WILLIAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INDICTED SENATOR REFUSES TO STEP DOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW JERSEY DEMOCRAT BOB MENENDEZ VOWS TO FIGHT UPTION CHARGES\par \par \uc2 ABUSE, THOMPSON, LEE, FRAMPTON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATON ROUGE POLICE UNDER INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFICERS ACCUSED OF ABUSING DETAINEES IN A WAREHOUSE\par \par \uc2 LONG COVID, SYMPTOMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LONG COVID AFFECTING MILLIONS OF AMERICANS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CDC: NEARLY 7% OF ADULTS HAVE HAD SYMPTOMS FOR THREE MONTHS OR MORE\par \par \uc2 SALTWATER INTRUSION, WATER SUPPLY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW ORLEANS SALTWATER INTRUSION CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOUISIANA GOVERNOR REQUESTS FEDERAL EMERGENCY DECLARATION\par \par \uc2 FOOTBALL, SWIFT, \uc2 NFL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLE OF THE UNBEATENS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EAGLES DEFEAT BUCCANEERS 25-10 ON MONDAY NIGHT FOOTBALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TURBULENCE, JETBLUE, TAJER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUDDEN SEVERE TURBULENCE INJURES EIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JETBLUE FLIGHT TO FLORIDA RUNS INTO ROUGH AIR\par \par \uc2 STUDENT LOANS, SCAM, AIZPURU, TYRELL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT WARNING ABOUT STUDENT LOAN PAYMENT SCAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW CRIMINALS ARE TARGETING BORROWERS WITH THE FEDERAL PAUSE SET TO EXPIRE\par \par \uc2 PUMPKIN, MCCUAN, HUYCK, SCAVUZZO, STOCKEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DON'T BE CAUGHT OFF GOURD!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHY PUMPKINS MAY BE HARDER TO FIND & SMALLER THIS YEAR\par \par \uc2 ZACKL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ANTARCTIC SEA ICE\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE, BIDEN, FORD, PICKET LINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN TO JOIN STRIKING AUTOWORKERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT TRAVELS TO MICHIGAN TO JOIN PICKET LINE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, we're going to begin with the news, President Biden heading to Michigan to join striking auto workers on the picket lines this afternoon, an unprecedented show of worker solidarity by a sitting president. Want to go back to our senior national correspondent, Terry Moran, outside a Ford plant in Michigan. Good morning, Terry.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George, yes, on the eleventh day of the auto workers' strike, history will be made. President Biden will join striking workers on the picket line. Yeah, presidents don't normally take sides in strikes, but \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has already broken that tradition, coming out last week and declaring support for union demands in this strike and now joining workers on the picket line. There's no historical record we can fine of any president ever doing that. White House officials, however, they insist that the details will up to negotiators in these talks, and those talks are progressing, but as of now, there is no deal in sight yet. And workers are looking for that 40 percent raise. They say that tracks with what CEOs have gotten in recent years. And they're also looking for better benefits. And their cause, polls show, is broadly popular.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT ON THE PICKET LINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN TO JOIN STRIKING AUTOWORKERS ONE DAY BEFORE TRUMP'S PLANNED VISIT\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 That's one reason that Republican frontrunner \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be here on Wednesday night. He's going to give a speech to about 500 union workers and Trump supporters. And workers, however, are telling us none of this really for them is about politics. It's about fairness in their lives and in these big companies, not just the auto companies. Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231010ej9q0000i\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HOLLYWOOD ON STRIKE WGA & STUDIOS REACH TENTATIVE DEAL TO END WRITERS' STRIKE\b0\par\par\uc2 436 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BIDEN, \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE, BECK, HALL\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, WGA, DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLLYWOOD ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WGA & STUDIOS REACH TENTATIVE DEAL TO END WRITERS' STRIKE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn now to the tentative deal to end the bitter writers' strike that put Hollywood on hold for months. Kayna Whitworth is in Los Angeles with the latest for us. Good morning, Kayna.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Michael, good morning. So, today, union leadership will be voting on this deal. And if it's approved, it will then go to the more than 11,000 members of the guild.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Many of them can actually return to work in at least some capacity during this remediation process. Now, once this contract is fully approved, some of the first shows taken off the air will be among the first to return, including those late-night talk shows.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, terms of the deal are supposed to be released later today. The reported agreement includes increases in royalty payments for streaming content and guarantees that artificial intelligence will not encroach on writers' credits and compensation. I'm told the guild made huge gains in the residuals area, and that they added a bonus structure tied to subscribers of the individual streaming services. And when I asked about the studio's terms regarding AI, I was told by a source, Michael, that it was a primary ask and again they made extraordinary gains there.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Kayna, negotiations for the 65,000 film and TV actors on strike, that resumes this week as well.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WRITERS COULD SOON RETURN TO WORK BUT 65,000 ACTORS REMAIN ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Certainly, Michael. And I'm also told hat they can use this deal now as a blueprint for their own.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) I spoke with Clayton Davis, he's the chief editor at "Variety." And he said, initially, the actors in the studios weren't as far apart as the writers were. He thinks Hollywood could be back up and running in some six to eight weeks. But, Michael, overnight a potential wrinkle in all of this. The union all voting to authorize a strike against video game companies.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Michael, they're citing some of these same concerns, specifically AI.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Kayna, thank you so much. George?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231010ej9q00003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HISTORIC BIDEN VISIT TO UAW STRIKERS PRESIDENT JOINS AUTOWORKERS ON PICKET LINE\b0\par\par\uc2 575 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , FRAUD, NET WORTH, TRUMP ORGANIZATION\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , PROTESTS, BIDEN, FAIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HISTORIC BIDEN VISIT TO UAW STRIKERS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are also following the scene playing out in Michigan today. For the first time ever, a president joining the autoworkers on the picket lines.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Showing his support for striking auto workers in Michigan, President Biden today wearing a \uc2 UAW\uc2  baseball cap, saying those workers gave up a lot for the companies after the crash of 2008. And now that the companies are doing, quote, "incredibly well," the workers should, quote, "be doing incredibly well, too."\par \par \uc2 AARON KATERSKY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ABC's Terry Moran in Michigan tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT JOINS AUTOWORKERS ON PICKET LINE\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) President Biden made history today as the first president ever to walk the picket line...\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 No pay?\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 No parts.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 No pay?\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 No parts.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...in a show of solidarity with auto workers.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 You heard me say it many times, Wall Street didn't build the country, the middle class built the country. Unions built the middle class. That's the fact. So, let's keep going. You deserve what you've earned. And you've earned a hell of a lot more than you're getting paid now. Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  are fighting for expanded benefits, shorter hours, and a 40%-pay raise over the next four years, which they say matches pay raises for the car companies' CEOs. And today, the President breaking with the practice of his predecessors, openly sided with the workers.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Stick with it because you deserve the significant raise you need and other benefits.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Let's get it.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Get back what we lost, okay?\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Afterwards, we talked with Carolyn Nippa (PH), who works in inventory at the GM parts distribution facility where Biden joined the picket line.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And what does it mean that the President came here to stand with you on the picket line?\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I mean, it means a lot. I mean, I think it's going to bring a lot of attention to our cause. It's going to get the attention of the CEOs that he's here, he's with us, he's standing with us.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The \uc2 UAW\uc2  hasn't endorsed a candidate for president yet. But today, the head of the union was enthusiastically grateful.\par \par \uc2 SHAWN FAIN (PRESIDENT UNITED AUTO WORKERS)\par \par \uc2 Thank you to the President. Thank you, Mr. President, for coming. Thank you for coming to stand up with us in our generation's defining moment.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tomorrow, Republican front-runner \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be here in Michigan to give a speech to about 500 union workers and other Trump supporters at a non-union auto parts manufacturer. And while workers we talked to on the picket lines here say they appreciate support from anyone, they also say their strike isn't about politics as usual. It's about their lives. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Terry Moran in Wayne, Michigan tonight. Terry, thanks.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230929ej9q00003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HOLLYWOOD WRITERS & STUDIO REACH TENTATIVE DEAL AGREEMENT WOULD END NEARLY FIVE MONTH LONG STRIKE\b0\par\par\uc2 534 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WE HAVE A DEAL\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, WRITERS, DEAL, STUDIOS, WOLKOFF, KILKENNY\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, now can we get to the breaking news overnight, guys. All right. Hollywood writers reaching a tentative deal with the studios and streaming the services to bring an end to the months long strike. Kayna Whitworth is in Los Angeles with those details for us. Good morning there, Kayna.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLLYWOOD WRITERS & STUDIOS REACH TENTATIVE DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AGREEMENT WOULD END NEARLY FIVE MONTH LONG STRIKE\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Robin, good morning to you. So we saw marathon negotiations over the weekend. And bow the two sides reaching this tentative deal. It's a three-year contract that still has to be approved by the guild, but the picketing is suspended immediately.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, a tentative deal reached between union leaders and Hollywood studios.\par \par \uc2 BILL WOLKOFF (STRIKE CAPTAIN/LOT COORDINATOR/TV WRITER)\par \par \uc2 I've been crying for the last 15 minutes. My phone has been blowing up. I just feel indescribable joy.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The agreement coming just five days shy of what would have been the longest Hollywood strike in more than 70 years. The Writers Guild of America touting solidarity in an email to members and thanking other union members for their "Extraordinary support on the picket lines for over 146 days."\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And while terms of the deal have yet to be made public, "\uc2 The New York Times\uc2 " reporting the agreement contains most of what was demanded by the union, including "Increases in royalty payments for streaming content and guarantees that artificial intelligence will not encroach on the writers' credits and compensation."\par \par \uc2 BILL WOLKOFF (STRIKE CAPTAIN/LOT COORDINATOR/TV WRITER)\par \par \uc2 It has been described as exemplary in all areas. We can all just celebrate and know that we have something is going to create transformative change for our business.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLLYWOOD WRITERS & STUDIOS REACH TENTATIVE DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT COMES NEXT & WHAT IT COULD MEAN FOR STRIKING ACTORS\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The WGA saying, "We can say with great pride that this deal is exceptional, with meaningful gains and protections for writers in every sector of the membership." But even if the writers' strike officially ends, don't expect work on TV and movie sets to instantly resume. Actors remain on strike. \uc2 SAG\uc2 /\uc2 AFTRA\uc2  releasing a statement congratulating the WGA, adding, "We remain committed to achieving the necessary terms for our members."\par \par \uc2 KATIE KILKENNY (LABOR & MEDIA REPORTER "THE HOLLYWOOD REPORTER")\par \par \uc2 It'll take at least six weeks to get up and running on scripted TV. SAG/\uc2 AFTRA\uc2  need to resolve their own negotiations before new television can be produced, which is a big hurdle here to get back to normal.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now Los Angeles Mayor Karen Bass weighing in, saying, now is time to focus on getting the entertainment industry and all the other businesses that rely on it back on their feet. So, George, it's certainly not over yet, but there is momentum here.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231009ej9p0008e\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 08:00 HALF-HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 445 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WE HAVE A DEAL\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, WRITERS, DEAL, STUDIOS, WOLKOFF, KILKENNY\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE, AUTOMAKERS, NEGOTIATIONS\par \par \uc2 OPHELIA, RAIN, WINDS, SURF, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 OPHELIA, RAIN, FLOODING, STORM, HAIL\par \par \uc2 POLL, BIDEN, ECONOMY, IMMIGRATION, TRUMP\par \par \uc2 REPUBLICANS, 2024, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, HOUSE\par \par \uc2 BORDER, MIGRANTS, CRISIS, LEE, OWENS\par \par \uc2 NFL\uc2 , DOLPHINS, SCORE, CHIEFS, SWIFT, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR WESTERN STORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 BRAWL, RIVERFRONT, PICKETT, CARLTON, HAMILTON-RUDOLPH\par \par \uc2 UNCLAIMED, CASH, TEXAS, HEGAR, RESIDENTS\par \par \uc2 USHER, SUPER BOWL, HALFTIME, HEADLINER\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. It's 8:00 AM.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING OVERNIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE "WRITE" DEAL\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Breaking overnight, we have a deal in the writers' strike. Hollywood writers reaching a tentative agreement with studios to end the nearly five-month strike. Now, what it could mean for actors.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AI PACKAGE PROTECTION?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLING PORCH PIRATES\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Battling porch pirates. The new high-tech tools, including artificial intelligence. The top delivery companies and retailers are using to help keep your home deliveries safe.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ULTIMATE GIFT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MODERN FAMILY\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The best friends giving the word family a whole new meaning. How they helped give each other their dreams.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KERRY WSHINGTON!\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Kerry Washington live in Times Square. What you didn't see in our special conversation last night. Are you ready?\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON (AUTHOR "THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 I don't know.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Kerry's live on "GMA" ahead of the release of her new book.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TAYLOR SWIFT & TRAVIS KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOVE STORY?\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Taylor Swift is going red, rooting on the \uc2 Kansas City Chiefs\uc2 . We'll have more details in "Pop News."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 ROBERT HERJAVEC\uc2  LIVE!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWIMMING WITH THE SHARKS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And get ready. We're swimming with the "Sharks" this week. They're sinking their teeth into your money questions. This morning, \uc2 Robert Herjavec\uc2  is here live tackling your debt. And he's saying...\par \par \uc2 ROBERT HERJAVEC\uc2  ("SHARK TANK")\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in Times Square, this is "GMA."\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 You just heard from Robert. He is here to kick off "GMA's" version of shark week, answering your questions about student loans, credit card debt, and how to be smart about mortgage payments. He'll also tell you about the new season of "Shark Tank" coming up.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And Dr. Jen Ashton is here to tell us about a new CDC approval of an RSV vaccine for pregnant women that can help protect newborns. That's just ahead.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231009ej9p0008r\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CRACKING DOWN ON PORCH PIRATES UPS USING AI TO HELP PROTECT YOUR PACKAGES\b0\par\par\uc2 652 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WE HAVE A DEAL\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, WRITERS, DEAL, STUDIOS, WOLKOFF, KILKENNY\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE, AUTOMAKERS, NEGOTIATIONS\par \par \uc2 OPHELIA, RAIN, WINDS, SURF, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 OPHELIA, RAIN, FLOODING, STORM, HAIL\par \par \uc2 POLL, BIDEN, ECONOMY, IMMIGRATION, TRUMP\par \par \uc2 REPUBLICANS, 2024, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, HOUSE\par \par \uc2 BORDER, MIGRANTS, CRISIS, LEE, OWENS\par \par \uc2 NFL\uc2 , DOLPHINS, SCORE, CHIEFS, SWIFT, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR WESTERN STORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 BRAWL, RIVERFRONT, PICKETT, CARLTON, HAMILTON-RUDOLPH\par \par \uc2 UNCLAIMED, CASH, TEXAS, HEGAR, RESIDENTS\par \par \uc2 USHER, SUPER BOWL, HALFTIME, HEADLINER\par \par \uc2 WGA, STRIKE, DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLLYWOOD WRITERS & STUDIOS REACH TENTATIVE DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AGREEMENT WOULD END NEARLY FIVE-MONTH LONG STRIKE\par \par \uc2 SALTWATER, EDWARDS, WATER SUPPLY, DROUGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW ORLEANS WATER CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SALTWATER IN MISSISSIPPI RIVER THREATENS SUPPLY IN SOUTHERN LOUISIANA\par \par \uc2 RSV, VACCINE, PREGNANCY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CDC RECOMMENDS RSV VACCINE FOR PREGNANT WOMEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT GETTING THE SHOT\par \par \uc2 PORCH PIRATE, AI, ROBINSON, STICKLE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A rainy, rainy Monday morning here in Times Square. But we are back with our "GMA Cover Story," the fight against porch pirates.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CRACKING DOWN ON PORCH PIRATES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UPS USING A.I. TO HELP PROTECT YOUR PACKAGES\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) UPS now using artificial intelligence to stop them from stealing your home deliveries. Eva Pilgrim is here with that story for us. Good morning, Eva.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Robin. It's a real problem. The number of stolen packages is up. And an expert telling us, after the pandemic, we got so used to getting deliveries that we're now ordering more items and more valuable items, making your front porch a prime target for thieves.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, thieves hoping to steel packages from your front door better beware. There's a new tool to keep an eye on would-be porch pirates, Artificial intelligence. \uc2 UPS Capital\uc2  introducing Delivery Defense, machine learning algorithms that assign a confidence score at potential delivery locations to help determine how likely a package is to get where it needs to be without being lost or stolen.\par \par \uc2 MARK ROBINSON (PRESIDENT \uc2 UPS CAPITAL\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 UPS has one of the largest delivery databases in the world. And we're using machine learning and AI tools to look at all this delivery information. We have the address confidence score from 1 to 1,000. So, 1,000 would be an absolute highest confidence that a package would be delivered successfully and 1 would be lower-dose confidence. And so, there's other choices that we can help merchants to use that increase the chance of successful delivery.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A beta test of delivery defense underway by \uc2 Costco Wholesale\uc2  in Colorado. But UPS is not alone in using technology to help prevent porch piracy.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DELIVERY TRACKING FEATURES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW COMPANIES ARE USING TECHNOLOGY TO REDUCE THEFT\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 FedEx\uc2  allows customers to customize their delivery location and time through their mobile app. And \uc2 Amazon\uc2  offering a map-tracking feature that allows customers to see the progress of their delivery in real time.\par \par \uc2 BEN STICKLE (PROFESSOR OF CRIMINAL JUSTICE ADMINISTRATION)\par \par \uc2 Porch piracy has been around for a few years. The real key to preventing package theft is removing the opportunity. So, if we can identify a house or a neighborhood that's at high risk for package theft, then it seems like a win-win for everybody. The delivery service gets the delivery the first time and you get your package.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, so here's the deal. If you have a package you really want to make sure you get, you have two good options. Make sure you're home or have it delivered somewhere with an attendant that you can pick up later. George and Linsey?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, Eva.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231009ej9p0008v\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ROUNDING UP UNCLAIMED CASH IN TEXAS "GMA" HELPS FANS FIND MONEY THEY'RE OWED IN THE LONE STAR STATE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,268 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WE HAVE A DEAL\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, WRITERS, DEAL, STUDIOS, WOLKOFF, KILKENNY\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE, AUTOMAKERS, NEGOTIATIONS\par \par \uc2 OPHELIA, RAIN, WINDS, SURF, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 OPHELIA, RAIN, FLOODING, STORM, HAIL\par \par \uc2 POLL, BIDEN, ECONOMY, IMMIGRATION, TRUMP\par \par \uc2 REPUBLICANS, 2024, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, HOUSE\par \par \uc2 BORDER, MIGRANTS, CRISIS, LEE, OWENS\par \par \uc2 NFL\uc2 , DOLPHINS, SCORE, CHIEFS, SWIFT, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR WESTERN STORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 BRAWL, RIVERFRONT, PICKETT, CARLTON, HAMILTON-RUDOLPH\par \par \uc2 UNCLAIMED, CASH, TEXAS, HEGAR, RESIDENTS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back with or series "Show Me The Money," we're helping people across the country find unclaimed cash. Gio Benitez in Texas for the latest stop. How'd it go, Gio?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ROUNDING UP UNCLAIMED CASH IN TEXAS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "GMA" HELPS FANS FIND MONEY THEY'RE OWED IN THE LONE STAR STATE\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, it went really well, George. I love that music. We are talking about real money here. In the 24 hours after our story aired last week, so many people in Florida alone, they went online and claimed nearly $4 million. It is a stunning number, and it shows how much of your money is out there just waiting for you. So this week we're going to Texas, while making money can sometimes feel like the wild west, getting this cash is no showdown.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We're back in our "GMA" "Show Me The Money" mobile driving through the lone star state towards the historic Ft. Worth Stock Yards, famous for its twice daily longhorn cattle drives and, as I learned, friendly livestock.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, they're ready. They're looking for some cash. It's time for "Show Me The Money," Texas style.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But first, I need to look the part.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So we're looking for a hat. This is my first hat. I want one that screams money. Yes.\par \par \uc2 STORE OWNER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 That hat will start off around 3,500 bucks.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, this is $3,500?\par \par \uc2 STORE OWNER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, it screams money.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It does scream money. Wow. Okay, so I think we need something a little cheaper than that. This one feels just right. All right, so we got the hat, now let's get some cash.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Yes, the perfect place to saddle up and mine for some of that Texas gold.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's find some big bucks.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Outside the famous Cow Town Coliseum we set up our "GMA" "Show Me The Money" booth, roping in members of the Texas comptroller's office to look up names and see how much unclaimed money they can wrangle up for these Texans.\par \par \uc2 TEXAS RESIDENT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 The state comptroller just found $217 for me. Yee-haw. Show me the money.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And of course when they do, they get to ring that bell. And despite what some may think, having unclaimed money doesn't always mean you did something wrong or lost the reins of your finances. In Texas, for example, some of the top sources include uncashed paychecks that simply could have gotten lost in the mail. Unused gift cards or insurance claims, sometimes from a deceased loved one, that turns out may go to you.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) By law if this money isn't claimed, typically within three years, companies are required to turn it over to state offices where it gets listed online. In Texas, where there's $8.1 billion stocked up, residents can search for their name on the government website claimittexas.gov.\par \par \uc2 GLENN HEGAR (TEXAS COMPTROLLER OF PUBLIC ACCOUNTS)\par \par \uc2 People come up to me all the time a say, oh my gosh I did not know I had $100, I have $1,000, I have $2,500. So it's really exciting to be able to return money back to the people in the state of Texas.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And just like that, the very first name we look up, $383. Part of that money, a refund from his utility company.\par \par \uc2 TEXAS RESIDENT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 This made my day. I wasn't expecting this at all.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) That gentleman, so impressed with how easy it was, he brought his mom down, and she got 363 bucks. That from a long forgotten old bank account. And there seems to be something about camera crews, these two lassoing a combined 159 big ones.\par \par \uc2 TEXAS RESIDENT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 What? Show me the money.\par \par \uc2 TEXAS RESIDENT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I saw your story last week on "Good Morning America," ran my name through the system, found over $200 for myself. Ran my deceased father's name from an out of state address and found over $400 in his name.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow. So now that's over 600 bucks.\par \par \uc2 TEXAS RESIDENT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 That's right.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But our biggest hat tip going to this woman who found more than $3,000 from an old retirement account. She tells us she's heard of unclaimed money before and thought it was a scam. But now she knows the ones who write checks like this are straight shooters.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This really is a big check, $3,167. We knew they had cattle here, but not cash cattle.\par \par \uc2 TEXAS RESIDENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Show me the money.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So we wrangled up some big bucks here in Ft. Worth. Now it's on to our next show me the money city. See y'all later.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) See, I got real cheesy. Just last year the state of Texas returned 344 million bucks to its residents. And across the country we're talking about billions of dollar. And I know this feels like a scam, but getting this money back is actually part of the law. You can go to missingmoney.com to see what's out there for you.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But a word of caution here, there are some websites out there that offer to find this money for you but they want to charge you a percentage of the earnings. You do not need to pay for anything, this is free. Just make sure you are using missingmoney.com or your state's official website. Guys.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is so important. Are you going to put the hat on? That's not the $3,500 one?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, no, definitely not.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You could not expense that one. Yeah. You're looking good. Looking good, partner.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Looking very Dallas.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You can scan the QR code on your screen right now or go to our website for more information on getting your money.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWIMMING WITH THE SHARKS\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, coming up, we are kicking off our swimming with the sharks week with \uc2 Robert Herjavec\uc2 , answering your questions about dealing with debt.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HALFTIME HYPE\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And next, OMG, it's our "Play of the Day." What we know about Usher and the Super Bowl halftime show.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Usher?\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Ursher, baby.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231009ej9p0008p\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HOLLYWOOD WRITERS & STUDIOS REACH TENTATIVE DEAL AGREEMENT WOULD END NEARLY FIVE-MONTH LONG STRIKE\b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WE HAVE A DEAL\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, WRITERS, DEAL, STUDIOS, WOLKOFF, KILKENNY\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE, AUTOMAKERS, NEGOTIATIONS\par \par \uc2 OPHELIA, RAIN, WINDS, SURF, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 OPHELIA, RAIN, FLOODING, STORM, HAIL\par \par \uc2 POLL, BIDEN, ECONOMY, IMMIGRATION, TRUMP\par \par \uc2 REPUBLICANS, 2024, TRUMP, SHUTDOWN, HOUSE\par \par \uc2 BORDER, MIGRANTS, CRISIS, LEE, OWENS\par \par \uc2 NFL\uc2 , DOLPHINS, SCORE, CHIEFS, SWIFT, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR WESTERN STORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 BRAWL, RIVERFRONT, PICKETT, CARLTON, HAMILTON-RUDOLPH\par \par \uc2 UNCLAIMED, CASH, TEXAS, HEGAR, RESIDENTS\par \par \uc2 USHER, SUPER BOWL, HALFTIME, HEADLINER\par \par \uc2 WGA, STRIKE, DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLLYWOOD WRITERS & STUDIOS REACH TENTATIVE DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AGREEMENT WOULD END NEARLY FIVE-MONTH LONG STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) First, the breaking news overnight, Hollywood writers reach a tentative deal with studios and streaming services to bring an end to the months-long strike. We're going to go back to Kayna Whitworth in Los Angeles. Good morning, Kayna.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning to you, George. So, the Writers' Guild saying they are full of pride, adding that this deal has meaningful gains. And while they are still in the approval process, the picketing has been suspended immediately. Now, the exact details of this tentative deal have not been made public yet.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENTATIVE DEAL\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But the WGA reporting they've made progress on viewership residual payments for writers, minimum staffing guarantees on shows and protections around the use of artificial intelligence. Now, the Writers Guild of America touting solidarity in an email to members and thanking other union members for their extraordinary support on the picket lines over 146 days. Now, actors remain on strike.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT COMES NEXT & WHAT IT COULD MEAN FOR STRIKING ACTORS\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  releasing a statement, congratulating the WGA but adding, "We remain committed to achieving the necessary terms for our members." So, Robin, while nobody is back to work just yet, there is certainly momentum out here in Hollywood.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely. Kayna, great news. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231009ej9p0008s\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AUTOWORKERS STRIKE EXPANDS NEW PICKETS AT 38 GM & STELLANTIS OPERATED PARTS CENTERS\b0\par\par\uc2 343 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WE HAVE A DEAL\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, WRITERS, DEAL, STUDIOS, WOLKOFF, KILKENNY\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE, AUTOMAKERS, NEGOTIATIONS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There sure is. Okay, Kayna, thanks very much. There's no momentum it appears for the autoworkers strike. The \uc2 UAW\uc2  has expanded walkouts against two of the big three automakers. President Biden is going to join the picket line tomorrow. Senior national correspondent Terry Moran reports from Wayne, Michigan. Good morning, Terry.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AUTOWORKERS STRIKE EXPANDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW PICKETS AT 38 GM & STELLANTIS OPERATED PARTS CENTERS\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. It's an extraordinary week here. Day 10 of this strike. As you say, President Biden, both presidential frontrunners are going to be here to stand with striking autoworkers. Biden's coming tomorrow and he'll be on the picket line. A President on the picket line. That's something no President has done in living memory.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , he'll be here Wednesday to give a speech to about 500 union workers and other supporters. That's a sign of how much the Republican Party has changed under Trump. And out here on the picket line, it's not about politics, they don't want to talk about politics, they're hoping for progress. And there's been some, but no real sign of a resolution yet.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Negotiations continued over the weekend, with Ford and the \uc2 UAW\uc2  reporting positive movement. But Ford issuing a statement last night saying, quote, "Significant gaps remain." As for \uc2 GM\uc2  and Chrysler's \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , it's a different story. The \uc2 UAW\uc2  expanding strikes to 38 new locations against those companies.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) 6,000 more workers out on strike at parts and distribution centers across 20 states. And that could impact consumers soon. Getting your car repaired or serviced, well, that could take longer and cost more as this strike goes on. Linsey.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231009ej9p0008f\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TENTATIVE DEAL IN WRITERS' STRIKE MAY CLEAR WAY FOR STRIKE BY ACTORS TO END\b0\par\par\uc2 414 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MENENDEZ, WILLIAMS, UPTION, INDICTMENT\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TROPICAL STORM OPHELIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAINS AND FLOODING\par \par \uc2 TURBULENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGERS HURT AFTER SEVERE TURBULENCE\par \par \uc2 FENTANYL, WILLIAMS, MANHUNT, ARRESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW SURVEILLANCE IN DAY CARE PROBE\par \par \uc2 SHUTDOWN, MCCARTHY, PRICE, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTING DOWN TO SHUTDOWN\par \par \uc2 DEAL, PROTESTS, WGA, DAVIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENTATIVE DEAL IN WRITERS' STRIKE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next, tonight here, we continue to report on this major breakthrough on the picket lines. Hollywood writers reaching a tentative deal with studios to end the nearly five-month walkout. Tonight here, what this could now mean for actors who are also still on strike. Here's ABC's Kayna Whitworth for us.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAY CLEAR WAY FOR STRIKE BY ACTORS TO END\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, after one of the longest strikes in Hollywood history, writers and studios reaching a tentative agreement, bringing the entertainment industry one step closer to getting back to business.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 If we don't' get it?\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Shut it down.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Neither side has released details, but the WGA says the deal is "exceptional with meaningful gains and protections for writers in every sector of the membership."\par \par \uc2 CLAYTON DAVIS (SENIOR AWARDS EDITOR "VARIETY")\par \par \uc2 They had most of their areas of concern addressed by the studios. One, AI. They have some protections in place that will ensure writers have a future in this industry. The second is residuals. They got a huge bump in residuals in addition to a new bonus structure.\par \par \uc2 JIMMY KIMMEL\uc2  (HOST "JIMMY KIMMEL LIVE")\par \par \uc2 Thank you for watching.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Writers on talk shows could soon return to work. But most TV and film production is on hold while the actors' union, \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 , remains on strike with no talks scheduled.\par \par \uc2 CLAYTON DAVIS (SENIOR AWARDS EDITOR "VARIETY")\par \par \uc2 You can't give actors something that you didn't give the writers. So, I think this is the blueprint that they're going to present to the \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  membership.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, David, union leadership will vote on this deal tomorrow. If it's approved, it will then go to the more than 11,000 members of the Writers Guild. Many of them will be able to return to work before the deal is fully ratified. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Kayna Whitworth reporting from Los Angeles. Kayna, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230927ej9p00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 UAW STRIKE EXPANDS TO DISTRIBUTION CENTERS 38 SITES OWNED BY \uc2 GM\uc2  AND \uc2 STELLANTIS\uc2  TARGETED BY UNION\b0\par\par\uc2 524 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OPHELIA'S REMNANTS DRENCH EAST COAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DESTRUCTIVE STORM\par \par \uc2 TRACK, O'NEAL, ETTORE, TROPICAL STORM OPHELIA, STORM\par \par \uc2 DEAL, WGA, KILKENNY, GILDAY, SEPTIEN, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORTS: WRITERS GUILD AND STUDIOS NEAR DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COULD END FIVE-MONTH WALKOUT BY HOLLYWOOD WRITERS\par \par \uc2 IMMIGRATION, RODRIGUES, LEESER, OWENS\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , PROTEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UAW STRIKE EXPANDS TO DISTRIBUTION CENTERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 38 SITES OWNED BY \uc2 GM\uc2  AND \uc2 STELLANTIS\uc2  TARGETED BY UNION\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) For now, though, we do turn to the autoworkers strike widening to some parts distributors and what that could mean if you need to get your car repaired. ABC's Melissa Adan joins us now from a \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  facility here in New York. Good morning to you, Melissa.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Janai. You can see some of the picketers here behind me this morning and we're at a key site. This is a plant distribution site here in Rockland County, New York, and it's so critical when we're talking about the strike and what this plant offers. I mean, they supply dealerships.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) So, this is key if you're trying to get a certain part to your automaker, you could possibly see a delay. And it's also going to be hitting \uc2 GM\uc2  right in their pockets. That's another thing here because this is one of the most profitable parts of the auto business as selling repair parts and service returns makes up 40% of their profits. Now the strike expanding over the weekend to now 38 \uc2 GM\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  parts distribution sites in 20 states across the country. This, of course, as the \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  remains steadfast in their demands of higher wages and stronger benefits.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UAW STRIKE EXPANDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNION PRESIDENT SAYS THEY ARE MAKING PROGRESS WITH FORD\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, the union president coming in and saying they are making progress with Ford. He's saying the automaker's showing that they're serious about reaching a deal. In a statement, Ford saying there are still significant gaps to close on the key economic issues. But workers say when it comes to \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and \uc2 GM\uc2 , that they have not gone far enough with their offers. \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  issuing a statement saying that it questions if the union's leadership wants to reach an agreement in a timely manner. Well, in any case, President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is expected to join the picket lines in Michigan come Tuesday, announcing his solidarity with the union. And, of course, all of this coming with those concerns when you talk about car shoppers heading out to maybe your auto repair shop.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You might start seeing those direct trickle-down effects anytime now within the next couple of weeks that this all keeps going. And, of course, the other people deeply impacted by this, those picketers and their families. Gio?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, an incredibly sequential strike there. Melissa, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231009ej9o0002x\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 REPORTS: WRITERS GUILD AND STUDIOS NEAR DEAL COULD END FIVE-MONTH WALKOUT BY HOLLYWOOD WRITERS\b0\par\par\uc2 518 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OPHELIA'S REMNANTS DRENCH EAST COAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DESTRUCTIVE STORM\par \par \uc2 TRACK, O'NEAL, ETTORE, TROPICAL STORM OPHELIA, STORM\par \par \uc2 DEAL, WGA, KILKENNY, GILDAY, SEPTIEN, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORTS: WRITERS GUILD AND STUDIOS NEAR DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COULD END FIVE-MONTH WALKOUT BY HOLLYWOOD WRITERS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn now to breaking news overnight, and reports Hollywood writers may be close to a deal to end their five-month walkout. ABC's Jaclyn Lee joins us now from Los Angeles with the latest. Good morning to you, Jaclyn.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Gio, good morning to you. Look, everyone wants some sort of resolution for this. And now, it looks like they are one step closer.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The strike that has left Hollywood paralyzed for nearly five months may finally be coming to an end. According to "The Hollywood Reporter," the Writers Guild of America and the \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2  concluded a full day of negotiations with attorneys reviewing the studios' so-called best and final offer.\par \par \uc2 KATIE KILKENNY (LABOR & MEDIA REPORTER "THE HOLLYWOOD REPORTER")\par \par \uc2 Everybody's on pins and needles to see how this is actually going to resolve, if this actually means the end of the strike. So, it's a big moment in Hollywood.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) According to multiple media reports, the offer made Saturday suggested that studios had taken steps in areas pertaining to residuals, minimum staffing, AI, and data transparency, all key facets of the Writers' Guild's agenda. More than 11,000 members of the WGA on strike for nearly five months, a near record amount of time over issues including pay, the size of writing staffs, and restrictions on the use of AI.\par \par \uc2 AL SEPTIEN (FILM PRODUCER AND WGA MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 What I hope is we get a fair contract. We've been out here a long time.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  joined the writers' strike in July still with no sign of resolution. As a result, movie releases have been delayed.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "DUNE: PART TWO"\par \par \uc2 TIMOTHEE CHALAMET (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 May thy knife chip and shatter.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And filming on several productions has been paused. Actors and supporters walking the picket lines. More determined than ever to get more compensation as streaming grows in popularity. The economic impact being felt outside of the guilds. Experts estimating the WGA and SGA strikes have cost California $3 billion. Some industry workers resorting to selling items at a local flea market to make ends meet while their productions are on pause.\par \par \uc2 GREG S GILDAY (PROP MAKER)\par \par \uc2 Anybody who could say they were out of work because of the film industry shutting down was in.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And overnight, the two sides releasing a joint statement confirming they met for bargaining on Saturday, and will meet again on Sunday. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is encouraging. Jaclyn, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231009ej9o0002v\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 REPORTS: WRITERS' STRIKE TALKS IN "HOMESTRETCH" STUDIOS: "BEST AND FINAL" OFFER ON THE TABLE\b0\par\par\uc2 403 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Sunday\par \uc2 WNSU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, OPHELIA, RAIN, WINDS, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE STORM DRENCHES EAST COAST\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, HAIL, THUNDER\par \par \uc2 SHUTDOWN, GOVERNMENT, REPUBLICANS, HOUSE, BIDEN, POLL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOVERNMENT SHUTDOWN SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, WRITERS, STUDIOS, NEGOTIATIONS, OFFER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORTS: WRITERS' STRIKE TALKS IN "HOMESTRETCH"\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) MaryAlice for us, thanks so much. We turn now to Hollywood where striking writers and studios are back at the bargaining table for a fifth straight day, with talks said to be in the home stretch. The two sides are trying to reach an agreement to end the nearly five-month long walkout by the writers, which has stymied production in Hollywood. A resolution would also put pressure on studios to reach an agreement with the SAG-AFTRA Actor's Union. ABC's Jaclyn Lee has the latest.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORTS: WRITERS' STRIKE TALKS IN "HOMESTRETCH"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDIOS: "BEST AND FINAL" OFFER ON THE TABLE\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE ( ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) With Hollywood paralyzed and production at a standstill amid ongoing talks today, there are reports of major progress between the Writers Guild of America and the studios. After a marathon four days of negotiations "Deadline" reports that attorneys for the WGA are reviewing the studio's reported best and final offer for a new three-year contract.\par \par \uc2 WRITER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 We know that our negotiating committee is not going to accept a deal that's subpar, because we trust them and they have led us through this strike.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE ( ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Multiple media reports suggest the studios may be compromising in areas related to minimum staffing, residuals, artificial intelligence and data transparency. If the two sides come to a resolution viewers would likely see the return of late night and day time talk shows, but absent Hollywood's biggest stars because the actor's union has not reached a deal.\par \par \uc2 WRITER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 What I hope it that we get a fair contract. We've been out here a long time. We don't want to fold for a less than fair and good contract for the writers.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE ( ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Linsey, any agreement made still needs to be ratified by the 11,000 members of the Writers Guild. And this writers' strike is reaching a record length. If it hits September 30th, it will officially be the longest strike in the union's history. Linsey.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSU000020230927ej9o00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PRESIDENT TO JOIN THE PICKET LINE BIDEN WILL STAND IN SOLIDARITY WITH STRIKING \uc2 UAW\uc2  WORKERS\b0\par\par\uc2 562 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS: OPHELIA'S LANDFALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TROPICAL STORM COMES ASHORE\par \par \uc2 OPHELIA, STORM, FLOODING, WINDS, NORTH CAROLINA, VIRGINIA\par \par \uc2 OPHELIA, STORM, SURGE, FLOODING, WIND\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE, AUTOWORKERS, NAPIORKO, FAIN, DAWSON\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the historic autoworkers strike expanding to more locations as President Biden accepts the \uc2 UAW\uc2 's invitation, saying he will join striking workers on the picket lines. ABC's Faith Abubey is in Wayne, Michigan with the latest on the President's support and the ongoing negotiations. Faith, good morning.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Whit. The fallout from the strike could be devastating. Some analysts already saying consumers who need car repairs at dealerships and service centers could start feeling the impact in just a matter of weeks.\par \par \uc2 STRIKER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 We are the union.\par \par \uc2 STRIKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 We are the union.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT SAYS HE WILL JOIN UAW PICKET LINE. AUTOWORKERS EXPAND STRIKE TO 38 FACILITIES IN 20 STATES\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  back on the picket lines as President Biden prepares to join the striking workers in solidarity next week. Friday, the union expanding their targeted strike, asking workers at 38 \uc2 GM\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  parts distribution facilities in 20 states from California to Florida to walk off of the job after a stalemate with the two automakers.\par \par \uc2 LUCAS NAPIORKO (AUTOWORKER ON STRIKE)\par \par \uc2 It's going to not only affect the company and all of us workers that are going to be on $500 a week, but it's also going to affect the consumer, the customers who will be waiting for car parts to get their cars fixed and they're going to be sitting.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In a statement, \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  saying it will continue to bargain in good faith and that the company presented a competitive offer, but the union never responded. Ford notably not affected by the strike expansion. Uaw President, Shawn Fain saying the automaker made some progress in critical areas like cost of living increases, profit sharing, and job security during layoffs.\par \par \uc2 SHAWN FAIN (PRESIDENT UNITED AUTO WORKERS)\par \par \uc2 We want to recognize that Ford is showing that they are serious about reaching a deal.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Still, Ford saying, quote, "We have more work ahead of us before we can reach an agreement." The workers are asking the automakers for, among other things, a 40 percent pay raise over four years, a four-day work week, and job security. Brandon Dawson works at the \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  parts distribution plant in Romulus, Michigan and says he didn't want to go on strike, but understands that he had to.\par \par \uc2 BRANDON DAWSON (AUTOWORKER ON STRIKE)\par \par \uc2 I'm a single parent. I had to raise my daughter working a shift from 5:00 PM to 4:00 AM. It's not fair and it's really corporate greed. They are making the money, they can pay us.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Gio, the White House says President Biden will touch down here in Michigan to stand with the striking workers on Tuesday. Gio.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, that'll put the President right in the middle of that dispute. All right, Faith, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231009ej9n00004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AUTOWORKERS SET TO EXPAND STRIKE \uc2 UAW\uc2  PROMISES MORE WALKOUTS AS NOON DEADLINE NEARS\b0\par\par\uc2 343 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHAOS ON CAPITOL HILL\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY, REPUBLICANS, CHAOS, DEADLINE\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, WINDS, FLOODING, SURGE\par \par \uc2 BORDER, MIGRANTS, SPIKE, PATROL, CRISIS\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE, AUTOMAKERS, DEADLINE, WORKERS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Okay, Matt, thanks very much. Now to that new deadline in the auto workers strike, union promising to expand their walkouts against the big three automakers unless there is serious progress at the negotiating table by Noon. Faith Abubey is in Detroit with the latest. Good morning, Faith.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AUTOWORKERS SET TO EXPAND STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 UAW\uc2  PROMISES MORE WALKOUTS AS NOON DEADLINE NEARS\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, George. A week into this unprecedented strike, and there are no signs, no clear signs that this is moving closer to an end. In fact, you can see the auto workers still picketing behind me, and the union is now poised to dial up the pressure in just a matter of hours if they don't see serious progress in these negotiations.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now just a reminder of what we are doing here, the union demands among other things, includes 40% pay increase and a four day work week. The automakers on the other hand, have offered a 20% pay raise and haven't really bugged on shrinking the work week right now. They have made some concessions, but the \uc2 UAW\uc2  President Shawn Fain has signaled that they are running out of patience.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They're giving Ford, \uc2 GM\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  until Noon today to move closer to meeting their demands, otherwise they plan to expand the strike from one plant at each of the big three automakers to more plants across the country, potentially crippling the supply chain.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The bottom line here is that the clock is clicking towards that Noon deadline. The two sides remain far apart, and there are major, major concerns about the potential impact on the US economy. Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231006ej9m0002x\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 UAW\uc2  EXPANDS AUTO STRIKE UNION TARGETS 38 GM & STELLANTIS FACILITIES, SPARES FORD\b0\par\par\uc2 502 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TROPICAL STORM OPHELIA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, TROPICAL STORM OPHELIA\par \par \uc2 MENENDEZ, WILLIAMS, UPTION, INDICTMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRIBERY CHARGES AGAINST SEN. MENENDEZ\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, PROTEST, \uc2 UAW\uc2 , FAIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 UAW\uc2  EXPANDS AUTO STRIKE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There is another developing headline tonight. A short time ago, President Biden revealing he will walk with the auto workers in Michigan amid a major expansion of the strike. Tonight, workers walking out at 38 facilities that distribute to auto parts from California to Florida. Tonight, why they're so angry with \uc2 GM\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and the progress they say they're making with Ford. ABC's Faith Abubey in Wayne, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNION TARGETS 38 GM & STELLANTIS FACILITIES, SPARES FORD\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, President Biden announcing he will join auto workers on the picket lines in Michigan next week, just as the union ramps up its pressure on \uc2 GM\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 No pay.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 No parts.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The \uc2 UAW\uc2  expanding its strike to all 38 parts distribution facilities across 20 states, from California to Florida.\par \par \uc2 SHAWN FAIN (PRESIDENT UNITED AUTO WORKERS)\par \par \uc2 We will shut down parts distribution until those two companies come to their senses and come to the table with a serious offer.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A week into the strike, 5,600 more auto workers today walking off jobs critical to the nation's supply of car parts. At this \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  plant outside Detroit, workers like Brandon Dawson tell me they're staying on the picket lines until there is a fair contract, but he warns consumers could feel the impact of today's walkout.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 The customer is directly impacted right here. You might need some windshield wipers. They're not going to be coming because we pick the parts that get them there.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And what do you say to those consumers who may not be able to get repairs or parts they need?\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I'm sorry to the consumers. I mean, I know it's not their fault, but it's really corporate greed. They're making the money. They can pay us.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Auto workers are still pushing all three companies for that 40% pay over four years. But for now, the union says it's not expanding its strike against Ford, saying talks with the automaker show progress on issues like cost-of-living increases, profit sharing and job security during layoffs.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, David, President Biden says he'll stand in solidarity with these union workers right here in Michigan next week and call for a deal that keeps the auto industry thriving with union jobs. Not since Teddy Roosevelt invited coal workers to the White House have we seen a president show such support for striking workers. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Faith Abubey in Michigan tonight. Faith, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230926ej9m00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TALKS RESUME IN WRITERS' STRIKE UNION & STUDIOS TO MEET AGAIN AFTER DAY OF NEGOTIATING\b0\par\par\uc2 543 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 IMMIGRATION, CRISIS, DESMOND, ZELENSKYY, DESANTIS\par \par \uc2 WAR, UKRAINE, RUSSIA, AIRSTRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RUSSIA LAUNCHES DEVASTATING NEW ATTACKS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST FIVE UKRAINIAN CITIES TARGETED BY MISSILE STRIKES\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, MASON, FORESTAL, HOLLAND, CAVALCANTE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT MANHUNT FOR ACCUSED MURDERER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUSPECT MISTAKENLY RELEASED FROM INDIANA JAIL DUE TO CLERICAL ERROR\par \par \uc2 FENTANYL, MANHUNT, O'SULLIVAN, MENDEZ, DAY CARE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY DAY CARE OVERDOSE INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE URGENTLY SEARCHING FOR HUSBAND OF DAY CARE OWNER\par \par \uc2 GARLAND, JORDAN, VAN DREW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ATTORNEY GENERAL GRILLED ON CAPITOL HILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GARLAND DEFENDS JUSTICE DEPARTMENT AGAINST GOP ATTACKS\par \par \uc2 SHUTDOWN, MCCARTHY, WOMACK, GAETZ, MEUSER, PELOSI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHUTDOWN SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPEAKER MCCARTHY CLAIMS PROGRESS AS DEADLINE NEARS\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, WGA, NEGOTIATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TALKS RESUME IN WRITERS' STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNION & STUDIOS TO MEET AGAIN AFTER DAY OF NEGOTIATING\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn now to the Hollywood writer strike. Negotiations are resuming between the union and the studios with hope for many workers that there is an end in sight. Zohreen Shah has more from Los Angeles. Good morning, Zohreen.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Robin. There could be an end in sight to part of the historic Hollywood strike that has up-ended the entertainment industry and halted nearly all movie and TV productions.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Hollywood writers and studios are reportedly close to an agreement to end the strike that started back in May. The WGA, an alliance of motion picture and television producers, releasing a joint statement overnight, that the two groups have met yesterday and would meet again today. The talks yesterday were described as encouraging. Still, the writers' union sent a letter to members saying they wanted writers to continue showing up to the picket lines. Writers and actors are looking for better residual pay and higher wages for streaming shows and protection of their likeness from AI. There is still no word on the negotiations regarding the actors' strike. It is the first time since the 1960s that both the actors and writers' unions had been on strike at the very same time.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Just a massive ripple effect on many industries here. Guys?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It truly is, Zohreen. But as you said, it is encouraging. At least it's encouraging.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yep, without a doubt.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALEX MURDAUGH DUE IN COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CONVICTED KILLER EXPECTED TO PLEAD GUILTY TO 22 FEDERAL CRIMES\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up, Alex Murdaugh due in court on federal fraud crimes, plus the new allegations about the murder of his wife and son in a new documentary.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ELIJAH MCCLAIN TRIAL BEGINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TWO COLORADO POLICE OFFICERS CHARGED IN YOUNG BLACK MAN'S DEATH\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And a trial getting underway for two Colorado police officers charged in the death of Elijah McClain four years ago.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHATGPT LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROMINENT AUTHORS ACCUSE CHATBOT CREATOR OF COPY RIGHT INFRINGEMENT\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Plus, why Jodi Picoult, George R. R. Martin, John Grisham, and other bestselling authors are suing the company behind ChatGPT. What it could mean for the future of AI.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231006ej9l00008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AUTOWORKERS THREATEN TO EXPAND STRIKE \uc2 UAW\uc2  CHIEF: UNION WILL ANNOUNCE NEW WALKOUTS IF NO "SERIOUS PROGRESS" BY FRIDAY\b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 IRAN, BLINKEN, PRISONER SWAP, MCCONNELL\par \par \uc2 IRAN DEAL, PRISONER SWAP, KIRBY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOP U.S. OFFICIAL ON $6 BILLION DEAL WITH IRAN TO FREE THEM\par \par \uc2 SEARCH, F-35, CRASH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MISSING F-35 FIGHTER JET FOUND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEARCH & RECOVERY TEAM FINDS DEBRIS FIELD IN SOUTH CAROLINA\par \par \uc2 SALAZAR, LUNA, CLINKUNBROOMER, ARREST\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AUTOWORKERS THREATEN TO EXPAND STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 UAW\uc2  CHIEF: UNION WILL ANNOUNCE NEW WALKOUTS IF NO "SERIOUS PROGRESS" BY FRIDAY\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn to the auto workers strike. The \uc2 UAW\uc2  has set a new deadline to expand the strike to more than just three plants if there isn't progress in negotiations. Senior national correspondent Terry Moran is at a Ford plant in Michigan. Good morning, Terry.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Michael. That's right. By the end of this week, high noon on Friday, is the deadline set by \uc2 UAW\uc2  president Shawn Fain, we could see more plants shut down or substantially disrupted by workers walking off the job like this one. Those workers over there, they usually make Ford Broncos, but not now.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Fain saying, quote, "We're not going to keep waiting around forever while the companies drag this thing out." Fain says, if there's not, quote, "substantial progress" made by the end of this week, then more plants will be hit. Economists, well, they are already forecasting and taking a look at the impact on consumers. Forecasting that if this strike goes on for more than a couple weeks, those price declines on new cars that we've seen in recent months, they would end. And if it goes down for more than three or four weeks, prices on new cars will rise.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Republican front-runner \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , well, he now plans to come here to Detroit and make a speech to about 500 autoworkers and other supporters trying to make his case to striking workers. George?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Terry, thanks so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231005ej9j00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SUING YE THE RAPPER FORMERLY KNOWN AS KANYE WEST IS BEING SUED BY CONTRACTOR\b0\par\par\uc2 1,768 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 , WGA, AMPTP, AICHS, DAVIS, HOLMES, BARRYMORE, SAMPSON, DRIVER\par \par \uc2 SAXON, YE, LAWSUIT, CONSTRUCTION, BUCKMIRE, KARDASHIAN\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back. It was a high-profile home remodeling job for an even more high-profile client. But Tony Saxon claims the rapper formerly known as Kanye West treated him wrong. He's suing the controversial superstar for what he says is rightfully his. Here's "Nightline's" Ashan Singh.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 Variety is the spice of life.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tony Saxon creates things for a living, like melodies as a musician, and million-dollar mansions as a construction consultant for some of the most demanding and particular jobs on the market, like this so-called Barbie palace in Northridge, California.\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 And when I find myself in many different fields, that's when you find yourself meeting a lot of people, that's when you find yourself getting crazy referrals.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 And the next thing you know, you end up in that house.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) That house, a Malibu beachfront home purchased by Ye, formerly known as Kanye West.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What did you know about Ye before?\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 Nothing. I just knew who he was 'cause you see him everywhere. Never voluntarily listened to any of his stuff.\par \par \uc2 MUSIC VIDEO CLIP BY YE\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Saxon says it was a referral turned walk-through turned job offer...\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 Day three of this.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...from the artist behind "Stronger," one of the highest-profile celebrities in Hollywood.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What was your understanding of what you were going to Malibu for?\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 Nothing. I just went. That walk-through turned into me walking in and seeing there's all these people scrambling around. I see all of them scrambling around, trying to be like, okay, now he wants this, now he wants that, now he wants this.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Saxon, who's not a licensed contractor or electrician, says he was tasked for a model the property Ye reportedly purchased in 2021 for more than $57 million.\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 I was the project manager. That's an umbrella term. Caretaker, security guard. I was the coordinator. I was the cleaner. I was the direct line between him and most, a lot of the different facets of his, his organization.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But he says it also came with another cost.\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 I can't do any kind of physical labor again. I feel like a 75-year-old man now.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Saxon is now suing Ye, claiming he is owed yearly $1 million in unpaid wages and was forced to work in dangerous conditions.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you're saying you were eating, sleeping, living here the whole time?\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What did that look like?\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 A little POW cot in the corner. You know, whatever. It's not like I, I need to stay at the \uc2 Ritz-Carlton\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 BRIAN BUCKMIRE (DEFENSE ATTORNEY)\par \par \uc2 It's just so bizarre. It's something that an employee would be on notice of and that no reasonable person would say that's okay. You just can't have employees do that. It's not safe.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, Ye never explicitly asked him to sleep there. But while he was there, he says he does recall seeing some familiar faces.\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 I mean, get this...\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 Kim Kardashian walks in with three kids. And then one of my guys walks in and he sees Kim from far away. And he did the worst thing in the world he could ever do, "Hi, Bianca." Now, I didn't even realize it. (Inaudible). You know, look, we're all old. We all don't know what the heck is going on.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) According to sources that ABC News has spoken to, Kim, having been mistaken for her ex-husband's new wife, laughed the interaction off.\par \par \uc2 FAN (MALE)\par \par \uc2 What's up, Ye?\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Ye is one of the most prolific and dominating personalities in music history. And the man behind the explosive brand "Yeesy." But last year, the 46-year-old mogul making headlines for his repeated offensive and anti-Semitic remarks. Balenciaga cut ties with the rapper. And Adidas, Ye's collaborator on a hugely popular Yeesy brand, ended its partnership since his comments last October. He married designer Bianca Censori in a private ceremony at the beginning of the year.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Ye now thrust back in the spotlight and not for good reasons. According to the lawsuit, Saxon made constant complaints to Ye of various safety hazards, including workers unsafely demolishing various parts of the house with no safety equipment. No action was taken by Ye to address complaints. Saxon claims that the working conditions worsened to the point that he told Ye that he had injured his back severely and needs time off to rest. The star allegedly disregarded Saxon's concerns and instead responded by asking to discuss the next phase of the project.\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 Told him I got hurt. I said, "My back and neck are destroyed, I can't be up there, and I can't be sleeping there." Now, admittedly, I always had a, you know...\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right.\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 ...back, but like, my neck, that was the nail in the coffin. So, you can only pay people so much to do crazy work.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Then Saxon says things came to a head one day when Ye allegedly demanded Saxon to remove all of the electricity and windows from the house, which led to Saxon expressing concerns about the extreme danger of such actions. Despite his explanations, Ye allegedly persisted, raising his voice and insisted on moving large generators inside the house.\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 He goes, "Well, you've got generators, just do the generators." And I'm like, "We can't have them outside. It's gonna blow our spot." And he goes, "Well, put them inside." I said, "You cannot have carbon monoxide running into a building, the exhaust from generators, you're gonna suffocate everyone." So, that's when he looks at me and he goes, he was just furious. He's like, "If you don't do what I ask you to do, you're a Clinton, you're a Kardashian."\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 "You're an enemy and I'm not gonna be your friend anymore. And you're only gonna see me on TV." You know, I just looked at him and the first thing I said, "I don't watch TV." And I walked out. And he said, "Get the hell out."\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, before things got sour, was there any part of you that like...\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 I liked him.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Any part of him, that - you liked that, that kind of kept you around?\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 I liked him, I liked him.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But some of Saxon's claims could be difficult to prove in court. Saxon didn't sign a contract before he started working, and says he voluntarily put in extra hours.\par \par \uc2 BRIAN BUCKMIRE (DEFENSE ATTORNEY)\par \par \uc2 Well, the devil's in the details. And the details are usually in a contract. If it's all verbal and no witnesses, the details get really difficult here.\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 I'm an old-school dirty rock 'n' roller. You got to stay late, you got to sweat, you got to work.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And while he's suing for unpaid wages and money of his own he says he spent, exactly how much that is in total isn't in the lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How much of your own money are you saying that you put into this project?\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 Everything that, that I felt responsible for as my own on that, every single thing. Because it was, because it was coming to me. It got to the point where I told him, like, "We're out of money. You need to send more money. We're completely out of money."\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Can I hear a number of your own money, how much you used?\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 A lot.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But Tony, how much of your own money are you saying went down the drain?\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 I, put this way, every ounce of my body, soul, and pocket invested in that job. Are you gonna turn down an opportunity to work with a multibillionaire?\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) After Saxon's firing, which he says violated disability and labor laws, the construction consultant says he's come to a sobering reality.\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 My mental state is just crazy and my neck is broken. I can't do anything. I'm was just so happy to be out of there that even going inside a \uc2 Burger King\uc2  felt like I was in the Taj Mahal.\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ABC News reached out to Ye for comment but did not receive one at a time of this broadcast. But Saxon says he's not backing down.\par \par \uc2 TONY SAXON (FORMER EMPLOYEE OF YE)\par \par \uc2 I've been through hell in my life. You cannot scare me, and you cannot embarrass me.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our thanks to Ashan.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAUI STRONG\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Up next, a story of survival and the symbol of hope growing tonight on Maui.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020230921ej9j00003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 STRIKING AUTOWORKERS BACK IN THE PICKET LINES STILL NO DEAL AFTER WEEKEND OF NEGOTIATIONS WITH BIG THREE AUTOMAKERS\b0\par\par\uc2 650 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IRAN-US PRISONER DEAL\par \par \uc2 PRISONERS, RELEASED, IRAN, ASSETS\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, DEPUTY, AMBUSH, CLINKUNBROOMER, LUNA, LACKEY\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE, AUTOMAKERS, WORKERS, NEGOTIATIONS, LAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, police hoping that the public may have some answers there. Matt, thank you. Now to the historic autoworkers walkout. The targeted strike taking aim at all three of the big there automakers. Negotiations are ongoing, but the opposing sides remain far apart. Our senior national correspondent Terry Moran is outside of a Ford plant in Michigan with the latest. Good morning, Terry.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STRIKING AUTOWORKERS BACK ON THE PICKET LINES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STILL NO DEAL AFTER WEEKEND OF NEGOTIATIONS WITH BIG THREE AUTOMAKER\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Linsey. Yeah, day 4 and you can see they're still on strike. That's a manager's car going, they're kind of slow walking that. Spirits are high here. They make Ford Broncos here. A lot of workers tell us they don't make enough money to buy the car that they build, and that's one of the reasons they're on the line. Still, we heard from a couple of workers, they hope this strike doesn't go on for a long time, but there is no deal in sight.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning nearly 13,000 autoworkers are back on the picket lines as the United Autoworkers Union battles America's big three car companies over wages and benefits. It's an unprecedented strike, using new tactics targeting only three facilities so far. A GM plant in Missouri, a Ford plant in Michigan, and a Chrysler Stellantis plant in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Over the weekend, negotiations puttered along. The \uc2 UAW\uc2  saying it had, quote, "Reasonably productive conversations with Ford," and meeting Sunday with \uc2 GM\uc2 . And \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  says, it's now increased its offer to workers matching Ford and \uc2 GM\uc2 , a roughly 20% increase for hourly wages.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But that's just half of the increase the \uc2 UAW\uc2  has demanded, along with better retiree benefits and a four day workweek, after years of concessions to automakers when the companies were struggling.\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I know we're asking for a lot, but over the years we gave up a lot.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And the \uc2 UAW\uc2 's targeted tactics are already having ripple effects on non-striking worker. \uc2 GM\uc2  announced temporary layoffs for 2,000 non-striking employees at a plant in Kansas. Ford did the same to 600 in Michigan. Both companies blaming the strike for disrupting operations. But the \uc2 UAW\uc2  accused the companies of, quote, "Trying to put the squeeze on our members to settle for less."\par \par \uc2 CHUCK TAYLOR (\uc2 UAW\uc2  WORKER)\par \par \uc2 Because we're out here on strike and we're picketing to stand up for ourselves.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HISTORIC AUTOWORKER WALKOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORD & GM ANNOUNCE TEMPORARY LAYOFFS AS STRIKE ENTERS NEW WEEK\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Farther down the supply chain, the strike is now starting to impact some car dealerships bracing themselves for possible shortages.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT KUNES (CEO KUNES AUTO & RV GROUP)\par \par \uc2 We can survive for a while, but if this thing prolongs out anywhere past that 30 day deadline, we're gonna really start to see some pricing influences.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Talking to workers here, we keep hearing two things. One, they say people, they aren't doing it just for themselves and their families, but for workers coming up. They want to make sure that younger workers coming into the industry, especially the electric vehicles industry, do well. And the other thing they say, they feel it is time, after workers taking hit after hit over the years and executives getting more and more pay. George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231004ej9i00004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 UAW\uc2 : STRIKE COULD EXPAND AUTO WORKERS TAKE TO PICKET LINES IN 4TH DAY OF STRIKE\b0\par\par\uc2 477 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BLINKEN, NAMAZI, IRAN, MCCONNELL, BIDEN, PRISONER SWAP\par \par \uc2 SALAZAR, LUNA, CLINKUNBROOMER, AMBUSH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE: ARREST IN DEPUTY'S MURDER\par \par \uc2 F-35, CRASH, DEBRIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEBRIS FROM MISSING FIGHTER JET FOUND\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, MICHAEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABC NEWS EXCLUSIVE\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , PROTESTS, FAIN, FARLEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 UAW\uc2 : STRIKE COULD EXPAND\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This evening, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  is now threatening to expand its walkout, day four of its strike against all three top American automakers, what they're demanding. And Terry Moran again tonight in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AUTO WORKERS TAKE TO PICKET LINES IN 4TH DAY OF STRIKE\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) With the negotiations over the auto workers strike progressing slowly, the president of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  issuing a warning. They're ready to expand their strike if they don't get better offers from the big three car makers.\par \par \uc2 SHAWN FAIN (PRESIDENT \uc2 UAW\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 They could double our wages, not raise the prices of vehicles, and they would still make billions in profits. This is a choice by the companies. It's nothing short of just two words, corporate greed.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The strike is already disrupting operations. \uc2 GM\uc2  says it will idle 2,000 workers this week at a Kansas plant after Ford laid off 600 workers here in Michigan, where today some strikers expressed their frustration with independent truck drivers who crossed the picket lines.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Come on, scab.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The \uc2 UAW\uc2  wants a 40% pay increase over four years, pensions for younger workers, and an end to lower wages for new hires. But the CEO of Ford told us they can't afford all that and make the critical transition to electric vehicles.\par \par \uc2 JIM FARLEY\uc2  (CEO \uc2 FORD MOTOR COMPANY\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 But a line in the sand is, if we can't invest in electric vehicles or future, what is the, what is the win here if we can't invest for the future?\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The workers we talked to say they want to be part of the EV revolution.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, you think you and these people can build electric vehicles for Ford?\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, we can do it. We can do anything. We can adapt to anything. You throw it at us, we'll do it.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Economists are already looking for potential impacts on consumers. Forecasting that if this strike lasts for more than a couple of weeks, the declines on new car we've seen in the past couple of months, they would end. And if it last for more than three or four weeks, new car prices will rise. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Terry Moran live in Wayne, Michigan, again for us tonight. Thanks, Terry.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230920ej9i00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HISTORIC UAW STRIKE ENTERS THIRD DAY FORD & GM ANNOUNCE TEMPORARY LAYOFFS, PRODUCTION HALTED IN 3 STATES\b0\par\par\uc2 625 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE LEE, WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECOVERY UNDERWAY AS LEE WINDS DOWNS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENS OF THOUSANDS WITHOUT POWER IN MAINE AFTER STORM CAUSES MASS WIND DAMAGE\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , PROTESTS, MARCINIAK, FAIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HISTORIC UAW STRIKE ENTERS THIRD DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORD & GM ANNOUNCE TEMPORARY LAYOFFS, PRODUCTION HALTED AT FACILITIES IN 3 STATES\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn now to the historic \uc2 UAW\uc2  strike against the big three automakers.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For a third day now, nearly 13,000 union members shutting down production at plants in three different states. And we could see much more of this in the coming days. ABC's Alex Presha is on the ground in Toledo, Ohio. Good morning, Alex.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Gio. Yeah, you see this group of workers behind me. They've been out here since 6:00 AM local time. They'll be here until about noon today. That is the new shift for these \uc2 UAW\uc2  workers as they fight for a new contract.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  are back at the negotiating table on day three of this historic strike with the big three automakers. The \uc2 UAW\uc2  with a counteroffer to Ford, \uc2 General Motors\uc2 , and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , Chrysler's parent company, as nearly 13,000 workers in three states walked off the job in a targeted strike.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEGOTIATION UPDATES\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The \uc2 UAW\uc2  reports there were reasonably productive conversations with Ford Saturday. And \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  says it's upped its offer to a new 21% increase for hourly wages. Still, no deal yet.\par \par \uc2 JOHN MARCINIAK (STRIKING WORKER)\par \par \uc2 Well, my money wasn't saving the company. It was lining their pockets.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) John Marciniak, who has been with \uc2 Jeep\uc2  for 40 years, now on strike for the first time in his career at \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 ' plant here in Toledo. Marciniak is preparing to dip into his 401 (k) to stay afloat if this continues. He says, whatever it takes.\par \par \uc2 JOHN MARCINIAK (STRIKING WORKER)\par \par \uc2 I'm here for the fight. I'm here for the duration because I believe in this fight.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Some workers already impacted by the picketing. \uc2 GM\uc2  announcing temporary layoffs for 2,000 employees, Ford doing the same to 600.\par \par \uc2 SHAWN FAIN (PRESIDENT UNITED AUTO WORKERS)\par \par \uc2 Our members will be taken care of no matter what happens. We'll take care of them. We have their back. They have our back.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 UAW\uc2  STATEMENT ON REPORTS OF LAYOFFS OF NON-STRIKING WORKERS\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 UAW\uc2  president Shawn Fain outraged by the cuts, saying in a statement, "They don't have to lay off a single employee. In fact, they could double every autoworker's pay, not raise car prices, and still rake in billions of dollars." The big three automakers have seen a decade of record profits, but say their offers have been generous and that the union should be reasonable.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 We are ready for a strike.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Among the \uc2 UAW\uc2 's demands, a return to pensions, better benefits for retirees, cost of living adjustments, and a 40% pay increase.\par \par \uc2 ROBERT MARCHESE (STRIKING WORKER)\par \par \uc2 I know we're asking for a lot but, over the years that I've worked for them, we gave up a lot.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Gio, so obviously no breakthrough yesterday, but a lot of people here hopeful that that changes soon. Gio?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This will not be an easy fight. All right, Alex, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230929ej9h0005n\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW CONCERNS ABOUT ECONOMIC IMPACT OF THE \uc2 UAW\uc2  STRIKE THE POTENTIAL DAMAGE TO AUTO INDUSTRY, ECONOMY, CONSUMERS\b0\par\par\uc2 370 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE LEE, WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECOVERY UNDERWAY AS LEE WINDS DOWNS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENS OF THOUSANDS WITHOUT POWER IN MAINE AFTER STORM CAUSES MASS WIND DAMAGE\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , PROTESTS, MARCINIAK, FAIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HISTORIC UAW STRIKE ENTERS THIRD DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORD & GM ANNOUNCE TEMPORARY LAYOFFS, PRODUCTION HALTED AT FACILITIES IN 3 STATES\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , ECONOMY, PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW CONCERNS ABOUT ECONOMIC IMPACT OF THE UAW STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE POTENTIAL DAMAGE TO AUTO INDUSTRY, ECONOMY, CONSUMERS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the potential economic impact of a prolonged strike, what it could mean for the industry, workers, their communities, and car buyers. ABC's Alexis Christoforous is here to help us break it all down. Good morning, Alexis.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Gio. Depending on how big the strike gets and how long it goes, finding the car you want at a price you can afford could get a lot harder. Heading into these strikes, the automakers said they had a combined 70 days worth of inventory. If the strike drags on, you could see fewer cars and trucks on dealer lots. And less inventory can put pressure on car prices, which had been trending lower after recording record highs last year. Now, the big three automakers aren't as dominant as they once were, accounting for 3% of overall economic growth. So, the strike's impact on the broader economy is expected to be limited. \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Analytics estimates a three to four-week strike will shave just 0.2% off gross domestic product this quarter.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Small but impactful when you consider Americans are still dealing with higher oil prices, rising mortgage rates, and the resumption of student loan payments next month. And communities where the affected plants are located could be hit the hardest. Three targeted assembly plants in Michigan, Ohio, and Missouri employ nearly 13,000 people, who will now have less money to spend and pump back into the economy. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You really get a sense of that ripple effect there. Alexis Christoforous, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230929ej9h0005o\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 UAW TALKS RESUME AMID LAYOFFS MEETS WITH \uc2 GM\uc2 , FORD; \uc2 STELLANTIS\uc2  INCREASES OFFER\b0\par\par\uc2 612 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Sunday\par \uc2 WNSU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, DEPUTY, KILLED, CLINKUNBROOMER, TARGETED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE, AUTOMAKERS, LAYOFFS, WORKERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UAW TALKS RESUME AMID LAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Detectives desperately asking the public for help. Jaclyn, thank you. Talks resumed today in the \uc2 UAW\uc2  strike against the big three automakers amid more layoffs. Nearly 13,000 union members are striking at three plants in Ohio, Michigan, and Missouri. The union wants a 40% raise over four years, pensions and health care and retirement. The automakers counter that they have made generous offers and simply cannot afford the union's demands. ABC's Alex Presha reports now from outside the Jeep plant in Toledo.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UAW TALKS RESUME AMID LAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MEET WITH \uc2 GM\uc2 , FORD; \uc2 STELLANTIS\uc2  INCREASE OFFER\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, striking autoworkers capping off a weekend of solidarity, with nearly 13,000 picketing across three states, now preparing to enter a fourth day. The \uc2 UAW\uc2  says it met with \uc2 General Motors\uc2  today and had reasonably productive conversations with Ford this weekend. \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , Chrysler's parent company, says it's upped its offer to a nearly 21% increase for hourly wages. But still, no deal yet.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Ripples of the targeted strike already felt, \uc2 GM\uc2  announcing temporary layoffs for 2,000 non-striking employees, Ford doing the same to 600. The \uc2 UAW\uc2  with a counteroffer to the big three automakers, demanding a return to pensions, better benefits for retirees, cost of living adjustments, and a 40% pay increase. \uc2 UAW\uc2 's President saying they're preparing to increase the strike if need be.\par \par \uc2 UAW PRESIDENT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 We'll amp up the pressure, we'll take more plants out.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The big three automakers say their offers have been generous, and that the union should be reasonable. From the \uc2 GM\uc2  plant in Wentzville, Missouri to this Ford assembly plant in Wayne, Michigan, workers with the same plea.\par \par \uc2 AUTO WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 The workload, it's a lot, so you pay me, I deserve what I'm working for.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Here in Toledo, striking workers make camp at stations surrounding the \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  plant. Brandi Kelly works at the Chrysler plant in Detroit. It's not part of this targeted strike, but she drove to Toledo to deliver a car full of pizzas in solidarity.\par \par \uc2 AUTO WORKER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 We're trying to fight for all the same things.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Workers now receiving just $500 a week in strike pay, a fraction of their normal paycheck.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So what's changed?\par \par \uc2 JASMIN WILLIAMS (AUTO WORKER)\par \par \uc2 I've had to cut back on spending, I can't really do much seeing that I just bought a house. No one knows how long we're going to be out here, nobody knows what we're going to get. It's just, it's the waiting game right now.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Waiting game with far reaching impacts. Alex Presha joins us now. And, Alex, we hear that honking there. So far, the strike has been limited to three plants with no deal in sight. What else could we ultimately see here?\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Linsey, the roughly 13,000 striking workers is a small fraction of the 150,000 \uc2 UAW\uc2  workers at the big three. Now, the union president believes his targeted strike is an effective strategy without putting undue pressure on the entirety of the union, but says if progress is not made, they can increase pressure by taking more plants off line. Linsey.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSU000020230919ej9h00003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PRESIDENT SENDS TOP ADVISERS TO DETROIT BIDEN: RECORD PROFITS SHOULD MEAN RECORD CONTRACTS FOR \uc2 UAW\b0\par\par\uc2 432 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WEATHER ALERT: STATES OF EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 LEE, TROPICAL, CYCLONE, NOVA SCOTIA, NEW ENGLAND, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POST-TROPICAL CYCLONE LEE: LATEST ALERTS\par \par \uc2 LEE, HURRICANE, MASSACHUSETTS, MAINE, EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE, AUTOMAKERS, LAYOFFS, CORNETT, FAIN, BIDEN, FARLEY\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, DETROIT, PROFITS, CONTRACTS, STRIKE, \uc2 UAW\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's go ahead and bring in White House Correspondent, Maryalice Parks to talk about the White House response to this historic strike. And Maryalice, we just saw there that the President is saying no one wants a strike, but that record profits should also bring record contracts for these workers. So, how involved is the White House right now?\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, Gio, good morning. That line from the President getting a lot of attention. The President said plainly that he thinks these companies need to go further in their offers to see that those record profits are shared. Now, I asked the White House Press Secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , whether that meant that the President supported all of the union's demand, including that 40 percent raise across four years. She wouldn't go there, but she again said the President thought that the companies should, quote, go further. Now, the President sent two members of his team to Detroit, but they are trying to walk a fine line here. They want to show that their engaged and involved, but they don't want to be seen as butting in. So, Gio, they said that if it is helpful, the President's team stands ready to assist.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Maryalice, we're already seeing those temporary layoffs, so what is the administration telling you about the economic impacts here?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IMPACT OF THE UAW STRIKE. WHAT MAJOR WALKOUT COULD MEAN FOR THE ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, they're trying to be really careful on this one, too. They say that they're optimistic that a deal can be reached. They hope it can be reached quickly. They are pointing to the fact that this is still a limited and targeted strike, that that changes things. But we have seen those predictions from some economists that say that even a ten-day strike could cost billions. Now, it is important to remember that any final deal could also have an impact on other unions, other groups of workers that are negotiating their own contracts and wages across the country. Whit.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Maryalice, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231003ej9g00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HISTORIC UAW STRIKE AGAINST BIG THREE AUTOMAKERS WORKERS HOLD MAJOR RALLY IN DETROIT AFTER MAKING COUNTEROFFER\b0\par\par\uc2 735 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WEATHER ALERT: STATES OF EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 LEE, TROPICAL, CYCLONE, NOVA SCOTIA, NEW ENGLAND, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POST-TROPICAL CYCLONE LEE: LATEST ALERTS\par \par \uc2 LEE, HURRICANE, MASSACHUSETTS, MAINE, EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE, AUTOMAKERS, LAYOFFS, CORNETT, FAIN, BIDEN, FARLEY\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Turning now to the thousands of United Autoworkers on the picket line for a second day this morning with the first of the big three automakers announcing temporary layoffs it says are a result of the strike. ABC's Morgan Norwood joins us now from Wayne, Michigan with the latest. Good morning, Morgan.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning to you Janai. Workers returning to the picket lines. You can see them starting to gather just right behind me, starting to rally this morning. All of this as both sides return to the negotiation table, hoping to hammer out this deal. Experts say if this continues to drag on, it could have a seismic impact on our economy.\par \par \uc2 PROTEST LEADER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 When I say union, you say strong. Union.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTORS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Strong.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, the sun rising as autoworkers take to the picket lines for day two of a historic strike against the big three automakers.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 No deal, no wheels. Union strong.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTORS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 People ought to know who we are.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Nearly 13,000 workers at Ford, \uc2 General Motors\uc2 , and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  walking off the job, bringing production lines to a grinding halt, hoping to strongarm the companies into handing over pensions, better benefits for retirees, cost-of-ling adjustments, and a 40 percent pay increase.\par \par \uc2 RODNEY CORNETT (STRIKING WORKER)\par \par \uc2 I mean, the companies are making record profits and it is not like we want all of it, we just would like to be able to support our families.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Ford and \uc2 GM\uc2  offering an 11th hour 20 percent wage increase, but uaw won't budge.\par \par \uc2 SHAWN FAIN (PRESIDENT UNITED AUTO WORKERS)\par \par \uc2 You guys are ready to rumble now, aren't you?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORD SAYS LAYOFFS ARE DUE TO STRIKE. WHERE NEGOTIATIONS STAND BETWEEN \uc2 UAW\uc2  AND AUTOMAKERS\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Union President Shawn Fain holding a rally overnight, urging CEOs to make a deal.\par \par \uc2 SHAWN FAIN (PRESIDENT UNITED AUTO WORKERS)\par \par \uc2 It boils down to one thing, it's corporate greed and it's got to stop.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) President Biden hoping to hustle the talks along, sending his acting Labor Secretary and a senior aide to Detroit.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Let's be clear, no one wants a strike, but I believe it should go further to ensure record corporate profits meaning record contracts.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) By one estimate, this strike could cost the economy more than $5 billion with tens of thousands of jobs lost. And this morning, it's already triggered a wave of some 600 temporary layoffs at Ford. Its CEO, \uc2 Jim Farley\uc2  telling ABC's Terry Moran the union needs to be reasonable.\par \par \uc2 JIM FARLEY\uc2  (CEO FORD)\par \par \uc2 And this offer is a great offer and we want to get feedback on it to make it even better for them.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we could see more local strikes as soon as Monday if both sides don't reach an agreement this weekend. Janai.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Incredible how many strikes we are seeing across the country. But, Morgan, big picture, what does this mean for Americans and the economy?\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So great question, Janai. If this continues and more plants start to strike, if this deal isn't reached, I want you to think dealerships. Of course, if they run out of cars, that's going to jack up the price. Think supply and demand. But, say you're not even in the market for a new car, say you are waiting around for a part, you are looking for a repair. That could take some time, could impact availability. But, bottom line, big picture, we are talking an impact to the economy, which, by the way, Janai and Gio, we are just starting to bounce back from inflation.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, quite an impact, indeed. All right, Morgan, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231003ej9g00004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 A CELEBRA-TORY AFFAIR! BIG BARGAINS FOR TORY'S BIRTHDAY\b0\par\par\uc2 1,199 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NO DEAL\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, AUTOWORKERS, CAR MAKERS, FAIN, FARLEY\par \par \uc2 LEE, EAST COAST, WIND, RIP CURRENTS, WAVES\par \par \uc2 LEE, ATLANTIC, WINDS, BEACHES\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, INDICTED, DOJ, GUN CHARGES, GARLAND, GOP, DEMS\par \par \uc2 LOWELL, BIDEN, INDICTMENT, ADDICTION, PLEA, POLITICS\par \par \uc2 LIBYA, FLOOD, DAMS, DEATHS, MISSING\par \par \uc2 CAVALCANTE, CAPTURED, PRISON, SECURITY, YODA\par \par \uc2 SANDERS, COLORADO, FOOTBALL, RIVAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WIND FORECAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 MURDAUGH, PROSECUTORS, TRAIL, HILL, JURORS, GRIFFIN, BLAND\par \par \uc2 CYBERATTACK, MGM, CAESARS, SHUTDOWN, CASINOS, STAMOS\par \par \uc2 TUOHY, OHER, CONSERVATORSHIP, "BLIND SIDE", LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 MORTGAGE, RATES, ASSUMABLE, TIKTOK, TRAPASSO, SINGH\par \par \uc2 FOOTBALL, EAGLES, HURTS, VIKINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TIMING THE RAIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING OVERNIGHT: ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GENERAL MOTORS\uc2 , BARRA, \uc2 UAW\uc2 , WALKOUT, STRIKE, NEGOTIATIONS\par \par \uc2 MOTHERS, JOBS, SHAIKH, BERINGER, HICKOK, MASON, CORBIN, HEGGENESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 OZEMPIC, WEIGHT LOSS, TREND, TIKTOK, WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA HEALTH ALERT\par \par \uc2 PREMATURE, TWINS, THOMAS, SAKER, JACKSON, DICKSON\par \par \uc2 TURNEY, MISSING, ARIZONA\par \par \uc2 ELEMIS LONDON, NIGHT, LIVELY, STERLING FOREVER, PUFFIN, SWIG\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now it's time for day two of Tory's birthday celebration, a special "Deals and Steals" tha